window.QB_LIM = [{"sys":"AG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0001","es":{"q":"En el capítulo LIMITATIONS del FCOM, y salvo que se indique otra cosa, ¿a qué se refieren todas las referencias a velocidad, Mach y altitud?","keys":["velocidad","indicada","mach"],"answer":"El capítulo contiene limitaciones operacionales del avión y de sus sistemas asociados, y establece que todas las referencias a airspeed, Mach y altitud se refieren a velocidad indicada, Mach indicado y altitud de presión, salvo que se indique lo contrario. (FCOM LIM-INT · p. 11 · rev 04 SEP 17)","opts":["A velocidad indicada, Mach indicado y altitud de presión","A velocidad verdadera (TAS), Mach verdadero y altitud geométrica","A velocidad calibrada (CAS), Mach indicado y altura radioaltimétrica","A velocidad indicada, Mach verdadero y altitud de densidad"]},"en":{"q":"In the FCOM LIMITATIONS chapter, and unless otherwise stated, what do all references to airspeed, Mach and altitude refer to?","keys":["indicated","mach","pressure"],"answer":"The chapter contains the operational limitations of the aircraft and its associated systems, and states that all references to airspeed, Mach and altitude refer to indicated airspeed, indicated Mach and pressure altitude, unless otherwise stated. (FCOM LIM-INT · p. 11 · rev 04 SEP 17)","opts":["Indicated airspeed, indicated Mach and pressure altitude","True airspeed (TAS), true Mach and geometric altitude","Calibrated airspeed (CAS), indicated Mach and radio altitude","Indicated airspeed, true Mach and density altitude"]}},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0002","es":{"q":"Sobre la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE del EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["2000","ft","altitud"],"answer":"Es falsa: el rótulo inferior de la envolvente es -1 000 ft, no -2 000 ft. Las otras tres afirmaciones se corresponden con los rótulos del gráfico (39 800 ft, 9 200 ft y borde inferior negativo). (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["La altitud de presión mínima rotulada es -2 000 ft","La altitud de presión máxima rotulada es 39 800 ft","La franja de despegue y aterrizaje llega hasta 9 200 ft","La envolvente admite altitudes de presión negativas"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE of the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["2000","ft","altitude"],"answer":"It is false: the lower label of the envelope is -1 000 ft, not -2 000 ft. The other three statements match the labels on the chart (39 800 ft, 9 200 ft and negative lower edge). (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["The minimum labelled pressure altitude is -2 000 ft","The maximum labelled pressure altitude is 39 800 ft","The takeoff and landing band extends up to 9 200 ft","The envelope allows negative pressure altitudes"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0003","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), todas estas altitudes de presión pueden quedar dentro de la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE con la OAT adecuada, EXCEPTO:","keys":["40500","ft","a320"],"answer":"40 500 ft supera el rótulo superior de la envolvente (39 800 ft), así que queda fuera con cualquier OAT. Las otras tres quedan entre -1 000 ft y 39 800 ft. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["40 500 ft","-500 ft","9 000 ft","39 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), all of these pressure altitudes can fall within the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE with the appropriate OAT, EXCEPT:","keys":["40500","ft","a320"],"answer":"40 500 ft exceeds the upper label of the envelope (39 800 ft), so it falls outside it with any OAT. The other three lie between -1 000 ft and 39 800 ft. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["40 500 ft","-500 ft","9 000 ft","39 000 ft"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0004","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la altitud de presión máxima que rotula la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["39800","ft","a320"],"answer":"El vértice superior de la envolvente está rotulado con 39 800 ft: es la altitud de presión máxima de la envolvente para ese avión. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["39 800 ft","37 000 ft","39 000 ft","41 100 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum pressure altitude labelled on the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["39800","ft","a320"],"answer":"The upper apex of the envelope is labelled 39 800 ft: it is the maximum pressure altitude of the envelope for that aircraft. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["39 800 ft","37 000 ft","39 000 ft","41 100 ft"]}},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0005","es":{"q":"Volando el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ATC te ofrece subir a FL410 para evitar turbulencia. Atendiendo a la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE, ¿qué haces?","keys":["39800","ft","rechazar"],"answer":"La envolvente rotula 39 800 ft como altitud de presión máxima. FL410 queda por encima de ese techo, así que no es aceptable con ninguna condición. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["Rechazar: la envolvente termina en 39 800 ft de altitud de presión","Aceptar: la envolvente admite hasta 41 100 ft","Aceptar sólo si la OAT es igual o inferior a ISA","Aceptar sólo si el peso está por debajo del máximo de aterrizaje"]},"en":{"q":"Flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), ATC offers you a climb to FL410 to avoid turbulence. Based on the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE, what do you do?","keys":["39800","ft","reject"],"answer":"The envelope labels 39 800 ft as the maximum pressure altitude. FL410 is above that ceiling, so it is not acceptable under any condition. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["Reject: the envelope ends at 39 800 ft pressure altitude","Accept: the envelope allows up to 41 100 ft","Accept only if the OAT is at or below ISA","Accept only if the weight is below the maximum landing weight"]}},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0006","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la altitud de presión mínima rotulada en la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["1000","ft","a320"],"answer":"El borde inferior de la envolvente lleva el rótulo -1 000 ft: es la altitud de presión mínima. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["-1 000 ft","0 ft","-500 ft","-2 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum pressure altitude labelled on the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["1000","ft","a320"],"answer":"The lower edge of the envelope carries the label -1 000 ft: it is the minimum pressure altitude. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["-1 000 ft","0 ft","-500 ft","-2 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0007","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿hasta qué altitud de presión se extiende la franja rotulada 'Takeoff and Landing' de la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["9200","ft","a320"],"answer":"La franja de despegue y aterrizaje está acotada por el rótulo 9 200 ft en su borde superior. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["9 200 ft","8 000 ft","9 800 ft","12 500 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), up to what pressure altitude does the band labelled 'Takeoff and Landing' of the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE extend?","keys":["9200","ft","a320"],"answer":"The takeoff and landing band is bounded by the label 9 200 ft on its upper edge. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["9 200 ft","8 000 ft","9 800 ft","12 500 ft"]}},{"sys":"ENV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0008","es":{"q":"Te planifican con el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) un destino cuya altitud de presión es de 9 500 ft. ¿Qué dice la ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["9200","ft","aterrizable"],"answer":"La franja 'Takeoff and Landing' llega hasta 9 200 ft de altitud de presión. Con 9 500 ft el aeropuerto queda fuera de la envolvente para despegue y aterrizaje. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["No es aterrizable: la franja de despegue y aterrizaje termina en 9 200 ft","Es aterrizable: el límite de la franja de despegue y aterrizaje es 12 500 ft","Es aterrizable si la OAT está por debajo de ISA","Es aterrizable, porque la envolvente sólo limita el techo en 39 800 ft"]},"en":{"q":"You are planned on the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) to a destination whose pressure altitude is 9 500 ft. What does the ENVIRONMENTAL ENVELOPE say?","keys":["9200","ft","landable"],"answer":"The 'Takeoff and Landing' band reaches up to 9 200 ft pressure altitude. At 9 500 ft the airport falls outside the envelope for takeoff and landing. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 26 · rev 19 JUL 17)","opts":["Not landable: the takeoff and landing band ends at 9 200 ft","Landable: the limit of the takeoff and landing band is 12 500 ft","Landable if the OAT is below ISA","Landable, because the envelope only limits the ceiling at 39 800 ft"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0009","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la anchura mínima de pista (minimal runway width)?","keys":["30","a320","motores"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para este avión una anchura mínima de pista de 30 m, además de la nominal de 45 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["30 m","23 m","45 m","No hay anchura mínima publicada"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimal runway width?","keys":["30","m","runway"],"answer":"For this aircraft the FCOM publishes a minimal runway width of 30 m, in addition to the nominal 45 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["30 m","23 m","45 m","No minimum width is published"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0010","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la anchura nominal de pista (nominal runway width)?","keys":["45","a320","motores"],"answer":"El FCOM publica una anchura nominal de pista de 45 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["45 m","30 m","40 m","60 m"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the nominal runway width?","keys":["45","m","runway"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes a nominal runway width of 45 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["45 m","30 m","40 m","60 m"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0011","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la pendiente media de pista (runway slope, mean) máxima admisible?","keys":["2","a320","motores"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para este avión una pendiente media de pista de ±2 %. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["±2 %","±1 %","±2,5 %","±3 %"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum allowable mean runway slope?","keys":["2","%","slope"],"answer":"For this aircraft the FCOM publishes a mean runway slope of ±2 %. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["±2 %","±1 %","±2.5 %","±3 %"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0012","es":{"q":"Con el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) te ofrecen un aeródromo cuya pista tiene una pendiente media del 2,5 %. ¿Es admisible?","keys":["2","limite","pendiente"],"answer":"La pendiente media de pista publicada para este avión es ±2 %. Un 2,5 % la excede, con independencia del sentido de la operación. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: el límite de pendiente media es ±2 %","Sí: el límite de pendiente media es ±3 %","Sí, si se despega cuesta abajo","Sí, si la pista es de más de 45 m de ancho"]},"en":{"q":"With the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you are offered an aerodrome whose runway has a mean slope of 2.5 %. Is it acceptable?","keys":["2","limit","slope"],"answer":"The mean runway slope published for this aircraft is ±2 %. A 2.5 % slope exceeds it, regardless of the direction of operation. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 29 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: the mean slope limit is ±2 %","Yes: the mean slope limit is ±3 %","Yes, if taking off downhill","Yes, if the runway is more than 45 m wide"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0013","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es el viento cruzado máximo demostrado (despegue y aterrizaje) publicado en LIM-AG-OPS?","keys":["38","kt","rafaga"],"answer":"El FCOM publica 38 kt (gust included) como máximo viento cruzado demostrado para despegue y aterrizaje, aplicable a toda la flota. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["38 kt (ráfaga incluida)","29 kt (ráfaga incluida)","33 kt (ráfaga excluida)","40 kt (ráfaga incluida)"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum demonstrated crosswind (takeoff and landing) published in LIM-AG-OPS?","keys":["38","kt","gust"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes 38 kt (gust included) as the maximum demonstrated crosswind for takeoff and landing, applicable to the whole fleet. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["38 kt (gust included)","29 kt (gust included)","33 kt (gust excluded)","40 kt (gust included)"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0014","es":{"q":"Sobre el viento cruzado máximo demostrado de 38 kt, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["afm","limitacion","airplane"],"answer":"Es falsa: el FCOM dice expresamente que el valor máximo demostrado NO es una limitación del AFM, sino la condición máxima experimentada en la campaña de certificación. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Es una limitación del Airplane Flight Manual (AFM)","Incluye la ráfaga","Es la condición máxima de viento cruzado experimentada durante la campaña de certificación","Airbus recomienda no operar intencionadamente por encima de ese valor"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the maximum demonstrated crosswind of 38 kt, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["afm","limitation","demonstrated"],"answer":"It is false: the FCOM expressly states that the maximum demonstrated value is NOT an AFM limitation, but the maximum condition experienced during the certification campaign. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["It is an Airplane Flight Manual (AFM) limitation","It includes the gust","It is the maximum crosswind condition experienced during the certification campaign","Airbus recommends not to intentionally operate above that value"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0015","es":{"q":"En pista seca, el viento reportado da 40 kt de componente cruzada con ráfagas incluidas. ¿Qué establece LIM-AG-OPS?","keys":["38","kt","afm"],"answer":"El FCOM aclara que los 38 kt demostrados no son una limitación del AFM, sino la máxima condición experimentada en certificación, y que Airbus recomienda a los operadores no operar intencionadamente por encima de ese valor. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No es una limitación del AFM, pero Airbus recomienda no operar intencionadamente por encima de 38 kt","Está prohibido: 38 kt es una limitación del AFM que no puede excederse","Es admisible: en pista seca no hay límite de viento cruzado","Es admisible si se descuenta la ráfaga del viento reportado"]},"en":{"q":"On a dry runway, the reported wind gives 40 kt of crosswind component, gust included. What does LIM-AG-OPS establish?","keys":["38","kt","afm"],"answer":"The FCOM clarifies that the 38 kt demonstrated is not an AFM limitation, but the maximum condition experienced in certification, and that Airbus recommends operators not to intentionally operate above that value. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["It is not an AFM limitation, but Airbus recommends not to intentionally operate above 38 kt","It is prohibited: 38 kt is an AFM limitation that cannot be exceeded","It is acceptable: on a dry runway there is no crosswind limit","It is acceptable if the gust is subtracted from the reported wind"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0016","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el viento en cola máximo para el despegue?","keys":["10","kt","a320"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para este avión un máximo de 10 kt de viento en cola para el despegue. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["10 kt","5 kt","15 kt","20 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum tailwind for takeoff?","keys":["10","kt","a320"],"answer":"For this aircraft the FCOM publishes a maximum of 10 kt tailwind for takeoff. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["10 kt","5 kt","15 kt","20 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0017","es":{"q":"Alineado para despegar con el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), la torre te da un viento que supone 12 kt de componente en cola. ¿Qué procede?","keys":["10","kt","despegar"],"answer":"El viento en cola máximo de despegue publicado para este avión es 10 kt. Con 12 kt de componente en cola hay que solicitar otra pista o esperar. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No despegar por esa pista: el límite de viento en cola para despegue es 10 kt","Despegar: el límite de viento en cola para despegue es 15 kt","Despegar, porque el viento en cola sólo está limitado en el aterrizaje","Despegar aplicando FLAPS FULL"]},"en":{"q":"Lined up for takeoff with the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), the tower gives you a wind amounting to 12 kt of tailwind component. What is appropriate?","keys":["10","kt","takeoff"],"answer":"The maximum takeoff tailwind published for this aircraft is 10 kt. With 12 kt of tailwind component you must request another runway or wait. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 30 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Do not take off from that runway: the takeoff tailwind limit is 10 kt","Take off: the takeoff tailwind limit is 15 kt","Take off, because tailwind is only limited for landing","Take off applying FLAPS FULL"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0018","es":{"q":"En aproximación con el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), el ATIS da un viento que supone 13 kt de componente en cola en la pista en servicio. ¿Qué procede?","keys":["10","kt","solicitar"],"answer":"El viento en cola máximo de aterrizaje publicado para este avión es 10 kt; 13 kt lo excede y hay que pedir otra pista o desviarse. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 31 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["Solicitar otra pista: el límite de viento en cola para aterrizar es 10 kt","Continuar: el límite de viento en cola para aterrizar es 15 kt","Continuar seleccionando FLAPS FULL, que amplía el límite a 15 kt","Continuar: 13 kt está por debajo del crosswind máximo demostrado de 38 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On approach with the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), the ATIS gives a wind amounting to 13 kt of tailwind component on the runway in use. What is appropriate?","keys":["10","kt","tailwind"],"answer":"The maximum landing tailwind published for this aircraft is 10 kt; 13 kt exceeds it and you must request another runway or divert. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 31 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["Request another runway: the landing tailwind limit is 10 kt","Continue: the landing tailwind limit is 15 kt","Continue selecting FLAPS FULL, which extends the limit to 15 kt","Continue: 13 kt is below the maximum demonstrated crosswind of 38 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0019","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), para conocer el viento en cola máximo en aterrizaje automático y rollout, la nota de TAILWIND LANDING remite a:","keys":["20","cat ii","a320"],"answer":"La nota remite a LIM-AFS-20, 'Maximum Wind Conditions for ILS/MLS (If Installed) CAT II or CAT III and for GLS (If Installed) CAT I or CAT II'. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 31 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["LIM-AFS-20","LIM-AFS-10","LIM-AG-SPD","LIM-NAV"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), to determine the maximum tailwind for automatic landing and rollout, the TAILWIND LANDING note refers to:","keys":["20","afs","cat"],"answer":"The note refers to LIM-AFS-20, 'Maximum Wind Conditions for ILS/MLS (If Installed) CAT II or CAT III and for GLS (If Installed) CAT I or CAT II'. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 31 · rev 21 MAR 17)","opts":["LIM-AFS-20","LIM-AFS-10","LIM-AG-SPD","LIM-NAV"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0020","es":{"q":"Según LIM-AG-OPS, las puertas de carga FWD y AFT deben estar cerradas antes de que la velocidad del viento supere:","keys":["65","kt","puertas"],"answer":"El FCOM exige que las puertas de carga FWD y AFT estén cerradas antes de que el viento supere los 65 kt. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["65 kt","40 kt","50 kt","75 kt"]},"en":{"q":"According to LIM-AG-OPS, the FWD and AFT cargo doors must be closed before the wind speed exceeds:","keys":["65","kt","cargo"],"answer":"The FCOM requires the FWD and AFT cargo doors to be closed before the wind exceeds 65 kt. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["65 kt","40 kt","50 kt","75 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0021","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es el viento máximo para la operación de las puertas de carga FWD y AFT?","keys":["40","50","kt"],"answer":"El FCOM publica 40 kt como máximo para las puertas de carga FWD y AFT, ampliable a 50 kt si el morro está encarado al viento o si las puertas quedan en el lado de sotavento. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["40 kt, o 50 kt si el morro del avión está encarado al viento o las puertas quedan a sotavento","50 kt en todos los casos","65 kt, o 50 kt si el morro está encarado al viento","40 kt en todos los casos, sin excepciones"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum wind for operating the FWD and AFT cargo doors?","keys":["40","50","kt"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes 40 kt as the maximum for the FWD and AFT cargo doors, extendable to 50 kt if the nose is headed into the wind or if the doors are on the leeward side. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["40 kt, or 50 kt if the aircraft nose is headed into the wind or the doors are on the leeward side","50 kt in all cases","65 kt, or 50 kt if the nose is headed into the wind","40 kt in all cases, without exceptions"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0022","es":{"q":"En plataforma sopla un viento de 48 kt y el avión está estacionado con el morro encarado al viento. ¿Puede la asistencia operar las puertas de carga FWD y AFT?","keys":["50","kt","morro"],"answer":"Con el morro encarado al viento (o con las puertas de carga a sotavento) el máximo para operar las puertas de carga FWD y AFT sube de 40 kt a 50 kt; 48 kt queda por debajo. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["Sí: con el morro encarado al viento el máximo para puertas de carga es 50 kt","No: el máximo para puertas de carga es 40 kt en cualquier circunstancia","Sí: el máximo para puertas de carga es 65 kt","No: por encima de 40 kt sólo pueden abrirse las puertas de pasaje"]},"en":{"q":"On the apron a wind of 48 kt is blowing and the aircraft is parked with the nose headed into the wind. Can the ground crew operate the FWD and AFT cargo doors?","keys":["50","kt","nose"],"answer":"With the nose headed into the wind (or with the cargo doors on the leeward side) the maximum for operating the FWD and AFT cargo doors rises from 40 kt to 50 kt; 48 kt is below it. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["Yes: with the nose headed into the wind the maximum for the cargo doors is 50 kt","No: the maximum for the cargo doors is 40 kt under any circumstances","Yes: the maximum for the cargo doors is 65 kt","No: above 40 kt only the passenger doors may be opened"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0023","es":{"q":"Pista mojada (wet, hasta 3 mm de agua) con AIREP de acción de frenado 'Good'. Según la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS, ¿cuál es el viento cruzado máximo recomendado para el despegue?","keys":["38","kt","airep"],"answer":"La primera banda de la tabla (damp, wet hasta 3 mm, slush/dry snow/wet snow hasta 3 mm, frost) con AIREP 'Good' da 38 kt con ráfaga incluida, tanto para despegue como para aterrizaje. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["38 kt (ráfaga incluida)","25 kt (ráfaga incluida)","29 kt (ráfaga incluida)","33 kt (ráfaga incluida)"]},"en":{"q":"Wet runway (wet, up to 3 mm of water) with a braking action AIREP of 'Good'. According to the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table, what is the maximum recommended crosswind for takeoff?","keys":["38","kt","airep"],"answer":"The first band of the table (damp, wet up to 3 mm, slush/dry snow/wet snow up to 3 mm, frost) with AIREP 'Good' gives 38 kt gust included, for both takeoff and landing. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["38 kt (gust included)","25 kt (gust included)","29 kt (gust included)","33 kt (gust included)"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0024","es":{"q":"Pista con nieve compactada (compacted snow) y OAT igual o inferior a -15 °C. Según la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS, ¿qué viento cruzado máximo recomendado y qué RWYCC le corresponden?","keys":["29","4","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"La nieve compactada con OAT igual o inferior a -15 °C figura en la banda AIREP 'Good to Medium', con 29 kt de crosswind máximo recomendado (despegue y aterrizaje) y RWYCC 4 / nivel GOOD TO MEDIUM. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["29 kt y RWYCC 4","38 kt y RWYCC 5","25 kt y RWYCC 3","20 kt y RWYCC 2"]},"en":{"q":"Runway with compacted snow and OAT at or below -15 °C. According to the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table, what maximum recommended crosswind and what RWYCC apply?","keys":["29","4","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"Compacted snow with OAT at or below -15 °C is in the AIREP 'Good to Medium' band, with 29 kt maximum recommended crosswind (takeoff and landing) and RWYCC 4 / GOOD TO MEDIUM level. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["29 kt and RWYCC 4","38 kt and RWYCC 5","25 kt and RWYCC 3","20 kt and RWYCC 2"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0025","es":{"q":"Vas a despegar de una pista con nieve compactada y OAT de -20 °C; el AIREP reporta acción de frenado 'Good to Medium'. El viento cruzado es de 31 kt con ráfagas. Según LIM-AG-OPS:","keys":["29","kt","airep"],"answer":"Con nieve compactada a -20 °C (OAT igual o inferior a -15 °C) y AIREP 'Good to Medium' la tabla recomienda un máximo de 29 kt con ráfaga incluida; 31 kt lo excede. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["Excede el máximo recomendado para esa condición, que es 29 kt con ráfaga incluida","Es aceptable: el crosswind máximo demostrado es 38 kt","Es aceptable: con AIREP 'Good to Medium' el máximo recomendado es 38 kt","Excede el máximo recomendado para esa condición, que es 25 kt con ráfaga incluida"]},"en":{"q":"You are about to take off from a runway with compacted snow and OAT of -20 °C; the AIREP reports braking action 'Good to Medium'. The crosswind is 31 kt with gusts. According to LIM-AG-OPS:","keys":["29","kt","airep"],"answer":"With compacted snow at -20 °C (OAT at or below -15 °C) and AIREP 'Good to Medium' the table recommends a maximum of 29 kt gust included; 31 kt exceeds it. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["It exceeds the maximum recommended for that condition, which is 29 kt gust included","It is acceptable: the maximum demonstrated crosswind is 38 kt","It is acceptable: with AIREP 'Good to Medium' the maximum recommended is 38 kt","It exceeds the maximum recommended for that condition, which is 25 kt gust included"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0026","es":{"q":"Pista con nieve seca de más de 3 mm y hasta 100 mm. Según la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS, ¿qué AIREP y qué viento cruzado máximo recomendado le corresponden?","keys":["25","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"La nieve seca de más de 3 mm y hasta 100 mm está en la banda AIREP 'Medium' / RWYCC 3 / nivel MEDIUM, con 25 kt de crosswind máximo recomendado para despegue y aterrizaje. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["'Medium' y 25 kt","'Good to Medium' y 29 kt","'Medium to Poor' y 20 kt","'Poor' y 15 kt"]},"en":{"q":"Runway with dry snow of more than 3 mm and up to 100 mm. According to the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table, what AIREP and what maximum recommended crosswind apply?","keys":["25","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"Dry snow of more than 3 mm and up to 100 mm is in the AIREP 'Medium' band / RWYCC 3 / MEDIUM level, with 25 kt maximum recommended crosswind for takeoff and landing. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["'Medium' and 25 kt","'Good to Medium' and 29 kt","'Medium to Poor' and 20 kt","'Poor' and 15 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0027","es":{"q":"El estado de pista notificado es 'slippery wet'. ¿Qué viento cruzado máximo recomendado para el aterrizaje aplica según LIM-AG-OPS?","keys":["25","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"'Slippery wet' figura en la banda AIREP 'Medium' / RWYCC 3 / nivel MEDIUM, cuyo crosswind máximo recomendado para aterrizaje es 25 kt con ráfaga incluida. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["25 kt","38 kt: 'slippery wet' es una pista mojada","29 kt","15 kt"]},"en":{"q":"The reported runway state is 'slippery wet'. What maximum recommended crosswind for landing applies according to LIM-AG-OPS?","keys":["25","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"'Slippery wet' is in the AIREP 'Medium' band / RWYCC 3 / MEDIUM level, whose maximum recommended crosswind for landing is 25 kt gust included. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["25 kt","38 kt: 'slippery wet' is a wet runway","29 kt","15 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0028","es":{"q":"Pista con agua estancada (standing water) de más de 3 mm y hasta 13 mm. Según la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS, ¿qué RWYCC y qué viento cruzado máximo recomendado le corresponden?","keys":["2","20","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"El agua estancada de más de 3 mm y hasta 13 mm (junto con el slush de ese mismo espesor) figura con AIREP 'Medium to Poor', RWYCC 2 / nivel MEDIUM TO POOR y 20 kt de crosswind máximo recomendado, tanto para despegue como para aterrizaje. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["RWYCC 2 y 20 kt","RWYCC 3 y 25 kt","RWYCC 1 y 15 kt","RWYCC 4 y 29 kt"]},"en":{"q":"Runway with standing water of more than 3 mm and up to 13 mm. According to the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table, what RWYCC and what maximum recommended crosswind apply?","keys":["2","20","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"Standing water of more than 3 mm and up to 13 mm (together with slush of that same depth) is listed with AIREP 'Medium to Poor', RWYCC 2 / MEDIUM TO POOR level and 20 kt maximum recommended crosswind, for both takeoff and landing. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["RWYCC 2 and 20 kt","RWYCC 3 and 25 kt","RWYCC 1 and 15 kt","RWYCC 4 and 29 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0029","es":{"q":"Destino con pista cubierta de hielo (ice, cold & dry) y AIREP de acción de frenado 'Poor'. El viento cruzado es de 18 kt con ráfagas. Según LIM-AG-OPS:","keys":["15","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"El hielo (cold & dry) es el único contaminante de la banda AIREP 'Poor' / RWYCC 1 / nivel POOR, con un crosswind máximo recomendado de 15 kt con ráfaga incluida; 18 kt lo excede. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["Excede el máximo recomendado para esa condición, que es 15 kt con ráfaga incluida","Es aceptable: el máximo recomendado para esa condición es 20 kt","Es aceptable: el máximo recomendado para esa condición es 25 kt","Es aceptable: en aterrizaje el crosswind sólo está limitado por los 38 kt demostrados"]},"en":{"q":"Destination with a runway covered in ice (ice, cold & dry) and a braking action AIREP of 'Poor'. The crosswind is 18 kt with gusts. According to LIM-AG-OPS:","keys":["15","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"Ice (cold & dry) is the only contaminant in the AIREP 'Poor' band / RWYCC 1 / POOR level, with a maximum recommended crosswind of 15 kt gust included; 18 kt exceeds it. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["It exceeds the maximum recommended for that condition, which is 15 kt gust included","It is acceptable: the maximum recommended for that condition is 20 kt","It is acceptable: the maximum recommended for that condition is 25 kt","It is acceptable: for landing the crosswind is only limited by the 38 kt demonstrated"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0030","es":{"q":"Sobre la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["airep","valores","viento"],"answer":"Es falsa: las columnas de la tabla se publican expresamente como 'Gust included', es decir, los valores incluyen la ráfaga. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["Los valores de viento cruzado de la tabla no incluyen la ráfaga","Son valores recomendados, basados en cálculos","AIREP es un informe especial en vuelo de la acción de frenado (Special Air Report of Braking Action)","RWYCC es el código de condición de pista (Runway Condition Code)"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["gust","airep","values"],"answer":"It is false: the columns of the table are expressly published as 'Gust included', that is, the values include the gust. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["The crosswind values in the table do not include the gust","They are recommended values, based on calculations","AIREP is a Special Air Report of Braking Action","RWYCC is the Runway Condition Code"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0031","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es el viento máximo para la operación de las puertas de pasaje?","keys":["65","kt","viento"],"answer":"El FCOM publica un viento máximo de 65 kt para la operación de las puertas de pasaje. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["65 kt","40 kt","50 kt","60 kt"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum wind for operating the passenger doors?","keys":["65","kt","passenger"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes a maximum wind of 65 kt for operating the passenger doors. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 32 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["65 kt","40 kt","50 kt","60 kt"]}},{"sys":"ARPT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0032","es":{"q":"La pista de salida está cubierta de slush (nieve fundente) de unos 8 mm de espesor. El viento cruzado es de 24 kt con ráfagas. Según la tabla MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS:","keys":["20","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"El espesor manda: el slush de más de 3 mm y hasta 13 mm comparte fila con el standing water del mismo espesor, en la banda AIREP 'Medium to Poor' / RWYCC 2, con un máximo recomendado de 20 kt con ráfaga incluida. Con 8 mm de slush y 24 kt de componente cruzada se excede. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 33 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["Excede el máximo recomendado para esa condición, que es 20 kt con ráfaga incluida","Es aceptable: el slush tiene un máximo recomendado de 38 kt","Es aceptable: el slush tiene un máximo recomendado de 25 kt","Excede el máximo recomendado para esa condición, que es 15 kt con ráfaga incluida"]},"en":{"q":"The departure runway is covered in slush about 8 mm thick. The crosswind is 24 kt with gusts. According to the MAXIMUM RECOMMENDED CROSSWIND ON WET AND CONTAMINATED RUNWAYS table:","keys":["20","kt","rwycc"],"answer":"Depth governs: slush of more than 3 mm and up to 13 mm shares a row with standing water of the same depth, in the AIREP 'Medium to Poor' band / RWYCC 2, with a maximum recommended of 20 kt gust included. With 8 mm of slush and 24 kt of crosswind component it is exceeded. (FCOM LIM-AG-OPS · p. 33 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["It exceeds the maximum recommended for that condition, which is 20 kt gust included","It is acceptable: slush has a maximum recommended of 38 kt","It is acceptable: slush has a maximum recommended of 25 kt","It exceeds the maximum recommended for that condition, which is 15 kt gust included"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0033","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima con una ventanilla de cockpit abierta?","keys":["200","kt","velocidad"],"answer":"La limitación COCKPIT WINDOW OPEN MAXIMUM SPEED es de 200 kt. Aplica a toda la flota, sin distinción de modelo ni de motor. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["200 kt","180 kt","195 kt","230 kt"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum speed with a cockpit window open?","keys":["200","kt","window"],"answer":"The COCKPIT WINDOW OPEN MAXIMUM SPEED limitation is 200 kt. It applies to the whole fleet, regardless of model or engine. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["200 kt","180 kt","195 kt","230 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0034","es":{"q":"En un A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es la velocidad máxima en CONF 1 (HOLDING)?","keys":["243","kt","vfe"],"answer":"En la tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS del A321neo, la CONF 1 (fase HOLDING) tiene una velocidad máxima de 243 kt. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["243 kt","215 kt","225 kt","230 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the maximum speed in CONF 1 (HOLDING)?","keys":["243","kt","vfe"],"answer":"In the A321neo MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table, CONF 1 (HOLDING phase) has a maximum speed of 243 kt. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["243 kt","215 kt","225 kt","230 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0035","es":{"q":"Vuelas un A321neo (motores PW1100G) y en aproximación seleccionas CONF 3. ¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima que no debes exceder?","keys":["195","kt","vfe"],"answer":"En la tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS del A321neo, la CONF 3 (fase TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING) está limitada a 195 kt. (Verificado sobre la página 35 del PDF: la tabla imprime CONF 2 = 215 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) y CONF 3 = 195 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING) para ese grupo.) (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["195 kt","186 kt","190 kt","215 kt"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying an A321neo (PW1100G engines) and on approach you select CONF 3. What is the maximum speed you must not exceed?","keys":["195","kt","vfe"],"answer":"In the A321neo MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table, CONF 3 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING phase) is limited to 195 kt. (Verified on page 35 of the PDF: the table prints CONF 2 = 215 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) and CONF 3 = 195 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING) for that group.) (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["195 kt","186 kt","190 kt","215 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0036","es":{"q":"Sobre la tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS de un A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["2","195","kt","vfe"],"answer":"Es falsa: en el A321neo la CONF 2 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) está limitada a 215 kt. Los 195 kt corresponden a la CONF 3 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING). El resto de afirmaciones reproducen la tabla correctamente. (Verificado sobre la página 35 del PDF: la tabla imprime CONF 2 = 215 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) y CONF 3 = 195 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING) para ese grupo.) (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["En CONF 2 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) la velocidad máxima es 195 kt.","En CONF 1 (HOLDING) la velocidad máxima es 243 kt.","En CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF) la velocidad máxima es 225 kt.","En CONF FULL (LANDING) la velocidad máxima es 186 kt."]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table of an A321neo (PW1100G engines), which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["2","195","kt","vfe"],"answer":"It is false: on the A321neo CONF 2 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) is limited to 215 kt. The 195 kt corresponds to CONF 3 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING). The rest of the statements reproduce the table correctly. (Verified on page 35 of the PDF: the table prints CONF 2 = 215 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) and CONF 3 = 195 kt (TAKEOFF/APPROACH/LANDING) for that group.) (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["In CONF 2 (TAKEOFF/APPROACH) the maximum speed is 195 kt.","In CONF 1 (HOLDING) the maximum speed is 243 kt.","In CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF) the maximum speed is 225 kt.","In CONF FULL (LANDING) the maximum speed is 186 kt."]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0037","es":{"q":"En un A320 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la velocidad máxima en CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF)?","keys":["215","kt","vfe"],"answer":"La tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS aplicable a los A319/A320 con CFM56, a los A320 con IAE V2500 y a los A320neo publica 215 kt para CONF 1+F en fase TAKEOFF. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["215 kt","200 kt","225 kt","230 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the maximum speed in CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF)?","keys":["215","kt","vfe"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table applicable to the A319/A320 with CFM56, the A320 with IAE V2500 and the A320neo publishes 215 kt for CONF 1+F in the TAKEOFF phase. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["215 kt","200 kt","225 kt","230 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0038","es":{"q":"Estás en corta final con un A319 (motores CFM56) y CONF FULL seleccionada. ¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima permitida en esa configuración?","keys":["177","kt","vfe"],"answer":"La tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS de los A319/A320 con CFM56, A320 con IAE V2500 y A320neo publica 177 kt para CONF FULL en fase LANDING. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["177 kt","185 kt","186 kt","190 kt"]},"en":{"q":"You are on short final with an A319 (CFM56 engines) and CONF FULL selected. What is the maximum speed allowed in that configuration?","keys":["177","kt","vfe"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table of the A319/A320 with CFM56, A320 with IAE V2500 and A320neo publishes 177 kt for CONF FULL in the LANDING phase. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["177 kt","185 kt","186 kt","190 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0039","es":{"q":"¿A qué aviones de la flota aplica la tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS con CONF 1 = 230 kt y CONF FULL = 177 kt?","keys":["319","320","vfe"],"answer":"Esa tabla es la aplicable a los A319 y A320 con motores CFM56, a los A320 con motores IAE V2500 y a los A320neo con PW1100G. Los A321 CEO y los A321neo tienen cada uno su propia tabla, con valores distintos. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["A los A319 y A320 con CFM56, a los A320 con IAE V2500 y a los A320neo con PW1100G.","A toda la flota A319/A320/A321, sin distinción.","Sólo a los A321 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500).","Sólo a los A321neo (motores PW1100G)."]},"en":{"q":"To which fleet aircraft does the MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table with CONF 1 = 230 kt and CONF FULL = 177 kt apply?","keys":["319","320","vfe"],"answer":"That table is the one applicable to the A319 and A320 with CFM56 engines, the A320 with IAE V2500 engines and the A320neo with PW1100G. The A321 CEO and the A321neo each have their own table, with different values. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["To the A319 and A320 with CFM56, the A320 with IAE V2500 and the A320neo with PW1100G.","To the whole A319/A320/A321 fleet, without distinction.","Only to the A321 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines).","Only to the A321neo (PW1100G engines)."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0040","es":{"q":"¿Cuánto mayor es la velocidad máxima en CONF 1 (HOLDING) de un A321neo (motores PW1100G) frente a la de un A320 con motores IAE V2500?","keys":["13","kt","vfe"],"answer":"El A321neo publica 243 kt en CONF 1, frente a los 230 kt del A320 con IAE V2500: 243 − 230 = 13 kt más. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["13 kt","8 kt","10 kt","15 kt"]},"en":{"q":"How much greater is the maximum speed in CONF 1 (HOLDING) of an A321neo (PW1100G engines) than that of an A320 with IAE V2500 engines?","keys":["13","kt","vfe"],"answer":"The A321neo publishes 243 kt in CONF 1, versus the 230 kt of the A320 with IAE V2500: 243 − 230 = 13 kt more. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 35 · rev 04 SEP 18)","opts":["13 kt","8 kt","10 kt","15 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0041","es":{"q":"En un A321 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), ¿cuál es la velocidad máxima en CONF FULL (LANDING)?","keys":["190","kt","vfe"],"answer":"La tabla MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS de los A321 CEO publica 190 kt para CONF FULL en fase LANDING. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["190 kt","177 kt","186 kt","195 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), what is the maximum speed in CONF FULL (LANDING)?","keys":["190","kt","vfe"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM FLAPS/SLATS SPEEDS table of the A321 CEO publishes 190 kt for CONF FULL in the LANDING phase. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["190 kt","177 kt","186 kt","195 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0042","es":{"q":"Todas estas velocidades máximas de flaps/slats son correctas según el FCOM, EXCEPTO:","keys":["321","1100","kt","vfe"],"answer":"En el A321neo la CONF 1+F está limitada a 225 kt, no a 215 kt. Los 215 kt son la CONF 1+F del grupo A319/A320 CEO y A320neo, y también la CONF 1+F de los A321 CEO. Las otras tres opciones reproducen fielmente sus tablas. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["A321neo (PW1100G), CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF): 215 kt.","A321neo (PW1100G), CONF 1 (HOLDING): 243 kt.","A319 con CFM56, CONF FULL (LANDING): 177 kt.","A321 CEO (CFM56 o IAE V2500), CONF FULL (LANDING): 190 kt."]},"en":{"q":"All of these maximum flaps/slats speeds are correct according to the FCOM, EXCEPT:","keys":["321","1100","kt","vfe"],"answer":"On the A321neo CONF 1+F is limited to 225 kt, not 215 kt. The 215 kt is the CONF 1+F of the A319/A320 CEO and A320neo group, and also the CONF 1+F of the A321 CEO. The other three options faithfully reproduce their tables. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["A321neo (PW1100G), CONF 1+F (TAKEOFF): 215 kt.","A321neo (PW1100G), CONF 1 (HOLDING): 243 kt.","A319 with CFM56, CONF FULL (LANDING): 177 kt.","A321 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500), CONF FULL (LANDING): 190 kt."]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0043","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la VMO publicada?","keys":["350","kt","vmo"],"answer":"La MAXIMUM OPERATING SPEED es VMO 350 kt (con MMO M 0.82). Aplica a toda la flota. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["350 kt","330 kt","340 kt","360 kt"]},"en":{"q":"What is the published VMO?","keys":["350","kt","vmo"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM OPERATING SPEED is VMO 350 kt (with MMO M 0.82). It applies to the whole fleet. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["350 kt","330 kt","340 kt","360 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0044","es":{"q":"¿Cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la VMO/MMO es FALSA?","keys":["vmo","varia","modelo"],"answer":"Es falsa: la VMO/MMO se publica como 'Applicable to: ALL', es decir, es la misma para toda la flota A319/A320/A321 con independencia del modelo y del motor. Las otras tres afirmaciones son correctas. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La VMO/MMO varía según el modelo y el motor del avión.","La VMO es 350 kt.","La MMO es M 0.82.","Con la palanca de flaps en 0 (CRUISE), la velocidad máxima es VMO/MMO."]},"en":{"q":"Which of these statements about the VMO/MMO is FALSE?","keys":["vmo","fleet","model"],"answer":"It is false: the VMO/MMO is published as 'Applicable to: ALL', that is, it is the same for the whole A319/A320/A321 fleet regardless of model and engine. The other three statements are correct. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 36 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The VMO/MMO varies with the aircraft model and engine.","The VMO is 350 kt.","The MMO is M 0.82.","With the flap lever at 0 (CRUISE), the maximum speed is VMO/MMO."]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0045","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima con el tren de aterrizaje extendido (VLE)?","keys":["280","0.67","kt","vle"],"answer":"La VLE (maximum speed with the landing gear extended) es 280 kt / M 0.67. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["280 kt / M 0.67","220 kt / M 0.54","250 kt / M 0.60","300 kt / M 0.70"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum speed with the landing gear extended (VLE)?","keys":["280","0.67","kt","vle"],"answer":"The VLE (maximum speed with the landing gear extended) is 280 kt / M 0.67. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["280 kt / M 0.67","220 kt / M 0.54","250 kt / M 0.60","300 kt / M 0.70"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0046","es":{"q":"El tren queda bloqueado abajo y decides continuar hasta el alternativo. En descenso, el avión acelera hasta 275 kt / M 0.60. ¿Qué es correcto?","keys":["280","0.67","kt","vle"],"answer":"Con el tren extendido el límite es la VLE, 280 kt / M 0.67. A 275 kt / M 0.60 estás dentro tanto del límite de IAS como del de Mach. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Estás dentro de límites: la VLE es 280 kt / M 0.67.","Has excedido la VLE, que es 250 kt / M 0.60.","Has excedido la VLE, que es 220 kt / M 0.54.","No aplica ninguna limitación de velocidad si el tren no se puede retraer."]},"en":{"q":"The gear is locked down and you decide to continue to the alternate. In the descent, the aircraft accelerates to 275 kt / M 0.60. What is correct?","keys":["280","0.67","kt","vle"],"answer":"With the gear extended the limit is the VLE, 280 kt / M 0.67. At 275 kt / M 0.60 you are within both the IAS limit and the Mach limit. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["You are within limits: the VLE is 280 kt / M 0.67.","You have exceeded the VLE, which is 250 kt / M 0.60.","You have exceeded the VLE, which is 220 kt / M 0.54.","No speed limitation applies if the gear cannot be retracted."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0047","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima a la que se puede extender el tren de aterrizaje (VLO extension)?","keys":["250","0.60","kt","vlo"],"answer":"La VLO de extensión (maximum speed at which the landing gear may be extended) es 250 kt / M 0.60. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["250 kt / M 0.60","220 kt / M 0.54","240 kt / M 0.58","280 kt / M 0.67"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum speed at which the landing gear may be extended (VLO extension)?","keys":["250","0.60","kt","vlo"],"answer":"The VLO for extension (maximum speed at which the landing gear may be extended) is 250 kt / M 0.60. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["250 kt / M 0.60","220 kt / M 0.54","240 kt / M 0.58","280 kt / M 0.67"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0048","es":{"q":"¿Cuántos nudos menor es la VLO de retracción respecto a la VLO de extensión?","keys":["30","kt","vlo"],"answer":"La VLO de extensión es 250 kt y la de retracción 220 kt: la de retracción es 30 kt menor. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["30 kt","20 kt","40 kt","60 kt"]},"en":{"q":"By how many knots is the VLO for retraction lower than the VLO for extension?","keys":["30","kt","vlo"],"answer":"The VLO for extension is 250 kt and for retraction 220 kt: the retraction one is 30 kt lower. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["30 kt","20 kt","40 kt","60 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0049","es":{"q":"Durante un descenso de emergencia estabilizas a 235 kt (Mach no limitativo). ¿Qué puedes hacer con el tren de aterrizaje?","keys":["vlo","extenderlo","retraerlo"],"answer":"A 235 kt estás por debajo de la VLO de extensión (250 kt), así que puedes extender el tren; pero estás por encima de la VLO de retracción (220 kt), así que no puedes retraerlo hasta reducir a 220 kt o menos. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Extenderlo, pero no retraerlo a esa velocidad.","Extenderlo y, si hace falta, retraerlo de nuevo a esa velocidad.","Retraerlo, pero no extenderlo a esa velocidad.","Ni extenderlo ni retraerlo: 235 kt excede ambas VLO."]},"en":{"q":"During an emergency descent you stabilise at 235 kt (Mach not limiting). What can you do with the landing gear?","keys":["vlo","extend","retract"],"answer":"At 235 kt you are below the VLO for extension (250 kt), so you can extend the gear; but you are above the VLO for retraction (220 kt), so you cannot retract it until you reduce to 220 kt or less. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Extend it, but not retract it at that speed.","Extend it and, if needed, retract it again at that speed.","Retract it, but not extend it at that speed.","Neither extend nor retract it: 235 kt exceeds both VLO."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0050","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima de neumático (maximum tire speed)?","keys":["195","kt","ground"],"answer":"El límite MAXIMUM TIRE SPEED se expresa como maximum ground speed: 195 kt. Aplica a toda la flota. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["195 kt de ground speed","185 kt de ground speed","190 kt de ground speed","200 kt de ground speed"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum tire speed?","keys":["195","kt","ground"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM TIRE SPEED limit is expressed as a maximum ground speed: 195 kt. It applies to the whole fleet. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["195 kt ground speed","185 kt ground speed","190 kt ground speed","200 kt ground speed"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0051","es":{"q":"Despegas de un aeropuerto de elevación elevada, día caluroso y con componente de viento en cola. Los cálculos indican que en rotación la ground speed sería de 200 kt. ¿Qué limitación estás comprometiendo?","keys":["195","kt","velocidad"],"answer":"El MAXIMUM TIRE SPEED se publica como maximum ground speed 195 kt. Una ground speed de 200 kt en rotación excede el límite, y por eso la elevación, la temperatura y el viento en cola son los factores que lo comprometen. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La velocidad máxima de neumático, que es 195 kt de ground speed.","Ninguna: el límite de neumático se expresa en IAS, no en ground speed.","La velocidad máxima de neumático, que es 195 kt de IAS.","La velocidad máxima con la ventanilla de cockpit abierta, que es 200 kt."]},"en":{"q":"You take off from a high-elevation airport, on a hot day and with a tailwind component. Calculations show that at rotation the ground speed would be 200 kt. Which limitation are you compromising?","keys":["195","kt","tire"],"answer":"The MAXIMUM TIRE SPEED is published as a maximum ground speed of 195 kt. A ground speed of 200 kt at rotation exceeds the limit, and that is why elevation, temperature and tailwind are the factors that compromise it. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 37 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The maximum tire speed, which is 195 kt ground speed.","None: the tire limit is expressed in IAS, not in ground speed.","The maximum tire speed, which is 195 kt IAS.","The maximum speed with the cockpit window open, which is 200 kt."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0052","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la VMCL (minimum control speed for landing)?","keys":["109","kt","vmcl"],"answer":"El bloque MINIMUM CONTROL SPEEDS aplicable al avión de referencia publica VMCL = 109 kt. Este dato se certifica avión a avión: otros grupos de la flota, aun siendo del mismo modelo y motor, tienen VMCL distinta. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["109 kt","108 kt","111 kt","116 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the VMCL (minimum control speed for landing)?","keys":["109","kt","vmcl"],"answer":"The MINIMUM CONTROL SPEEDS block applicable to the reference aircraft publishes VMCL = 109 kt. This figure is certified aircraft by aircraft: other fleet groups, even of the same model and engine, have a different VMCL. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["109 kt","108 kt","111 kt","116 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0053","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la VMCA a nivel del mar (0 ft)?","keys":["112","kt","vmca"],"answer":"En la tabla MINIMUM CONTROL SPEEDS IN THE AIR (VMCA) AND ON THE GROUND (VMCG) del avión de referencia, la VMCA a 0 ft es 112 kt IAS. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["112 kt","109 kt","111 kt","114 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the VMCA at sea level (0 ft)?","keys":["112","kt","vmca"],"answer":"In the MINIMUM CONTROL SPEEDS IN THE AIR (VMCA) AND ON THE GROUND (VMCG) table for the reference aircraft, the VMCA at 0 ft is 112 kt IAS. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["112 kt","109 kt","111 kt","114 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0054","es":{"q":"Operas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) desde un aeródromo situado a 6 000 ft de elevación. ¿Qué VMCA debes considerar?","keys":["105","kt","vmca"],"answer":"En la tabla del avión de referencia, la VMCA a 6 000 ft es 105 kt IAS. La VMCA decrece con la altitud: 112 kt a nivel del mar, 105 kt a 6 000 ft y 94 kt a 14 100 ft. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["105 kt","100 kt","103 kt","108 kt"]},"en":{"q":"You operate the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) from an aerodrome located at 6 000 ft elevation. Which VMCA must you consider?","keys":["105","kt","vmca"],"answer":"In the reference aircraft table, the VMCA at 6 000 ft is 105 kt IAS. VMCA decreases with altitude: 112 kt at sea level, 105 kt at 6 000 ft and 94 kt at 14 100 ft. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["105 kt","100 kt","103 kt","108 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0055","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la VMCG en CONF 3 a nivel del mar (0 ft)?","keys":["109","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"En la tabla VMCG del avión de referencia, a 0 ft la columna CONF 3 publica 109 kt IAS. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["109 kt","108 kt","110 kt","112 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the VMCG in CONF 3 at sea level (0 ft)?","keys":["109","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"In the VMCG table for the reference aircraft, at 0 ft the CONF 3 column publishes 109 kt IAS. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["109 kt","108 kt","110 kt","112 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0056","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), a 14 100 ft, ¿qué diferencia hay entre la VMCG en CONF 1+F y la VMCG en CONF 3?","keys":["1","2","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"A 14 100 ft el avión de referencia publica VMCG CONF 1+F = 95 kt y VMCG CONF 3 = 93 kt: la de CONF 1+F es 2 kt mayor. En toda la tabla la VMCG en CONF 1+F es igual o mayor que en CONF 3. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["La de CONF 1+F es 2 kt mayor (95 kt frente a 93 kt).","Son iguales: 93 kt en ambas.","La de CONF 3 es 2 kt mayor (95 kt frente a 93 kt).","La de CONF 1+F es 5 kt mayor (98 kt frente a 93 kt)."]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), at 14 100 ft, what is the difference between the VMCG in CONF 1+F and the VMCG in CONF 3?","keys":["1","2","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"At 14 100 ft the reference aircraft publishes VMCG CONF 1+F = 95 kt and VMCG CONF 3 = 93 kt: the CONF 1+F value is 2 kt higher. Throughout the table the VMCG in CONF 1+F is equal to or higher than in CONF 3. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 40 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["The CONF 1+F value is 2 kt higher (95 kt versus 93 kt).","They are equal: 93 kt in both.","The CONF 3 value is 2 kt higher (95 kt versus 93 kt).","The CONF 1+F value is 5 kt higher (98 kt versus 93 kt)."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0057","es":{"q":"Vas a despegar con el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) de una pista de 30 m de ancho. ¿Qué corrección debes aplicar a la VMCG?","keys":["2.5","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"Para pistas de ancho inferior a 40 m la VMCG debe incrementarse: +2.5 kt con 30 m de ancho, +1.5 kt con 35 m y +0 kt con 40 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["Incrementarla en 2.5 kt.","Ninguna: la VMCG no depende del ancho de pista.","Incrementarla en 1.5 kt.","Reducirla en 2.5 kt."]},"en":{"q":"You are going to take off in the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) from a runway 30 m wide. What correction must you apply to the VMCG?","keys":["2.5","kt","vmcg"],"answer":"For runways narrower than 40 m the VMCG must be increased: +2.5 kt with 30 m width, +1.5 kt with 35 m and +0 kt with 40 m. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["Increase it by 2.5 kt.","None: the VMCG does not depend on runway width.","Increase it by 1.5 kt.","Reduce it by 2.5 kt."]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0058","es":{"q":"En un A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) con un peso de despegue superior a 76 000 kg (167 550 lb), ¿qué velocidad de rodaje no debes exceder en un viraje?","keys":["20","kt","a320"],"answer":"La sección TAXI SPEED incluye un CAUTION: cuando el peso de despegue es superior a 76 000 kg (167 550 lb), no exceder una velocidad de rodaje de 20 kt durante un viraje. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["20 kt","10 kt","15 kt","30 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) with a takeoff weight above 76 000 kg (167 550 lb), what taxi speed must you not exceed in a turn?","keys":["20","kt","a320"],"answer":"The TAXI SPEED section includes a CAUTION: when the takeoff weight is above 76 000 kg (167 550 lb), do not exceed a taxi speed of 20 kt during a turn. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["20 kt","10 kt","15 kt","30 kt"]}},{"sys":"SPD","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0059","es":{"q":"Vuelas en lluvia intensa a 240 kt y consideras conectar los limpiaparabrisas. ¿Qué es correcto?","keys":["230","kt","debes"],"answer":"La WIPERS MAXIMUM OPERATING SPEED es 230 kt. La nota L2 precisa que la limitación aplica cuando los limpiaparabrisas están barriendo (sweeping), y no aplica si no barren por cualquier motivo. A 240 kt, por tanto, no debes ponerlos a barrer. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No debes usarlos barriendo: la velocidad máxima de operación es 230 kt.","Puedes usarlos: no existe limitación de velocidad para los limpiaparabrisas.","No debes usarlos barriendo: la velocidad máxima de operación es 200 kt.","Puedes usarlos: la limitación de 230 kt sólo aplica con los limpiaparabrisas parados."]},"en":{"q":"You are flying in heavy rain at 240 kt and consider switching on the windshield wipers. What is correct?","keys":["230","kt","wipers"],"answer":"The WIPERS MAXIMUM OPERATING SPEED is 230 kt. Note L2 specifies that the limitation applies when the wipers are sweeping, and does not apply if they are not sweeping for any reason. At 240 kt, therefore, you must not set them sweeping. (FCOM LIM-AG-SPD · p. 42 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["You must not use them sweeping: the maximum operating speed is 230 kt.","You can use them: there is no speed limitation for the windshield wipers.","You must not use them sweeping: the maximum operating speed is 200 kt.","You can use them: the 230 kt limitation only applies with the wipers stopped."]}},{"sys":"WGHT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0060","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el maximum landing weight?","keys":["64500","kg","mlw"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para el avión de referencia un maximum landing weight de 64 500 kg (142 198 lb). (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["64 500 kg","61 000 kg","66 000 kg","73 500 kg"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum landing weight?","keys":["64500","kg","mlw"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes for the reference aircraft a maximum landing weight of 64 500 kg (142 198 lb). (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["64 500 kg","61 000 kg","66 000 kg","73 500 kg"]}},{"sys":"WGHT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0061","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el maximum takeoff weight (brake release)?","keys":["73500","kg","mtow"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para el avión de referencia un maximum takeoff weight (brake release) de 73 500 kg (162 039 lb). El peso máximo se certifica avión a avión, por eso hay que anclar la pregunta a un avión concreto. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["73 500 kg","71 500 kg","73 900 kg","77 000 kg"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum takeoff weight (brake release)?","keys":["73500","kg","mtow"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes for the reference aircraft a maximum takeoff weight (brake release) of 73 500 kg (162 039 lb). The maximum weight is certified aircraft by aircraft, which is why the question must be anchored to a specific aircraft. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["73 500 kg","71 500 kg","73 900 kg","77 000 kg"]}},{"sys":"WGHT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0062","es":{"q":"Cargas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota). El zero fuel weight calculado va por 60 200 kg y handling te ofrece embarcar 1 200 kg más de carga en bodega. ¿Puedes aceptarla?","keys":["61400","400","kg","mzfw"],"answer":"60 200 + 1 200 = 61 400 kg de ZFW, por encima del maximum zero fuel weight de 61 000 kg (134 481 lb) publicado para el avión de referencia. Hay que rechazar 400 kg como mínimo. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["No: el ZFW quedaría en 61 400 kg y superaría en 400 kg el maximum zero fuel weight de 61 000 kg.","Sí: el ZFW quedaría en 61 400 kg, por debajo del maximum zero fuel weight de 62 500 kg.","Sí, siempre que el peso de despegue resultante no supere los 73 500 kg de MTOW.","No: se superaría el maximum landing weight de 64 500 kg."]},"en":{"q":"You are loading the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft). The calculated zero fuel weight is running at 60 200 kg and handling offers to board 1 200 kg more cargo in the hold. Can you accept it?","keys":["61400","400","kg","mzfw"],"answer":"60 200 + 1 200 = 61 400 kg ZFW, above the maximum zero fuel weight of 61 000 kg (134 481 lb) published for the reference aircraft. At least 400 kg must be rejected. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["No: the ZFW would be 61 400 kg and would exceed the maximum zero fuel weight of 61 000 kg by 400 kg.","Yes: the ZFW would be 61 400 kg, below the maximum zero fuel weight of 62 500 kg.","Yes, provided the resulting takeoff weight does not exceed the 73 500 kg MTOW.","No: the maximum landing weight of 64 500 kg would be exceeded."]}},{"sys":"WGHT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0063","es":{"q":"Vuelas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota). Poco después del despegue, una emergencia obliga a un in flight turn back y el peso está claramente por encima del maximum landing weight de 64 500 kg. ¿Qué permite la limitación del FCOM?","keys":["mlw","aterrizar","inmediato"],"answer":"El FCOM contempla el caso excepcional: 'In exceptional cases (in flight turn back or diversion), an immediate landing at weight above maximum landing weight is permitted, provided the pilot follows the overweight landing procedure'. La única condición es aplicar el procedimiento de overweight landing. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["Aterrizar de inmediato es aceptable, siempre que el piloto siga el procedimiento de overweight landing.","Hay que reducir peso hasta el maximum landing weight antes de aterrizar, sin excepción.","Se permite aterrizar por encima del MLW sólo si no se supera el maximum takeoff weight de 73 500 kg.","Se permite aterrizar por encima del MLW hasta el maximum zero fuel weight de 61 000 kg."]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft). Shortly after takeoff, an emergency forces an in flight turn back and the weight is clearly above the maximum landing weight of 64 500 kg. What does the FCOM limitation permit?","keys":["mlw","overweight","immediate"],"answer":"The FCOM covers the exceptional case: 'In exceptional cases (in flight turn back or diversion), an immediate landing at weight above maximum landing weight is permitted, provided the pilot follows the overweight landing procedure'. The only condition is to apply the overweight landing procedure. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["An immediate landing is acceptable, provided the pilot follows the overweight landing procedure.","Weight must be reduced to the maximum landing weight before landing, without exception.","Landing above the MLW is permitted only if the maximum takeoff weight of 73 500 kg is not exceeded.","Landing above the MLW is permitted up to the maximum zero fuel weight of 61 000 kg."]}},{"sys":"WGHT","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0064","es":{"q":"¿Cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones sobre los pesos publicados del EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) es FALSA?","keys":["62500","kg","mtw"],"answer":"El maximum zero fuel weight del avión de referencia es 61 000 kg (134 481 lb), no 62 500 kg. Las otras tres cifras son las publicadas. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["El maximum zero fuel weight es 62 500 kg.","El maximum taxi weight es 73 900 kg.","El minimum weight es 37 230 kg.","El maximum landing weight es 64 500 kg."]},"en":{"q":"Which of the following statements about the published weights of the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) is FALSE?","keys":["62500","kg","mtw"],"answer":"The maximum zero fuel weight of the reference aircraft is 61 000 kg (134 481 lb), not 62 500 kg. The other three figures are the published ones. (FCOM LIM-AG-WGHT · p. 44 · rev 18 MAR 11)","opts":["The maximum zero fuel weight is 62 500 kg.","The maximum taxi weight is 73 900 kg.","The minimum weight is 37 230 kg.","The maximum landing weight is 64 500 kg."]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0065","es":{"q":"¿Qué establece el FCOM sobre el uso simultáneo del aire de sangrado del APU BLEED y de la HP Air Start Unit?","keys":["tripulacion","usar","ambos"],"answer":"La tripulación no debe usar aire de sangrado del APU BLEED y de la HP Air Start Unit al mismo tiempo, para evitar efectos adversos sobre el Bleed Air System. Es una prohibición sin condiciones. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 53 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La tripulación no debe usar ambos a la vez","Está permitido si se limita a 20 min","Está permitido sólo con un pack en servicio","Está permitido siempre que el APU no supere el 107 % de N"]},"en":{"q":"What does the FCOM state about the simultaneous use of bleed air from the APU BLEED and the HP Air Start Unit?","keys":["crew","both","bleed"],"answer":"The crew must not use bleed air from the APU BLEED and the HP Air Start Unit at the same time, to avoid adverse effects on the Bleed Air System. It is an unconditional prohibition. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 53 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The crew must not use both at the same time","It is permitted if limited to 20 min","It is permitted only with one pack in service","It is permitted provided the APU does not exceed 107 % N"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0066","es":{"q":"Con pasajeros a bordo, ¿qué tiempo no se recomienda exceder sin suministro de aire acondicionado?","keys":["20","min","pasajeros"],"answer":"Con pasajeros a bordo no se recomienda exceder 20 min sin suministro de aire acondicionado: la falta de aire fresco reduce significativamente la calidad del aire de cabina. Es una recomendación, no una prohibición. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 53 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 min","10 min","30 min","60 min"]},"en":{"q":"With passengers on board, what time is it not recommended to exceed without air conditioning supply?","keys":["20","min","passengers"],"answer":"With passengers on board it is not recommended to exceed 20 min without air conditioning supply: the lack of fresh air significantly reduces cabin air quality. It is a recommendation, not a prohibition. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 53 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 min","10 min","30 min","60 min"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0067","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), en operaciones en tierra y con el sistema de ventilación de aviónica en configuración normal, ¿hasta qué OAT no hay limitación de tiempo de uso de la alimentación eléctrica del avión?","keys":["49","oat","a320"],"answer":"Para este avión, con OAT ≤ 49 °C no hay limitación de tiempo. A partir de ahí la tabla escalona: 2 h hasta 55 °C, 1 h hasta 60 °C y 0.5 h hasta 64 °C. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["OAT ≤ 49 °C","OAT ≤ 41 °C","OAT ≤ 55 °C","OAT ≤ 64 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), in ground operations and with the avionics ventilation system in normal configuration, up to what OAT is there no time limitation on the use of aircraft electrical power?","keys":["49","oat","a320"],"answer":"For this aircraft, with OAT ≤ 49 °C there is no time limitation. Beyond that the table steps up: 2 h up to 55 °C, 1 h up to 60 °C and 0.5 h up to 64 °C. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["OAT ≤ 49 °C","OAT ≤ 41 °C","OAT ≤ 55 °C","OAT ≤ 64 °C"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0068","es":{"q":"Estás en tierra en el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), con la ventilación de aviónica en configuración normal y una OAT de 58 °C. ¿Cuánto tiempo puedes usar la alimentación eléctrica del avión?","keys":["1","oat","estas"],"answer":"58 °C cae en el escalón 55 °C < OAT ≤ 60 °C, que limita el uso a 1 h. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 h","Sin limitación","2 h","0.5 h"]},"en":{"q":"You are on the ground in the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), with the avionics ventilation in normal configuration and an OAT of 58 °C. How long can you use the aircraft electrical power?","keys":["1","hour","oat"],"answer":"58 °C falls in the step 55 °C < OAT ≤ 60 °C, which limits use to 1 h. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 h","No limitation","2 h","0.5 h"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0069","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la limitación de ventilación de aviónica en tierra es FALSA?","keys":["60","64","oat"],"answer":"FALSA: en el escalón 60 °C < OAT ≤ 64 °C el límite es 0.5 h, no 2 h. Las 2 h corresponden al escalón 49 °C < OAT ≤ 55 °C. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Con 60 °C < OAT ≤ 64 °C el límite es 2 h","Con OAT ≤ 49 °C no hay limitación de tiempo","Con 49 °C < OAT ≤ 55 °C el límite es 2 h","Con 55 °C < OAT ≤ 60 °C el límite es 1 h"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements about the ground avionics ventilation limitation is FALSE?","keys":["60","64","oat"],"answer":"FALSE: in the step 60 °C < OAT ≤ 64 °C the limit is 0.5 h, not 2 h. The 2 h correspond to the step 49 °C < OAT ≤ 55 °C. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["With 60 °C < OAT ≤ 64 °C the limit is 2 h","With OAT ≤ 49 °C there is no time limitation","With 49 °C < OAT ≤ 55 °C the limit is 2 h","With 55 °C < OAT ≤ 60 °C the limit is 1 h"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0070","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la máxima presión diferencial positiva publicada?","keys":["9.0","psi","maxima"],"answer":"La máxima presión diferencial positiva es 9.0 PSI, con una tolerancia de ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["9.0 PSI","8.0 PSI","8.6 PSI","1.0 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"What is the published maximum positive differential pressure?","keys":["9.0","psi","differential"],"answer":"The maximum positive differential pressure is 9.0 PSI, with a tolerance of ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["9.0 PSI","8.0 PSI","8.6 PSI","1.0 PSI"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0071","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es el tarado (setting) de la safety relief valve?","keys":["8.6","psi","tarado"],"answer":"El tarado de la safety relief valve es 8.6 PSI, por debajo de la máxima presión diferencial positiva de 9.0 PSI. Su tolerancia es ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["8.6 PSI","-1.0 PSI","9.0 PSI","9.1 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"What is the setting of the safety relief valve?","keys":["8.6","psi","setting"],"answer":"The setting of the safety relief valve is 8.6 PSI, below the maximum positive differential pressure of 9.0 PSI. Its tolerance is ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 54 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["8.6 PSI","-1.0 PSI","9.0 PSI","9.1 PSI"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0072","es":{"q":"Sobre las tolerancias publicadas en la sección CABIN PRESSURE, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["350","ft","tolerancia"],"answer":"FALSA: la tolerancia de la máxima Δp y del tarado de la safety valve es ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). Los ± 350 ft son la tolerancia de un parámetro distinto de la misma sección: el aviso de altitud de cabina (Cab Alt Warning = 9 550 ft ± 350 ft). Son dos tolerancias que conviven en la misma página y no deben cruzarse: una es de presión y la otra de altitud. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La tolerancia de la máxima presión diferencial y del tarado de la safety valve es de ± 350 ft","La máxima presión diferencial positiva es 9.0 PSI","La tolerancia de la máxima presión diferencial y del tarado de la safety valve es de ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI)","La máxima presión diferencial negativa es -1.0 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the tolerances published in the CABIN PRESSURE section, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["350","ft","tolerance"],"answer":"FALSE: the tolerance of the maximum Δp and of the safety valve setting is ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI). The ± 350 ft is the tolerance of a different parameter in the same section: the cabin altitude warning (Cab Alt Warning = 9 550 ft ± 350 ft). These are two tolerances that coexist on the same page and must not be crossed: one is of pressure and the other of altitude. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The tolerance of the maximum differential pressure and of the safety valve setting is ± 350 ft","The maximum positive differential pressure is 9.0 PSI","The tolerance of the maximum differential pressure and of the safety valve setting is ± 7 hPa (0.1 PSI)","The maximum negative differential pressure is -1.0 PSI"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0073","es":{"q":"¿A qué altitud de cabina se dispara el aviso de altitud de cabina (Cab Alt Warning), y con qué tolerancia?","keys":["9550","350","ft"],"answer":"El Cab Alt Warning se dispara a 9 550 ft, con una tolerancia de ± 350 ft, según el gráfico de CABIN PRESSURE. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["9 550 ft (± 350 ft)","8 000 ft (± 350 ft)","10 000 ft (± 350 ft)","14 000 ft (± 350 ft)"]},"en":{"q":"At what cabin altitude does the cabin altitude warning (Cab Alt Warning) trigger, and with what tolerance?","keys":["9550","350","ft"],"answer":"The Cab Alt Warning triggers at 9 550 ft, with a tolerance of ± 350 ft, according to the CABIN PRESSURE graph. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["9 550 ft (± 350 ft)","8 000 ft (± 350 ft)","10 000 ft (± 350 ft)","14 000 ft (± 350 ft)"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0074","es":{"q":"Sobre las altitudes de cabina publicadas en el gráfico de CABIN PRESSURE, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["15000","ft","maxima"],"answer":"FALSA: la máxima altitud de cabina seleccionable es 14 000 ft. Los 15 000 ft son el Outflow Valve Closure, un parámetro distinto. El gráfico apila tres valores cercanos que conviene no mezclar: 8 000 ft (máxima normal), 14 000 ft (máxima seleccionable) y 15 000 ft (cierre de la outflow valve). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La máxima altitud de cabina seleccionable (Max Cabin Alt Selection) es 15 000 ft","La máxima altitud de cabina normal (Max Norm Cab Alt) es 8 000 ft","El cierre de la outflow valve (Outflow Valve Closure) se produce a 15 000 ft","El aviso de altitud de cabina se dispara a 9 550 ft (± 350 ft)"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the cabin altitudes published in the CABIN PRESSURE graph, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["15000","ft","selection"],"answer":"FALSE: the maximum selectable cabin altitude is 14 000 ft. The 15 000 ft is the Outflow Valve Closure, a different parameter. The graph stacks three close values that should not be mixed up: 8 000 ft (max normal), 14 000 ft (max selectable) and 15 000 ft (outflow valve closure). (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The maximum selectable cabin altitude (Max Cabin Alt Selection) is 15 000 ft","The maximum normal cabin altitude (Max Norm Cab Alt) is 8 000 ft","The outflow valve closure (Outflow Valve Closure) occurs at 15 000 ft","The cabin altitude warning triggers at 9 550 ft (± 350 ft)"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0075","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la Max Operating Alt que figura en el gráfico de CABIN PRESSURE?","keys":["39800","ft","operating"],"answer":"El gráfico de CABIN PRESSURE publica una Max Operating Alt de 39 800 ft. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["39 800 ft","39 000 ft","40 000 ft","41 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"What is the Max Operating Alt shown in the CABIN PRESSURE graph?","keys":["39800","ft","operating"],"answer":"The CABIN PRESSURE graph publishes a Max Operating Alt of 39 800 ft. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["39 800 ft","39 000 ft","40 000 ft","41 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"AC","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0076","es":{"q":"En escala, con una LP Air Conditioning Unit conectada al avión, el ambiente de cabina no acaba de refrescar y se plantea arrancar además los packs. ¿Qué establece el FCOM?","keys":["tripulacion","usar","aire"],"answer":"La tripulación no debe usar aire acondicionado procedente de los packs y de la LP Air Conditioning Unit al mismo tiempo, para evitar efectos adversos sobre el sistema de aire acondicionado. Hay que elegir una de las dos fuentes. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La tripulación no debe usar aire acondicionado de los packs y de la LP Air Conditioning Unit al mismo tiempo","Se permite, siempre que no se exceda 20 min","Se permite con un solo pack en servicio","Se permite si la OAT es superior a 49 °C"]},"en":{"q":"During a stopover, with an LP Air Conditioning Unit connected to the aircraft, the cabin does not quite cool down and starting the packs as well is considered. What does the FCOM state?","keys":["crew","packs","conditioning"],"answer":"The crew must not use air conditioning from the packs and from the LP Air Conditioning Unit at the same time, to avoid adverse effects on the air conditioning system. One of the two sources must be selected. (FCOM LIM-AIR · p. 55 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The crew must not use air conditioning from the packs and from the LP Air Conditioning Unit at the same time","It is permitted, provided 20 min is not exceeded","It is permitted with a single pack in service","It is permitted if the OAT is above 49 °C"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0077","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático en el despegue?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"El FCOM fija para el despegue: '100 ft AGL and at least 5 s after liftoff'. Son dos condiciones acumulativas: altura Y tiempo transcurrido desde el despegue. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["100 ft AGL y al menos 5 s después del liftoff","100 ft AGL, sin ninguna condición de tiempo","160 ft AGL y al menos 5 s después del liftoff","250 ft AGL y al menos 5 s después del liftoff"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use on takeoff?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"The FCOM sets for takeoff: '100 ft AGL and at least 5 s after liftoff'. These are two cumulative conditions: height AND time elapsed since liftoff. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["100 ft AGL and at least 5 s after liftoff","100 ft AGL, with no time condition","160 ft AGL and at least 5 s after liftoff","250 ft AGL and at least 5 s after liftoff"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0078","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) despegas y, 3 s después del liftoff, pasas 120 ft AGL. ¿Puedes acoplar el piloto automático?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"El FCOM exige en el despegue 100 ft AGL Y al menos 5 s después del liftoff. Se cumple la altura pero no el tiempo, así que todavía no puede acoplarse el AP. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["No: aunque estás por encima de 100 ft AGL, aún no han transcurrido los 5 s mínimos desde el liftoff","Sí: ya has superado los 100 ft AGL, que es la única condición","Sí, siempre que la FMA muestre CAT1","No: el mínimo de uso del AP en el despegue es 250 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you take off and, 3 s after liftoff, you pass 120 ft AGL. Can you engage the autopilot?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"The FCOM requires on takeoff 100 ft AGL AND at least 5 s after liftoff. The height is met but not the time, so the AP cannot yet be engaged. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["No: although you are above 100 ft AGL, the minimum 5 s since liftoff have not yet elapsed","Yes: you have already passed 100 ft AGL, which is the only condition","Yes, provided the FMA shows CAT1","No: the minimum for AP use on takeoff is 250 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0079","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), respecto al mínimo de uso del piloto automático en el despegue, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"El FCOM redacta el mínimo del despegue como '100 ft AGL AND at least 5 s after liftoff': las dos condiciones son acumulativas, no alternativas. Hay que cumplir ambas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["Basta con que se cumpla una de las dos condiciones: 100 ft AGL o 5 s tras el liftoff","Deben alcanzarse 100 ft AGL","Deben haber transcurrido al menos 5 s desde el liftoff","Alcanzar 100 ft AGL antes de que transcurran los 5 s no habilita el acoplamiento del AP"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), regarding the minimum for autopilot use on takeoff, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["100","5","ft"],"answer":"The FCOM words the takeoff minimum as '100 ft AGL AND at least 5 s after liftoff': the two conditions are cumulative, not alternative. Both must be met. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["It is enough for one of the two conditions to be met: 100 ft AGL or 5 s after liftoff","100 ft AGL must be reached","At least 5 s must have elapsed since liftoff","Reaching 100 ft AGL before the 5 s have elapsed does not enable AP engagement"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0080","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático en aproximación con modo F-G/S?","keys":["200","ft","f-g/s"],"answer":"La tabla del FCOM asigna 200 ft AGL a la aproximación con modo F-G/S, frente a los 250 ft AGL de la aproximación con FINAL APP, V/S o FPA. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","500 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use on approach with F-G/S mode?","keys":["200","ft","f-g/s"],"answer":"The FCOM table assigns 200 ft AGL to the approach with F-G/S mode, versus the 250 ft AGL of the approach with FINAL APP, V/S or FPA. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","500 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0081","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) vuelas una aproximación con el modo FINAL APP acoplado. ¿Hasta qué altura mínima puedes mantener el piloto automático?","keys":["250","ft","final app"],"answer":"La tabla del FCOM agrupa FINAL APP, V/S y FPA con un mínimo de 250 ft AGL, superior a los 200 ft AGL del modo F-G/S. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["250 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","500 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you fly an approach with FINAL APP mode engaged. Down to what minimum height can you keep the autopilot?","keys":["250","ft","final app"],"answer":"The FCOM table groups FINAL APP, V/S and FPA with a minimum of 250 ft AGL, higher than the 200 ft AGL of F-G/S mode. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 23 JUL 18)","opts":["250 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","500 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0082","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático en una aproximación en circuito (circling approach)?","keys":["500","600","ft"],"answer":"El FCOM fija para el circling: '500 ft AGL for aircraft category C (600 ft AGL for aircraft category D)'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 09 JUN 17)","opts":["500 ft AGL para aeronaves de categoría C (600 ft AGL para categoría D)","600 ft AGL para aeronaves de categoría C (500 ft AGL para categoría D)","250 ft AGL para aeronaves de categoría C (300 ft AGL para categoría D)","500 ft AGL, con independencia de la categoría de la aeronave"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use on a circling approach?","keys":["500","600","ft"],"answer":"The FCOM sets for circling: '500 ft AGL for aircraft category C (600 ft AGL for aircraft category D)'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 09 JUN 17)","opts":["500 ft AGL for category C aircraft (600 ft AGL for category D)","600 ft AGL for category C aircraft (500 ft AGL for category D)","250 ft AGL for category C aircraft (300 ft AGL for category D)","500 ft AGL, regardless of aircraft category"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0083","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) vas a volar un circling que, por la velocidad de maniobra prevista, debe realizarse con criterios de categoría D. ¿Cuál es el mínimo de uso del piloto automático?","keys":["600","ft","a320"],"answer":"El FCOM fija 500 ft AGL para categoría C y 600 ft AGL para categoría D. Al aplicar criterios de categoría D, el mínimo es 600 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 09 JUN 17)","opts":["600 ft AGL","500 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","160 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you are going to fly a circling that, due to the expected maneuvering speed, must be flown with category D criteria. What is the minimum for autopilot use?","keys":["600","ft","a320"],"answer":"The FCOM sets 500 ft AGL for category C and 600 ft AGL for category D. Applying category D criteria, the minimum is 600 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 09 JUN 17)","opts":["600 ft AGL","500 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","160 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0084","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático en una aproximación ILS/MLS cuando la FMA muestra CAT1?","keys":["160","ft","ils"],"answer":"El FCOM fija 160 ft AGL para la aproximación ILS/MLS cuando en la FMA se muestra CAT1. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["160 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","0 ft AGL si se realiza autoland"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use on an ILS/MLS approach when the FMA shows CAT1?","keys":["160","ft","ils"],"answer":"The FCOM sets 160 ft AGL for the ILS/MLS approach when CAT1 is shown on the FMA. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["160 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","0 ft AGL if autoland is performed"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0085","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) vuelas un ILS con CAT3 DUAL mostrado en la FMA y vas a realizar un autoland. ¿Hasta qué altura puedes mantener el piloto automático?","keys":["0","ft","cat3 dual"],"answer":"El FCOM fija 0 ft AGL si autoland para la aproximación ILS/MLS cuando en la FMA se muestra CAT2, CAT3 SINGLE o CAT3 DUAL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["Hasta 0 ft AGL, por realizarse autoland","Hasta 160 ft AGL","Hasta 100 ft AGL","Hasta 200 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you fly an ILS with CAT3 DUAL shown on the FMA and you are going to perform an autoland. Down to what height can you keep the autopilot?","keys":["0","ft","cat3 dual"],"answer":"The FCOM sets 0 ft AGL if autoland for the ILS/MLS approach when CAT2, CAT3 SINGLE or CAT3 DUAL is shown on the FMA. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["Down to 0 ft AGL, because an autoland is performed","Down to 160 ft AGL","Down to 100 ft AGL","Down to 200 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0086","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), todas las siguientes situaciones tienen un mínimo de uso del piloto automático de 160 ft AGL, EXCEPTO:","keys":["gls","aproximacion","auto"],"answer":"La GLS con AUTO LAND mostrado en la FMA tiene un mínimo de 0 ft AGL si se realiza autoland. Las otras tres (ILS/MLS con CAT1, GLS con CAT1 y LPV con APPR1) comparten el mínimo de 160 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["Aproximación GLS con AUTO LAND mostrado en la FMA","Aproximación ILS/MLS con CAT1 mostrado en la FMA","Aproximación GLS con CAT1 mostrado en la FMA","Aproximación LPV (con SLS) con APPR1 mostrado en la FMA"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), all the following situations have a minimum for autopilot use of 160 ft AGL, EXCEPT:","keys":["gls","autoland","approach"],"answer":"The GLS with AUTO LAND shown on the FMA has a minimum of 0 ft AGL if autoland is performed. The other three (ILS/MLS with CAT1, GLS with CAT1 and LPV with APPR1) share the minimum of 160 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 06 SEP 22)","opts":["GLS approach with AUTO LAND shown on the FMA","ILS/MLS approach with CAT1 shown on the FMA","GLS approach with CAT1 shown on the FMA","LPV approach (with SLS) with APPR1 shown on the FMA"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0087","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el mínimo de uso del piloto automático en una aproximación PAR (Precision Approach Radar) y con qué modos está autorizada?","keys":["250","ft","par"],"answer":"El FCOM fija 250 ft AGL para la aproximación PAR y su nota precisa que el uso del AP y/o FD está autorizado en PAR con HDG V/S o TRK FPA. Añade que las PAR pueden estar sujetas a aprobación operacional. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["250 ft AGL, con HDG V/S o TRK FPA","160 ft AGL, con FINAL APP","250 ft AGL, pero solo con FD; el AP no está autorizado en PAR","200 ft AGL, con HDG V/S o TRK FPA"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum for autopilot use on a PAR (Precision Approach Radar) approach and with which modes is it authorized?","keys":["250","ft","par"],"answer":"The FCOM sets 250 ft AGL for the PAR approach and its note specifies that the use of AP and/or FD is authorized on PAR with HDG V/S or TRK FPA. It adds that PAR approaches may be subject to operational approval. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["250 ft AGL, with HDG V/S or TRK FPA","160 ft AGL, with FINAL APP","250 ft AGL, but only with FD; the AP is not authorized on PAR","200 ft AGL, with HDG V/S or TRK FPA"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0088","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático después de un go-around manual?","keys":["100","ft","a320"],"answer":"El FCOM fija 100 ft AGL como mínimo de uso del AP después de un go-around manual. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["100 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use after a manual go-around?","keys":["100","ft","a320"],"answer":"The FCOM sets 100 ft AGL as the minimum for AP use after a manual go-around. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 62 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["100 ft AGL","160 ft AGL","200 ft AGL","250 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0089","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el valor mínimo para el uso del piloto automático en el resto de fases de vuelo (in all other phases)?","keys":["500","ft","a320"],"answer":"La tabla del FCOM cierra con 'In all other phases — 500 ft AGL' para este avión. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["500 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","900 ft AGL","100 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the minimum value for autopilot use in all other phases of flight?","keys":["500","ft","a320"],"answer":"The FCOM table closes with 'In all other phases — 500 ft AGL' for this aircraft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["500 ft AGL","250 ft AGL","900 ft AGL","100 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0090","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) vuelas una aproximación con MDA/MDH de 700 ft AGL y quieres usar el AP en modo OP DES con la altitud de la FCU seleccionada a 500 ft AGL. ¿Es admisible?","keys":["500","700","ft","op des"],"answer":"El FCOM permite el AP o FD en OP DES o DES en aproximación solo si la altitud seleccionada en la FCU está a o por encima de la MAYOR de las dos: MDA/MDH o 500 ft AGL. Con MDA/MDH de 700 ft AGL, la mayor es 700 ft AGL, así que 500 ft AGL en la FCU no es admisible. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["No: la altitud seleccionada en la FCU debe estar a o por encima de la mayor de las dos, MDA/MDH o 500 ft AGL; aquí, 700 ft AGL","Sí: 500 ft AGL es el mínimo que fija el FCOM y se cumple","Sí, siempre que se desconecte el piloto automático al alcanzar la MDA/MDH","No: el uso del AP o FD en modo OP DES o DES está prohibido en aproximación"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you fly an approach with an MDA/MDH of 700 ft AGL and you want to use the AP in OP DES mode with the FCU altitude selected at 500 ft AGL. Is it admissible?","keys":["500","700","ft","op des"],"answer":"The FCOM allows the AP or FD in OP DES or DES on approach only if the altitude selected on the FCU is at or above the HIGHER of the two: MDA/MDH or 500 ft AGL. With an MDA/MDH of 700 ft AGL, the higher is 700 ft AGL, so 500 ft AGL on the FCU is not admissible. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["No: the altitude selected on the FCU must be at or above the higher of the two, MDA/MDH or 500 ft AGL; here, 700 ft AGL","Yes: 500 ft AGL is the minimum set by the FCOM and it is met","Yes, provided the autopilot is disconnected on reaching the MDA/MDH","No: the use of AP or FD in OP DES or DES mode is prohibited on approach"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0091","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), sobre el uso del AP o FD en modo OP DES o DES en aproximación, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["500","ft","op des"],"answer":"El FCOM exige que la altitud seleccionada en la FCU esté a o por encima de la MAYOR de las dos: MDA/MDH o 500 ft AGL. Quedarse por debajo de la MDA/MDH nunca es admisible, aunque se superen los 500 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["Basta con que la altitud seleccionada en la FCU esté a o por encima de 500 ft AGL, aunque quede por debajo de la MDA/MDH","El AP o el FD en OP DES o DES pueden usarse en aproximación","La altitud seleccionada en la FCU debe estar a o por encima de la mayor de las dos: MDA/MDH o 500 ft AGL","Si la MDA/MDH es inferior a 500 ft AGL, el valor que manda es 500 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), regarding the use of AP or FD in OP DES or DES mode on approach, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["500","ft","op des"],"answer":"The FCOM requires the altitude selected on the FCU to be at or above the HIGHER of the two: MDA/MDH or 500 ft AGL. Staying below the MDA/MDH is never admissible, even if 500 ft AGL is exceeded. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 63 · rev 06 JUL 17)","opts":["It is enough for the altitude selected on the FCU to be at or above 500 ft AGL, even if it is below the MDA/MDH","The AP or FD in OP DES or DES can be used on approach","The altitude selected on the FCU must be at or above the higher of the two: MDA/MDH or 500 ft AGL","If the MDA/MDH is below 500 ft AGL, the governing value is 500 ft AGL"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0092","es":{"q":"¿Para qué operaciones está certificada la navegación lateral y vertical del FMGS?","keys":["fmgs","despues","despegue"],"answer":"El FCOM certifica la navegación lateral y vertical del FMGS para: después del despegue, en ruta y área terminal; navegación en espacio aéreo RNAV/RNP; procedimientos de aproximación instrumental (excepto las finales ILS, LOC, LOC B/C, LDA, SDF, GLS, MLS y FLS); y procedimientos de aproximación frustrada. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["Después del despegue, en ruta y en área terminal, navegación en espacio aéreo RNAV/RNP, procedimientos de aproximación instrumental (con excepciones) y procedimientos de aproximación frustrada","Solo para navegación en ruta dentro de espacio aéreo RNAV/RNP","Después del despegue, en ruta y en área terminal, pero nunca para procedimientos de aproximación frustrada","Para todas las fases de vuelo, incluidas las finales ILS, LOC y GLS"]},"en":{"q":"For which operations is the lateral and vertical navigation of the FMGS certified?","keys":["fmgs","takeoff","approach"],"answer":"The FCOM certifies the lateral and vertical navigation of the FMGS for: after takeoff, en route and terminal area; navigation in RNAV/RNP airspace; instrument approach procedures (except ILS, LOC, LOC B/C, LDA, SDF, GLS, MLS and FLS final approaches); and missed approach procedures. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["After takeoff, en route and terminal area, navigation in RNAV/RNP airspace, instrument approach procedures (with exceptions) and missed approach procedures","Only for en route navigation within RNAV/RNP airspace","After takeoff, en route and terminal area, but never for missed approach procedures","For all phases of flight, including ILS, LOC and GLS final approaches"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0093","es":{"q":"La navegación lateral y vertical del FMGS está certificada para procedimientos de aproximación instrumental, EXCEPTO para determinadas aproximaciones finales. ¿Cuál de las siguientes NO está excluida de esa certificación?","keys":["fmgs","final","rnav"],"answer":"La lista de exclusiones del FCOM es: ILS, LOC, LOC B/C, LDA, SDF, GLS, MLS y FLS final approaches. La aproximación RNAV (GNSS) no figura en esa lista, por lo que queda cubierta por la certificación de navegación lateral y vertical del FMGS. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["La final RNAV (GNSS)","La final ILS","La final GLS","La final LOC B/C"]},"en":{"q":"The lateral and vertical navigation of the FMGS is certified for instrument approach procedures, EXCEPT for certain final approaches. Which of the following is NOT excluded from that certification?","keys":["fmgs","final","rnav"],"answer":"The FCOM exclusion list is: ILS, LOC, LOC B/C, LDA, SDF, GLS, MLS and FLS final approaches. The RNAV (GNSS) approach is not on that list, so it is covered by the FMGS lateral and vertical navigation certification. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["The RNAV (GNSS) final approach","The ILS final approach","The GLS final approach","The LOC B/C final approach"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0094","es":{"q":"Respecto a la aprobación del FMGS, ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["fmgs","aprobacion","exime"],"answer":"El FCOM establece expresamente que la separación con obstáculos Y la adherencia a las restricciones de espacio aéreo siguen siendo responsabilidad de la tripulación de vuelo. La aprobación del FMGS no exime de ninguna de las dos. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["La aprobación del FMGS exime a la tripulación de la adherencia a las restricciones de espacio aéreo","La aprobación del FMGS se basa en la asunción de que la base de datos de navegación está validada para el uso previsto","La separación con obstáculos sigue siendo responsabilidad de la tripulación de vuelo","Las predicciones de combustible y tiempo se proporcionan únicamente con carácter informativo (advisory)"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the FMGS approval, which of the following statements is FALSE?","keys":["fmgs","approval","crew"],"answer":"The FCOM expressly states that obstacle clearance AND adherence to airspace restrictions remain the responsibility of the flight crew. The FMGS approval does not relieve the crew of either. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["The FMGS approval relieves the crew of adherence to airspace restrictions","The FMGS approval is based on the assumption that the navigation database is validated for the intended use","Obstacle clearance remains the responsibility of the flight crew","Fuel and time predictions are provided for advisory purposes only"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0095","es":{"q":"Vas a volar un ILS cuya senda de planeo está fuera de servicio (G/S out). ¿Cómo está certificada la función FLS para esta aproximación?","keys":["fls","navegacion"],"answer":"El FCOM certifica el FLS para aproximaciones LOC, ILS (G/S out) o LOC B/C usando la navegación FMS para la navegación vertical, asociada a LOC o LOC B/C para la navegación lateral. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["El FLS usa navegación FMS para la navegación vertical, asociada al modo LOC para la navegación lateral","El FLS no está certificado para aproximaciones ILS de ningún tipo","El FLS proporciona la navegación lateral y la vertical de forma íntegra, sin necesidad del LOC","El FLS solo está certificado si se dispone de mínimos LPV publicados"]},"en":{"q":"You are going to fly an ILS whose glideslope is out of service (G/S out). How is the FLS function certified for this approach?","keys":["fls","loc","navigation"],"answer":"The FCOM certifies the FLS for LOC, ILS (G/S out) or LOC B/C approaches using FMS navigation for vertical navigation, associated with LOC or LOC B/C for lateral navigation. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["The FLS uses FMS navigation for vertical navigation, associated with the LOC mode for lateral navigation","The FLS is not certified for ILS approaches of any kind","The FLS provides lateral and vertical navigation in full, without the need for the LOC","The FLS is only certified if published LPV minima are available"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0096","es":{"q":"Según el FCOM, ¿de qué depende la precisión de navegación (navigation accuracy)?","keys":["irs","deriva","bien"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que la precisión de navegación depende de: la deriva de las IRS, o bien de una de las siguientes: la disponibilidad de radioayudas, o el tiempo transcurrido desde el último cálculo de posición por radioayudas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["De la deriva de las IRS, o bien de la disponibilidad de radioayudas o del tiempo transcurrido desde el último cálculo de posición por radioayudas","Exclusivamente de la deriva de las IRS","Únicamente de la disponibilidad de GPS PRIMARY","Del modo de guiado seleccionado y del peso del avión"]},"en":{"q":"According to the FCOM, what does the navigation accuracy depend on?","keys":["irs","drift","navaids"],"answer":"The FCOM states that navigation accuracy depends on: the drift of the IRS, or on one of the following: the availability of navaids, or the time elapsed since the last position computation by navaids. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["On the drift of the IRS, or on the availability of navaids or the time elapsed since the last position computation by navaids","Exclusively on the drift of the IRS","Only on the availability of GPS PRIMARY","On the selected guidance mode and the aircraft weight"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0097","es":{"q":"¿Para qué está certificada la función SLS?","keys":["sls","aproximaciones","rnav"],"answer":"El FCOM es explícito: 'The SLS function is certified for RNAV (GNSS) approach with LPV or LP minima'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["Para aproximaciones RNAV (GNSS) con mínimos LPV o LP","Para aproximaciones RNAV (GNSS) con mínimos LNAV o LNAV/VNAV","Para aproximaciones LOC, ILS (G/S out) o LOC B/C","Para aproximaciones VOR, VOR/DME, NDB y NDB/DME"]},"en":{"q":"What is the SLS function certified for?","keys":["sls","rnav","lpv"],"answer":"The FCOM is explicit: 'The SLS function is certified for RNAV (GNSS) approach with LPV or LP minima'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 64 · rev 12 MAY 22)","opts":["For RNAV (GNSS) approaches with LPV or LP minima","For RNAV (GNSS) approaches with LNAV or LNAV/VNAV minima","For LOC, ILS (G/S out) or LOC B/C approaches","For VOR, VOR/DME, NDB and NDB/DME approaches"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0098","es":{"q":"Vas a volar una aproximación basada en radioayudas con GPS PRIMARY disponible, pero el VOR de referencia está fuera de servicio por NOTAM. ¿Qué dice el FCOM?","keys":["gps primary","radioayuda","referencia"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que, si GPS PRIMARY está disponible, la radioayuda de referencia puede estar fuera de servicio, o el equipo de radio de a bordo puede estar inoperativo o no instalado, siempre que se obtenga una aprobación operacional. Si GPS PRIMARY no estuviera disponible, la radioayuda y su equipo deberían estar operativos, sintonizados y monitorizados durante la aproximación. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La radioayuda de referencia puede estar fuera de servicio, o el equipo de radio de a bordo inoperativo o no instalado, siempre que se obtenga una aprobación operacional","La aproximación no puede realizarse: la radioayuda de referencia debe estar siempre operativa","La radioayuda de referencia puede estar fuera de servicio siempre que se muestre HIGH accuracy en el MCDU","La aproximación solo puede volarse con FD, nunca con AP acoplado"]},"en":{"q":"You are going to fly a navaid-based approach with GPS PRIMARY available, but the reference VOR is out of service by NOTAM. What does the FCOM say?","keys":["gps primary","navaid","reference"],"answer":"The FCOM states that, if GPS PRIMARY is available, the reference navaid may be out of service, or the onboard radio equipment may be inoperative or not installed, provided an operational approval is obtained. If GPS PRIMARY were not available, the navaid and its equipment would have to be operative, tuned and monitored during the approach. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The reference navaid may be out of service, or the onboard radio equipment inoperative or not installed, provided an operational approval is obtained","The approach cannot be flown: the reference navaid must always be operative","The reference navaid may be out of service provided HIGH accuracy is shown on the MCDU","The approach can only be flown with FD, never with AP engaged"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0099","es":{"q":"Si se muestra GPS PRIMARY LOST en la ND y el MCDU, ¿bajo qué condición la precisión de navegación sigue siendo suficiente para operaciones RNP?","keys":["rnp","siempre","compruebe"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que si se muestra GPS PRIMARY LOST, la precisión de navegación sigue siendo suficiente para operaciones RNP siempre que el valor RNP sea comprobado o introducido en el MCDU y se muestre HIGH ACCURACY. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 04 MAY 18)","opts":["Siempre que se compruebe o se introduzca el valor RNP en el MCDU y se muestre HIGH ACCURACY","Siempre, sin condición adicional, mientras las IRS estén alineadas","Siempre que se compruebe o se introduzca el valor RNP en el MCDU, con independencia de la precisión mostrada","Nunca: la pérdida de GPS PRIMARY prohíbe cualquier operación RNP"]},"en":{"q":"If GPS PRIMARY LOST is displayed on the ND and the MCDU, under what condition does navigation accuracy remain sufficient for RNP operations?","keys":["rnp","checked","accuracy"],"answer":"The FCOM states that if GPS PRIMARY LOST is displayed, navigation accuracy remains sufficient for RNP operations provided that the RNP value is checked or entered in the MCDU and HIGH ACCURACY is displayed. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 04 MAY 18)","opts":["Provided that the RNP value is checked or entered in the MCDU and HIGH ACCURACY is displayed","Always, with no additional condition, as long as the IRS are aligned","Provided that the RNP value is checked or entered in the MCDU, regardless of the accuracy displayed","Never: loss of GPS PRIMARY prohibits any RNP operation"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0100","es":{"q":"Con GPS PRIMARY LOST mostrado, introduces el valor RNP en el MCDU pero la página NO muestra HIGH ACCURACY. ¿Qué implica esto según las limitaciones del FCOM?","keys":["rnp","cumple","condicion"],"answer":"El FCOM exige las DOS condiciones de forma conjunta: valor RNP comprobado o introducido en el MCDU Y HIGH ACCURACY mostrado. Si falta la indicación HIGH ACCURACY, la condición no se cumple. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 04 MAY 18)","opts":["No se cumple la condición del FCOM, por lo que no puede darse por suficiente la precisión de navegación para operaciones RNP","Nada: basta con haber introducido el valor RNP en el MCDU","La precisión es suficiente si se mantiene el modo NAV con AP acoplado","La precisión es suficiente si el tiempo transcurrido desde el último cálculo de posición por radioayudas es inferior a 30 min"]},"en":{"q":"With GPS PRIMARY LOST displayed, you enter the RNP value in the MCDU but the page does NOT display HIGH ACCURACY. What does this imply according to the FCOM limitations?","keys":["rnp","condition","not"],"answer":"The FCOM requires BOTH conditions jointly: RNP value checked or entered in the MCDU AND HIGH ACCURACY displayed. If the HIGH ACCURACY indication is missing, the condition is not met. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 04 MAY 18)","opts":["The FCOM condition is not met, so navigation accuracy cannot be considered sufficient for RNP operations","Nothing: having entered the RNP value in the MCDU is enough","Accuracy is sufficient if NAV mode is maintained with the AP engaged","Accuracy is sufficient if the time elapsed since the last radio-aid position update is less than 30 min"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0101","es":{"q":"¿Bajo qué condiciones puede usarse el modo NAV después del despegue?","keys":["gps primary","siempre","primary"],"answer":"El FCOM permite el uso del modo NAV después del despegue siempre que: GPS PRIMARY esté disponible, o bien la tripulación haya comprobado el takeoff updating del FMGS. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Siempre que GPS PRIMARY esté disponible, o que la tripulación haya comprobado el takeoff updating del FMGS","Siempre que se muestre HIGH ACCURACY en el MCDU","Solo si GPS PRIMARY está disponible; no hay alternativa","Siempre que la navegación FMS se contraste con datos crudos (raw data) de radioayudas"]},"en":{"q":"Under what conditions may NAV mode be used after takeoff?","keys":["gps primary","takeoff","updating"],"answer":"The FCOM allows the use of NAV mode after takeoff provided that: GPS PRIMARY is available, or the flight crew has checked the FMGS takeoff updating. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Provided that GPS PRIMARY is available, or that the flight crew has checked the FMGS takeoff updating","Provided that HIGH ACCURACY is displayed on the MCDU","Only if GPS PRIMARY is available; there is no alternative","Provided that FMS navigation is cross-checked against radio-aid raw data"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0102","es":{"q":"¿Bajo qué condiciones puede usarse el modo NAV en área terminal?","keys":["rnp","primary","disponible"],"answer":"El FCOM admite tres condiciones alternativas para usar el NAV en área terminal: GPS PRIMARY disponible; o RNP apropiado comprobado o introducido en el MCDU con HIGH accuracy mostrado; o navegación FMS contrastada con datos crudos de radioayudas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Si GPS PRIMARY está disponible, o si se comprueba/introduce el RNP apropiado en el MCDU y se muestra HIGH accuracy, o si la navegación FMS se contrasta con datos crudos de radioayudas","Solo si GPS PRIMARY está disponible","Si GPS PRIMARY está disponible, o si la tripulación ha comprobado el takeoff updating del FMGS","En cualquier caso: el FCOM no impone condiciones al uso del NAV en área terminal"]},"en":{"q":"Under what conditions may NAV mode be used in the terminal area?","keys":["rnp","primary","available"],"answer":"The FCOM accepts three alternative conditions for using NAV in the terminal area: GPS PRIMARY available; or appropriate RNP checked or entered in the MCDU with HIGH accuracy displayed; or FMS navigation cross-checked against radio-aid raw data. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["If GPS PRIMARY is available, or if the appropriate RNP is checked/entered in the MCDU and HIGH accuracy is displayed, or if FMS navigation is cross-checked against radio-aid raw data","Only if GPS PRIMARY is available","If GPS PRIMARY is available, or if the flight crew has checked the FMGS takeoff updating","In any case: the FCOM imposes no conditions on the use of NAV in the terminal area"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0103","es":{"q":"Todas las siguientes condiciones permiten el uso del modo NAV en área terminal, EXCEPTO:","keys":["gps primary","tripulacion","comprobado"],"answer":"La comprobación del takeoff updating del FMGS es condición del uso del NAV después del despegue. En área terminal el FCOM solo admite: GPS PRIMARY disponible, RNP comprobado/introducido con HIGH accuracy, o navegación FMS contrastada con datos crudos de radioayudas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La tripulación ha comprobado el takeoff updating del FMGS","GPS PRIMARY está disponible","El RNP apropiado se comprueba o introduce en el MCDU y se muestra HIGH accuracy","La navegación FMS se contrasta con datos crudos (raw data) de radioayudas"]},"en":{"q":"All of the following conditions allow the use of NAV mode in the terminal area, EXCEPT:","keys":["gps primary","takeoff","updating"],"answer":"Checking the FMGS takeoff updating is a condition for using NAV after takeoff. In the terminal area the FCOM only accepts: GPS PRIMARY available, RNP checked/entered with HIGH accuracy, or FMS navigation cross-checked against radio-aid raw data. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The flight crew has checked the FMGS takeoff updating","GPS PRIMARY is available","The appropriate RNP is checked or entered in the MCDU and HIGH accuracy is displayed","FMS navigation is cross-checked against radio-aid raw data"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0104","es":{"q":"Vuelas una STAR en modo NAV. GPS PRIMARY no está disponible y el MCDU no muestra HIGH accuracy con el RNP introducido. ¿Qué te queda para poder mantener el modo NAV en área terminal?","keys":["contrastar","navegacion","datos"],"answer":"La tercera condición alternativa del FCOM para el uso del NAV en área terminal es que la navegación FMS se contraste con datos crudos de radioayudas. Al fallar las otras dos, es la que queda disponible. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Contrastar la navegación FMS con los datos crudos (raw data) de las radioayudas","Nada: debes desconectar el NAV y volar en HDG/TRK selectado","Comprobar el takeoff updating del FMGS realizado en la salida","Mantener el NAV mientras la deriva de las IRS se mantenga por debajo del RNP requerido"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying a STAR in NAV mode. GPS PRIMARY is not available and the MCDU does not display HIGH accuracy with the RNP entered. What is left to allow you to keep NAV mode in the terminal area?","keys":["cross-check","raw data","fms"],"answer":"The third alternative FCOM condition for using NAV in the terminal area is that FMS navigation be cross-checked against radio-aid raw data. With the other two failed, it is the one remaining available. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 66 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Cross-check FMS navigation against the radio-aid raw data","Nothing: you must disengage NAV and fly in selected HDG/TRK","Check the FMGS takeoff updating performed on departure","Keep NAV as long as the IRS drift stays below the required RNP"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0105","es":{"q":"¿Qué condición exige el FCOM para realizar una aproximación RNAV (GNSS)?","keys":["gps primary","primary","disponible"],"answer":"El FCOM es directo: 'An RNAV(GNSS) approach may be performed provided that GPS PRIMARY is available'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Que GPS PRIMARY esté disponible","Que se obtenga una aprobación operacional específica","Que la cobertura de radioayudas soporte el valor RNP","Que se vuele necesariamente en modo FINAL APP con AP acoplado"]},"en":{"q":"What condition does the FCOM require to perform an RNAV (GNSS) approach?","keys":["gps primary","available","approach"],"answer":"The FCOM is direct: 'An RNAV(GNSS) approach may be performed provided that GPS PRIMARY is available'. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["That GPS PRIMARY is available","That a specific operational approval is obtained","That radio-aid coverage supports the RNP value","That it is necessarily flown in FINAL APP mode with the AP engaged"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0106","es":{"q":"Te ofrecen una RNAV(RNP) y GPS PRIMARY no está disponible. ¿Qué debe cumplirse para poder realizarla?","keys":["gps primary","cobertura","radioayudas"],"answer":"El FCOM permite realizar una RNAV(RNP) sin GPS PRIMARY únicamente si la cobertura de radioayudas soporta el valor RNP, se muestra HIGH accuracy en el MCDU con el RNP especificado y se obtiene una aprobación operacional. Las tres condiciones son acumulativas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Que la cobertura de radioayudas soporte el valor RNP, que se muestre HIGH accuracy en el MCDU con el RNP especificado, y que se obtenga una aprobación operacional","Nada: una RNAV(RNP) nunca puede volarse sin GPS PRIMARY","Basta con que se muestre HIGH accuracy en el MCDU","Que la radioayuda de referencia esté operativa, sintonizada y monitorizada durante la aproximación"]},"en":{"q":"You are offered an RNAV(RNP) and GPS PRIMARY is not available. What must be met to be able to perform it?","keys":["gps primary","coverage","approval"],"answer":"The FCOM allows an RNAV(RNP) to be performed without GPS PRIMARY only if radio-aid coverage supports the RNP value, HIGH accuracy is displayed on the MCDU with the specified RNP, and an operational approval is obtained. The three conditions are cumulative. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["That radio-aid coverage supports the RNP value, that HIGH accuracy is displayed on the MCDU with the specified RNP, and that an operational approval is obtained","Nothing: an RNAV(RNP) can never be flown without GPS PRIMARY","It is enough that HIGH accuracy is displayed on the MCDU","That the reference radio aid is operative, tuned and monitored during the approach"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0107","es":{"q":"Volando una aproximación basada en radioayudas con el FLS, ¿qué diferencia hay entre que la FMA muestre la capacidad F-APP o F-APP + RAW?","keys":["fls","radioayudas","referencia"],"answer":"El FCOM distingue: con F-APP mostrado, las radioayudas de referencia pueden estar fuera de servicio, o el equipo de radio de a bordo inoperativo o no instalado, con aprobación operacional. Con F-APP + RAW mostrado, las radioayudas de referencia y el equipo correspondiente deben estar operativos, sintonizados y monitorizados durante la aproximación. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Con F-APP las radioayudas de referencia pueden estar fuera de servicio (con aprobación operacional); con F-APP + RAW deben estar operativas, sintonizadas y monitorizadas durante la aproximación","Con F-APP + RAW las radioayudas pueden estar fuera de servicio; con F-APP deben estar operativas y monitorizadas","No hay diferencia operativa: ambas capacidades exigen radioayudas operativas y monitorizadas","Con F-APP la aproximación solo puede volarse con FD; con F-APP + RAW puede volarse con AP acoplado"]},"en":{"q":"Flying a radio-aid-based approach with the FLS, what is the difference between the FMA displaying the F-APP capability or F-APP + RAW?","keys":["fls","raw","monitored"],"answer":"The FCOM distinguishes: with F-APP displayed, the reference radio aids may be out of service, or the associated on-board radio equipment inoperative or not installed, with operational approval. With F-APP + RAW displayed, the reference radio aids and the corresponding equipment must be operative, tuned and monitored during the approach. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["With F-APP the reference radio aids may be out of service (with operational approval); with F-APP + RAW they must be operative, tuned and monitored during the approach","With F-APP + RAW the radio aids may be out of service; with F-APP they must be operative and monitored","There is no operational difference: both capabilities require operative and monitored radio aids","With F-APP the approach may only be flown with FD; with F-APP + RAW it may be flown with the AP engaged"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0108","es":{"q":"Vuelas un ILS con G/S fuera de servicio usando el modo lateral LOC y el modo F-G/S del FLS. La FMA muestra la capacidad F-APP (sin RAW). ¿Qué exige el FCOM sobre las radioayudas usadas para validar la senda vertical?","keys":["fls","estar","sintonizadas"],"answer":"Con F-APP mostrado, el FCOM exige que las radioayudas de referencia usadas para la validación de la senda vertical estén sintonizadas y comprobadas en el final descent point. La monitorización durante la aproximación solo se añade cuando la capacidad mostrada es F-APP + RAW. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["Deben estar sintonizadas y comprobadas en el final descent point","Nada: con F-APP no se requiere ninguna acción sobre las radioayudas","Deben estar sintonizadas, comprobadas en el final descent point y monitorizadas durante toda la aproximación","Deben estar sintonizadas antes del inicio de la aproximación inicial y monitorizadas hasta el aterrizaje"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying an ILS with G/S out of service using the LOC lateral mode and the FLS F-G/S mode. The FMA displays the F-APP capability (without RAW). What does the FCOM require regarding the radio aids used to validate the vertical path?","keys":["fls","tuned","checked"],"answer":"With F-APP displayed, the FCOM requires the reference radio aids used for vertical-path validation to be tuned and checked at the final descent point. Monitoring during the approach is only added when the displayed capability is F-APP + RAW. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["They must be tuned and checked at the final descent point","Nothing: with F-APP no action on the radio aids is required","They must be tuned, checked at the final descent point and monitored throughout the approach","They must be tuned before the start of the initial approach and monitored until landing"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0109","es":{"q":"¿Qué capacidad debe mostrarse en la FMA para volar con el FLS una aproximación RNAV (GNSS) con mínimo LNAV o con mínimo LNAV/VNAV?","keys":["fls","ambos","casos"],"answer":"El FCOM exige la capacidad F-APP mostrada en la FMA tanto para la RNAV (GNSS) con mínimo LNAV como para la RNAV (GNSS) con mínimo LNAV/VNAV voladas con el FLS. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["F-APP en ambos casos","F-APP + RAW en ambos casos","F-APP para el mínimo LNAV y F-APP + RAW para el mínimo LNAV/VNAV","APPR1 en ambos casos"]},"en":{"q":"What capability must be displayed on the FMA to fly with the FLS an RNAV (GNSS) approach to LNAV minima or to LNAV/VNAV minima?","keys":["fls","f-app","both"],"answer":"The FCOM requires the F-APP capability displayed on the FMA both for the RNAV (GNSS) to LNAV minima and for the RNAV (GNSS) to LNAV/VNAV minima flown with the FLS. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 67 · rev 13 MAY 25)","opts":["F-APP in both cases","F-APP + RAW in both cases","F-APP for the LNAV minima and F-APP + RAW for the LNAV/VNAV minima","APPR1 in both cases"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0110","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), para volar una RNAV (GNSS) o una aproximación basada en VOR/NDB en modo lateral gestionado (o lateral y vertical gestionado), ¿qué debe cumplir la aproximación almacenada en la base de datos de navegación?","keys":["76","200","ed76/do200a"],"answer":"El FCOM exige que la aproximación almacenada sea 'either' producida por un proveedor aprobado conforme a ED76/DO200A o DAT Type 2, 'or' validada y aprobada por el operador. Es una condición alternativa. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 68 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["Debe estar producida por un proveedor aprobado conforme a ED76/DO200A o DAT Type 2, O BIEN validada y aprobada por el operador","Debe estar producida por un proveedor aprobado conforme a ED76/DO200A o DAT Type 2, Y ADEMÁS validada y aprobada por el operador","Basta con que el ciclo AIRAC esté en vigor","Debe estar validada y aprobada por el operador; el origen del proveedor es indiferente"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), to fly an RNAV (GNSS) or a VOR/NDB-based approach in managed lateral mode (or managed lateral and vertical), what must the approach stored in the navigation database comply with?","keys":["76","200","ed76/do200a"],"answer":"The FCOM requires the stored approach to be 'either' produced by an approved supplier in accordance with ED76/DO200A or DAT Type 2, 'or' validated and approved by the operator. It is an alternative condition. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 68 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["It must be produced by an approved supplier in accordance with ED76/DO200A or DAT Type 2, OR validated and approved by the operator","It must be produced by an approved supplier in accordance with ED76/DO200A or DAT Type 2, AND ALSO validated and approved by the operator","It is enough that the AIRAC cycle is in force","It must be validated and approved by the operator; the supplier origin is irrelevant"]}},{"sys":"AF_GEN","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0111","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), observas una diferencia de algunos grados entre la derrota lateral que muestra la página F-PLN del MCDU y la de la carta de una RNAV (GNSS). ¿Qué dice la nota del FCOM?","keys":["deberse","inconsistencia","magvar"],"answer":"La nota del FCOM explica que la trayectoria lateral de las RNAV (GNSS) se basa geométricamente en las coordenadas de los waypoints, y que la diferencia de grados observada entre la página F-PLN y las cartas puede venir de una inconsistencia entre la MagVar del FMS y la MagVar de la carta, sin efecto sobre la trayectoria lateral. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 68 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["Puede deberse a una inconsistencia entre la MagVar del FMS y la de la carta, y no tiene efecto sobre la trayectoria lateral","Indica un error de codificación de la aproximación: no debe volarse en modo gestionado","Obliga a validar de nuevo las coordenadas de los waypoints antes de continuar","Indica pérdida de precisión de navegación: debe comprobarse HIGH ACCURACY en el MCDU"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), you observe a difference of a few degrees between the lateral track shown on the MCDU F-PLN page and that of the chart for an RNAV (GNSS). What does the FCOM note say?","keys":["magvar","inconsistency","lateral"],"answer":"The FCOM note explains that the RNAV (GNSS) lateral path is geometrically based on the waypoint coordinates, and that the observed difference in degrees between the F-PLN page and the charts may come from an inconsistency between the FMS MagVar and the chart MagVar, with no effect on the lateral path. (FCOM LIM-AFS-10 · p. 68 · rev 05 MAY 22)","opts":["It may be due to an inconsistency between the FMS MagVar and that of the chart, and it has no effect on the lateral path","It indicates an approach coding error: it must not be flown in managed mode","It requires re-validating the waypoint coordinates before continuing","It indicates a loss of navigation accuracy: HIGH ACCURACY must be checked on the MCDU"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0112","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la altura de decisión (DH) mínima publicada para una aproximación CAT II?","keys":["100","ft","cat ii"],"answer":"La DH mínima para CAT II es 100 ft. Además, al menos un autopiloto debe estar engranado en modo APPR y el FMA debe mostrar CAT 2, CAT 3 SINGLE o CAT 3 DUAL. (Verificado sobre la página 71 del PDF: el bloque «ILS CATEGORY II» —Ident. 00020136.0001001 / 18 SEP 18, Applicable to: ALL— publica «Minimum decision height 100 ft» y «For manual landing, AP should be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL».) (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["100 ft","50 ft","75 ft","200 ft"]},"en":{"q":"What is the minimum published decision height (DH) for a CAT II approach?","keys":["100","ft","cat ii"],"answer":"The minimum DH for CAT II is 100 ft. In addition, at least one autopilot must be engaged in APPR mode and the FMA must display CAT 2, CAT 3 SINGLE or CAT 3 DUAL. (Verified against page 71 of the PDF: the «ILS CATEGORY II» block —Ident. 00020136.0001001 / 18 SEP 18, Applicable to: ALL— publishes «Minimum decision height 100 ft» and «For manual landing, AP should be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL».) (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["100 ft","50 ft","75 ft","200 ft"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0113","es":{"q":"Realizas una aproximación CAT II y decides efectuar un aterrizaje manual. ¿A qué altura, como máximo, debe quedar desconectado el autopiloto?","keys":["80","ft","cat ii"],"answer":"Para aterrizaje manual, el AP debe desconectarse no más tarde de 80 ft AGL. (Verificado sobre la página 71 del PDF: el bloque «ILS CATEGORY II» —Ident. 00020136.0001001 / 18 SEP 18, Applicable to: ALL— publica «Minimum decision height 100 ft» y «For manual landing, AP should be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL».) (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["No más tarde de 80 ft AGL","No más tarde de 50 ft AGL","No más tarde de 100 ft AGL","No más tarde de 160 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"You perform a CAT II approach and decide to carry out a manual landing. At what height, at the latest, must the autopilot be disconnected?","keys":["80","ft","cat ii"],"answer":"For manual landing, the AP must be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL. (Verified against page 71 of the PDF: the «ILS CATEGORY II» block —Ident. 00020136.0001001 / 18 SEP 18, Applicable to: ALL— publishes «Minimum decision height 100 ft» and «For manual landing, AP should be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL».) (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["No later than 80 ft AGL","No later than 50 ft AGL","No later than 100 ft AGL","No later than 160 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0114","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la altura de decisión (DH) mínima para una aproximación ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE)?","keys":["50","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"La DH mínima en CAT III fail passive (SINGLE) es 50 ft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["50 ft","20 ft","22 ft","100 ft"]},"en":{"q":"What is the minimum decision height (DH) for an ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE) approach?","keys":["50","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"The minimum DH in CAT III fail passive (SINGLE) is 50 ft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["50 ft","20 ft","22 ft","100 ft"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0115","es":{"q":"Todas las siguientes son condiciones publicadas para una aproximación ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE) EXCEPTO:","keys":["cat iii","autopilotos","estar"],"answer":"En fail passive (SINGLE) basta con al menos un autopiloto engranado en APPR. La exigencia de los DOS autopilotos pertenece a CAT III fail operational (DUAL). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Los dos autopilotos deben estar engranados en modo APPR","El A/THR debe usarse en selected o managed speed","Al menos un autopiloto debe estar engranado en modo APPR","El FMA debe mostrar CAT 3 SINGLE o CAT 3 DUAL"]},"en":{"q":"All of the following are published conditions for an ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE) approach EXCEPT:","keys":["cat iii","autopilots","both"],"answer":"In fail passive (SINGLE) at least one autopilot engaged in APPR is enough. The requirement for BOTH autopilots belongs to CAT III fail operational (DUAL). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Both autopilots must be engaged in APPR mode","The A/THR must be used in selected or managed speed","At least one autopilot must be engaged in APPR mode","The FMA must display CAT 3 SINGLE or CAT 3 DUAL"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0116","es":{"q":"¿Qué anuncio del FMA es aceptable para realizar una aproximación CAT II pero NO permite una ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE)?","keys":["2","cat iii","anuncio"],"answer":"Para CAT II el FMA puede mostrar CAT 2, CAT 3 SINGLE o CAT 3 DUAL. Para CAT III fail passive sólo valen CAT 3 SINGLE o CAT 3 DUAL: un anuncio CAT 2 no es suficiente. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["CAT 2","CAT 3 SINGLE","CAT 3 DUAL","CAT 1"]},"en":{"q":"Which FMA annunciation is acceptable to perform a CAT II approach but does NOT allow an ILS CATEGORY III FAIL PASSIVE (SINGLE)?","keys":["cat 2","cat iii","annunciation"],"answer":"For CAT II the FMA may display CAT 2, CAT 3 SINGLE or CAT 3 DUAL. For CAT III fail passive only CAT 3 SINGLE or CAT 3 DUAL are valid: a CAT 2 annunciation is not sufficient. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["CAT 2","CAT 3 SINGLE","CAT 3 DUAL","CAT 1"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0117","es":{"q":"¿En qué se diferencian las limitaciones publicadas para OTS CAT II (Other Than Standard CAT II) respecto a las de SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II)?","keys":["100","ft","ots cat ii"],"answer":"El FCOM publica para OTS CAT II exactamente las mismas limitaciones que para SA CAT II: DH mínima 100 ft, al menos un AP en APPR con CAT 2 / CAT 3 SINGLE / CAT 3 DUAL en el FMA, y la misma regla de HUD (con HUD, aterrizaje automático o manual con AP fuera a 80 ft AGL como muy tarde; sin HUD, aterrizaje automático obligatorio). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["En nada: ambas publican DH mínima de 100 ft y las mismas reglas de HUD y de FMA","La OTS CAT II tiene una DH mínima de 50 ft frente a los 100 ft de la SA CAT II","En la OTS CAT II el aterrizaje automático es obligatorio aunque se lleve HUD","La OTS CAT II exige los dos autopilotos engranados en APPR"]},"en":{"q":"How do the published limitations for OTS CAT II (Other Than Standard CAT II) differ from those for SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II)?","keys":["100","ft","ots cat ii"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes for OTS CAT II exactly the same limitations as for SA CAT II: minimum DH 100 ft, at least one AP in APPR with CAT 2 / CAT 3 SINGLE / CAT 3 DUAL on the FMA, and the same HUD rule (with HUD, automatic landing or manual landing with the AP off no later than 80 ft AGL; without HUD, automatic landing mandatory). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["In nothing: both publish a minimum DH of 100 ft and the same HUD and FMA rules","OTS CAT II has a minimum DH of 50 ft versus the 100 ft of SA CAT II","In OTS CAT II automatic landing is mandatory even when a HUD is fitted","OTS CAT II requires both autopilots engaged in APPR"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0118","es":{"q":"En una aproximación SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II) en un avión SIN HUD, ¿qué tipo de aterrizaje debe realizar la tripulación?","keys":["sa cat ii","aterrizaje","automatico"],"answer":"Sin HUD, la tripulación debe realizar un aterrizaje automático. La opción de aterrizaje manual sólo existe con HUD, usándolo para monitorizar la aproximación. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Un aterrizaje automático obligatoriamente","Un aterrizaje manual, desconectando el AP no más tarde de 80 ft AGL","Indistintamente manual o automático, a criterio del PF","Un aterrizaje manual, desconectando el AP no más tarde de 50 ft AGL"]},"en":{"q":"On an SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II) approach in an aircraft WITHOUT HUD, what type of landing must the flight crew perform?","keys":["sa cat ii","automatic","landing"],"answer":"Without HUD, the flight crew must perform an automatic landing. The manual landing option only exists with HUD, using it to monitor the approach. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["An automatic landing, mandatorily","A manual landing, disconnecting the AP no later than 80 ft AGL","Either manual or automatic, at the PF's discretion","A manual landing, disconnecting the AP no later than 50 ft AGL"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0119","es":{"q":"Vuelas una SA CAT II en un avión equipado con HUD. Decides realizar la aproximación automática pero SIN aterrizaje automático. ¿Qué exige la limitación?","keys":["80","ft","sa cat ii"],"answer":"Con HUD, la tripulación debe usarlo para monitorizar la aproximación y puede realizar aterrizaje automático o manual. Si se hace aproximación automática sin aterrizaje automático, el AP debe desengrancharse no más tarde de 80 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Que el autopiloto se desconecte no más tarde de 80 ft AGL","Que el autopiloto permanezca engranado hasta el rollout","Que se desconecte el autopiloto al alcanzar la DH de 100 ft","No está permitido: con HUD el aterrizaje automático es obligatorio"]},"en":{"q":"You fly an SA CAT II in an aircraft equipped with HUD. You decide to perform the automatic approach but WITHOUT automatic landing. What does the limitation require?","keys":["80","ft","sa cat ii"],"answer":"With HUD, the flight crew must use it to monitor the approach and may perform an automatic or manual landing. If an automatic approach is flown without automatic landing, the AP must be disengaged no later than 80 ft AGL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["That the autopilot be disconnected no later than 80 ft AGL","That the autopilot remain engaged until rollout","That the autopilot be disconnected upon reaching the 100 ft DH","It is not permitted: with HUD the automatic landing is mandatory"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0120","es":{"q":"Respecto a la SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II), ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["80","ft","sa cat ii"],"answer":"Es falsa: sin HUD la tripulación DEBE realizar un aterrizaje automático. El resto son requisitos correctos de la SA CAT II. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Sin HUD, la tripulación puede realizar un aterrizaje manual desconectando el AP a 80 ft AGL","La altura de decisión mínima es 100 ft","Al menos un autopiloto debe estar engranado en modo APPR","Con HUD, la tripulación debe usar el HUD para monitorizar la aproximación"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding SA CAT II (Special Authorization CAT II), which of the following statements is FALSE?","keys":["80","ft","sa cat ii"],"answer":"It is false: without HUD the flight crew MUST perform an automatic landing. The rest are correct SA CAT II requirements. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 71 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Without HUD, the flight crew may perform a manual landing disconnecting the AP at 80 ft AGL","The minimum decision height is 100 ft","At least one autopilot must be engaged in APPR mode","With HUD, the flight crew must use the HUD to monitor the approach"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0121","es":{"q":"En un A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) con un motor inoperativo, ¿en qué configuración está aprobado el autoland CAT II y CAT III fail passive?","keys":["conf full","configuracion","full"],"answer":"En el A320 CEO, con motor parado el autoland CAT II y CAT III fail passive sólo está aprobado en configuración FULL (y siempre que los procedimientos de engine-out se completen antes de 1 000 ft en aproximación). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Sólo en configuración FULL","En configuración 3 y FULL","En configuración 2, 3 y FULL","En cualquier configuración de aterrizaje"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) with one engine inoperative, in which configuration is CAT II and CAT III fail passive autoland approved?","keys":["conf full","approved","full"],"answer":"On the A320 CEO, with one engine out CAT II and CAT III fail passive autoland is only approved in FULL configuration (and provided the engine-out procedures are completed before 1 000 ft on approach). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Only in FULL configuration","In configuration 3 and FULL","In configuration 2, 3 and FULL","In any landing configuration"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0122","es":{"q":"Vuelas un A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) con un motor inoperativo. Los procedimientos de engine-out quedaron completados a 1 500 ft y planificas CONF 3 por performance. ¿Puedes realizar un autoland CAT III fail passive?","keys":["conf full","avion","autoland"],"answer":"Se cumple la condición de tiempo (procedimientos completados antes de 1 000 ft), pero falla la de configuración: en el A320 CEO el autoland CAT II/CAT III fail passive con motor parado sólo está aprobado en CONF FULL. Ambas condiciones deben cumplirse a la vez. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: en este avión el autoland con motor parado sólo está aprobado en CONF FULL","Sí: los procedimientos se completaron antes de 1 000 ft, que es la única condición","Sí, siempre que el FMA muestre CAT 3 DUAL","Sí, siempre que el aeropuerto esté a 5 750 ft de elevación o menos"]},"en":{"q":"You fly an A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) with one engine inoperative. The engine-out procedures were completed at 1 500 ft and you plan CONF 3 for performance. Can you perform a CAT III fail passive autoland?","keys":["conf full","autoland","config"],"answer":"The time condition is met (procedures completed before 1 000 ft), but the configuration one fails: on the A320 CEO the CAT II/CAT III fail passive autoland with one engine out is only approved in CONF FULL. Both conditions must be met at the same time. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: on this aircraft the engine-out autoland is only approved in CONF FULL","Yes: the procedures were completed before 1 000 ft, which is the only condition","Yes, provided the FMA displays CAT 3 DUAL","Yes, provided the airport elevation is 5 750 ft or below"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0123","es":{"q":"¿En qué aviones de la flota el autoland CAT II y CAT III fail passive con un motor inoperativo está aprobado ÚNICAMENTE en configuración FULL?","keys":["320","56","conf full"],"answer":"La restricción a CONF FULL exclusiva aplica al grupo de A320 CEO (CFM56 o IAE V2500). El resto de grupos (A319/A321 CFM56, A321 IAE V2500 y los neo con PW1100G) tienen aprobado el autoland con motor parado en CONF 3 y FULL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En los A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500)","En los A319 y A321 con motores CFM56","En los A320neo y A321neo con motores PW1100G","En toda la flota A319/A320/A321"]},"en":{"q":"On which fleet aircraft is CAT II and CAT III fail passive autoland with one engine inoperative approved ONLY in FULL configuration?","keys":["320","56","conf full"],"answer":"The exclusive restriction to CONF FULL applies to the A320 CEO group (CFM56 or IAE V2500). The other groups (A319/A321 CFM56, A321 IAE V2500 and the neo with PW1100G) have engine-out autoland approved in CONF 3 and FULL. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["On the A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines)","On the A319 and A321 with CFM56 engines","On the A320neo and A321neo with PW1100G engines","On the entire A319/A320/A321 fleet"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0124","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el alert height publicado para una ILS CATEGORY III FAIL OPERATIONAL (DUAL)?","keys":["100","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"El alert height es 100 ft. Este dato el FCOM lo certifica avión a avión, por eso se ancla al avión de referencia de la flota. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["100 ft","50 ft","75 ft","200 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the published alert height for an ILS CATEGORY III FAIL OPERATIONAL (DUAL)?","keys":["100","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"The alert height is 100 ft. This figure the FCOM certifies aircraft by aircraft, which is why it is anchored to the fleet reference aircraft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["100 ft","50 ft","75 ft","200 ft"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0125","es":{"q":"Vas a volar una CAT III CON DH fail operational (DUAL) en el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota). La carta de aproximación publica DH 20 ft. ¿Puedes aceptarla?","keys":["22","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"Para este avión, la DH mínima en CAT III con DH es 22 ft; una DH de 20 ft queda por debajo del mínimo certificado y no puede aceptarse. La DH que se aplica es siempre la más restrictiva entre la del avión y la de la carta. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["No, el mínimo certificado del avión es 22 ft","Sí, 20 ft está por encima del mínimo certificado","Sí, siempre que el RVR sea igual o superior a 75 m","No, en CAT III con DH el mínimo certificado del avión es 50 ft"]},"en":{"q":"You are going to fly a CAT III WITH DH fail operational (DUAL) on the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft). The approach chart publishes DH 20 ft. Can you accept it?","keys":["22","ft","cat iii"],"answer":"For this aircraft, the minimum DH in CAT III with DH is 22 ft; a DH of 20 ft is below the certified minimum and cannot be accepted. The applicable DH is always the more restrictive of the aircraft's and the chart's. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["No, the aircraft's certified minimum is 22 ft","Yes, 20 ft is above the certified minimum","Yes, provided the RVR is equal to or greater than 75 m","No, in CAT III with DH the aircraft's certified minimum is 50 ft"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0126","es":{"q":"Sobre la ILS CATEGORY III FAIL OPERATIONAL (DUAL) en el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["cat iii","basta","autopiloto"],"answer":"Es falsa: en fail operational (DUAL) los DOS autopilotos deben estar engranados en modo APPR. Con un solo autopiloto la capacidad sería, como mucho, CAT 3 SINGLE (fail passive). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["Basta con un autopiloto engranado en modo APPR","El A/THR debe usarse en selected o managed speed","En CAT III sin DH, el RVR mínimo es 75 m","El FMA debe mostrar CAT 3 DUAL"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the ILS CATEGORY III FAIL OPERATIONAL (DUAL) on the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["cat iii","autopilot","both"],"answer":"It is false: in fail operational (DUAL) BOTH autopilots must be engaged in APPR mode. With a single autopilot the capability would be, at most, CAT 3 SINGLE (fail passive). (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 73 · rev 18 SEP 18)","opts":["One autopilot engaged in APPR mode is enough","The A/THR must be used in selected or managed speed","In CAT III without DH, the minimum RVR is 75 m","The FMA must display CAT 3 DUAL"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0127","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500 y un motor inoperativo, ¿en qué configuraciones está aprobado el autoland CAT II y CAT III fail passive?","keys":["3","conf 3","configuracion"],"answer":"En este grupo el autoland CAT II y CAT III fail passive con motor parado está aprobado en configuración 3 y FULL, siempre que los procedimientos de engine-out se completen antes de alcanzar 1 000 ft en aproximación. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En configuración 3 y FULL","Sólo en configuración FULL","Sólo en configuración 3","En configuración 2 y 3"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines and one engine inoperative, in which configurations is CAT II and CAT III fail passive autoland approved?","keys":["conf 3","full","config"],"answer":"On this group the CAT II and CAT III fail passive autoland with one engine out is approved in configuration 3 and FULL, provided the engine-out procedures are completed before reaching 1 000 ft on approach. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["In configuration 3 and FULL","Only in FULL configuration","Only in configuration 3","In configuration 2 and 3"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0128","es":{"q":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un A320neo (motores PW1100G) y un A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) en cuanto al autoland CAT II/CAT III fail passive con un motor inoperativo?","keys":["320","3","conf 3"],"answer":"La diferencia está en la configuración: el A320neo (PW1100G) lo tiene aprobado en CONF 3 y FULL, mientras que el A320 CEO sólo en CONF FULL. El límite de 1 000 ft para completar los procedimientos de engine-out es común a ambos. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El A320neo lo tiene aprobado en CONF 3 y FULL; el A320 CEO sólo en CONF FULL","El A320neo sólo lo tiene aprobado en CONF FULL; el A320 CEO en CONF 3 y FULL","Ninguna: ambos lo tienen aprobado en CONF 3 y FULL","El A320neo debe completar los procedimientos de engine-out antes de 1 500 ft; el A320 CEO antes de 1 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"What is the difference between an A320neo (PW1100G engines) and an A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) regarding CAT II/CAT III fail passive autoland with one engine inoperative?","keys":["320","conf 3","full"],"answer":"The difference is in the configuration: the A320neo (PW1100G) has it approved in CONF 3 and FULL, whereas the A320 CEO only in CONF FULL. The 1 000 ft limit to complete the engine-out procedures is common to both. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The A320neo has it approved in CONF 3 and FULL; the A320 CEO only in CONF FULL","The A320neo only has it approved in CONF FULL; the A320 CEO in CONF 3 and FULL","None: both have it approved in CONF 3 and FULL","The A320neo must complete the engine-out procedures before 1 500 ft; the A320 CEO before 1 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0129","es":{"q":"En un A321neo (motores PW1100G) con un motor inoperativo, la tripulación termina los procedimientos de engine-out pasando 800 ft en la aproximación, con CONF FULL seleccionada. ¿Puede realizar un autoland CAT III fail passive?","keys":["1000","ft","procedimientos"],"answer":"La aprobación exige DOS condiciones simultáneas: configuración 3 o FULL Y procedimientos de engine-out completados antes de alcanzar 1 000 ft en aproximación. Completarlos a 800 ft incumple la segunda. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: los procedimientos de engine-out debían estar completados antes de alcanzar 1 000 ft","Sí: la CONF FULL está aprobada y eso es suficiente","Sí, siempre que se seleccione CONF 3 en lugar de FULL","Sí, siempre que ambos autopilotos estén engranados en APPR"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321neo (PW1100G engines) with one engine inoperative, the flight crew finishes the engine-out procedures passing 800 ft on the approach, with CONF FULL selected. Can they perform a CAT III fail passive autoland?","keys":["1000","ft","procedures"],"answer":"The approval requires TWO simultaneous conditions: configuration 3 or FULL AND engine-out procedures completed before reaching 1 000 ft on approach. Completing them at 800 ft fails the second. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 74 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: the engine-out procedures had to be completed before reaching 1 000 ft","Yes: CONF FULL is approved and that is enough","Yes, provided CONF 3 is selected instead of FULL","Yes, provided both autopilots are engaged in APPR"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0130","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el viento cruzado máximo para ILS/MLS CAT II o CAT III y para GLS CAT I?","keys":["20","15","kt"],"answer":"El viento cruzado máximo es 20 kt sin automatic rollout y 15 kt con automatic rollout. Este dato el FCOM lo certifica avión a avión, de ahí que se ancle al avión de referencia. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 kt sin rollout automático / 15 kt con rollout automático","10 kt, tanto con rollout automático como sin él","25 kt sin rollout automático / 20 kt con rollout automático","20 kt, tanto con rollout automático como sin él"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum crosswind for ILS/MLS CAT II or CAT III and for GLS CAT I?","keys":["20","15","kt"],"answer":"The maximum crosswind is 20 kt without automatic rollout and 15 kt with automatic rollout. This figure the FCOM certifies aircraft by aircraft, which is why it is anchored to the reference aircraft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 kt without automatic rollout / 15 kt with automatic rollout","10 kt, both with and without automatic rollout","25 kt without automatic rollout / 20 kt with automatic rollout","20 kt, both with and without automatic rollout"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0131","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) estás en una CAT III y el viento del ND excede las limitaciones de autoland, pero la torre reporta un viento en superficie dentro de límites. ¿Qué puedes hacer?","keys":["nd","mantener","autopiloto"],"answer":"La limitación de viento se basa en el viento en superficie reportado por ATC. Si el ND excede los límites pero la torre reporta viento dentro de límites, el autopiloto puede permanecer engranado. El caso inverso (torre por encima de límites) es el que obliga a CAT I automática sin autoland. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Mantener el autopiloto engranado: la limitación se basa en el viento en superficie reportado por ATC","Desconectar el autopiloto de inmediato: manda siempre el viento más restrictivo de los dos","Sólo realizar una aproximación automática CAT I sin autoland","Mantener el autopiloto, pero prohibido el rollout automático"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) you are on a CAT III and the ND wind exceeds the autoland limitations, but the tower reports a surface wind within limits. What can you do?","keys":["nd","surface","autopilot"],"answer":"The wind limitation is based on the surface wind reported by ATC. If the ND exceeds the limits but the tower reports wind within limits, the autopilot may remain engaged. The reverse case (tower above limits) is the one that forces automatic CAT I without autoland. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Keep the autopilot engaged: the limitation is based on the surface wind reported by ATC","Disconnect the autopilot immediately: the more restrictive of the two winds always governs","Only perform an automatic CAT I approach without autoland","Keep the autopilot, but automatic rollout is prohibited"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0132","es":{"q":"Sobre los vientos máximos para ILS/MLS CAT II o CAT III y GLS CAT I en el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["30","kt","viento"],"answer":"Es falsa: el viento en cola máximo de este avión es 10 kt, un valor único. Los 30 kt son de viento en CARA (headwind) de otro grupo de la flota, y para aterrizaje y rollout automáticos. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El viento en cola máximo es 30 kt para aterrizaje y rollout automáticos","El viento en cara máximo es 30 kt","El viento en cola máximo es 10 kt","Si la torre reporta viento por encima de límites, sólo puede realizarse aproximación automática CAT I sin autoland"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the maximum winds for ILS/MLS CAT II or CAT III and GLS CAT I on the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["30","kt","tailwind"],"answer":"It is false: this aircraft's maximum tailwind is 10 kt, a single value. The 30 kt is a headwind of another fleet group, and for automatic landing and rollout. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 76 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The maximum tailwind is 30 kt for automatic landing and rollout","The maximum headwind is 30 kt","The maximum tailwind is 10 kt","If the tower reports wind above limits, only an automatic CAT I approach without autoland may be performed"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0133","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿hasta qué elevación de aeropuerto está demostrado el aterrizaje automático?","keys":["6500","ft","a320"],"answer":"En este avión el aterrizaje automático está demostrado con una elevación de aeropuerto igual o inferior a 6 500 ft. Es un dato certificado avión a avión: otros grupos de la flota tienen 2 500, 5 750 o 9 200 ft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 82 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["6 500 ft o menos","2 500 ft o menos","5 750 ft o menos","9 200 ft o menos"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), up to what airport elevation is automatic landing demonstrated?","keys":["6500","ft","a320"],"answer":"On this aircraft the automatic landing is demonstrated with an airport elevation equal to or below 6 500 ft. It is a figure certified aircraft by aircraft: other fleet groups have 2 500, 5 750 or 9 200 ft. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 82 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["6 500 ft or below","2 500 ft or below","5 750 ft or below","9 200 ft or below"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0134","es":{"q":"Vuelas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) a un aeropuerto situado a 7 000 ft de elevación. ¿Qué implica esto para el aterrizaje automático?","keys":["6500","ft","aterrizaje"],"answer":"El aterrizaje automático de este avión está demostrado con elevación de aeropuerto igual o inferior a 6 500 ft. A 7 000 ft queda fuera de las condiciones demostradas. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 82 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El aterrizaje automático no está demostrado: la elevación supera los 6 500 ft de este avión","Nada: el aterrizaje automático está demostrado hasta 9 200 ft","Nada, siempre que el peso esté por debajo del máximo de aterrizaje","El aterrizaje automático sigue demostrado, pero sólo en CONF FULL"]},"en":{"q":"You fly the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) to an airport located at 7 000 ft elevation. What does this imply for automatic landing?","keys":["6500","ft","landing"],"answer":"The automatic landing of this aircraft is demonstrated with an airport elevation equal to or below 6 500 ft. At 7 000 ft it is outside the demonstrated conditions. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 82 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The automatic landing is not demonstrated: the elevation exceeds this aircraft's 6 500 ft","Nothing: the automatic landing is demonstrated up to 9 200 ft","Nothing, provided the weight is below the maximum landing weight","The automatic landing is still demonstrated, but only in CONF FULL"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0135","es":{"q":"¿En qué pistas de Johannesburgo NO está permitido el aterrizaje automático?","keys":["03","21","pistas"],"answer":"El aterrizaje automático no está permitido en las pistas 03R/21L de Johannesburgo. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 90 · rev 25 APR 13)","opts":["03R/21L","03L/21R","En ninguna pista de Johannesburgo","En todas salvo la más larga"]},"en":{"q":"On which runways at Johannesburg is automatic landing NOT permitted?","keys":["03","21","runways"],"answer":"Automatic landing is not permitted on runways 03R/21L at Johannesburg. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 90 · rev 25 APR 13)","opts":["03R/21L","03L/21R","On no runway at Johannesburg","On all except the longest"]}},{"sys":"AF_FG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0136","es":{"q":"La prohibición de aterrizaje automático en las pistas 03R/21L de Johannesburgo, ¿a qué aviones aplica?","keys":["319","320","toda"],"answer":"La limitación está publicada como aplicable a toda la flota (ALL): ningún avión del FCOM A319/A320/A321 puede realizar aterrizaje automático en las pistas 03R/21L de Johannesburgo. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 90 · rev 25 APR 13)","opts":["A toda la flota A319/A320/A321","Sólo a los A320 CEO con motores CFM56","Sólo a los A321 y A321neo","Sólo a los aviones sin capacidad CAT III fail operational"]},"en":{"q":"The prohibition of automatic landing on runways 03R/21L at Johannesburg applies to which aircraft?","keys":["319","320","fleet"],"answer":"The limitation is published as applicable to the whole fleet (ALL): no FCOM A319/A320/A321 aircraft may perform automatic landing on runways 03R/21L at Johannesburg. (FCOM LIM-AFS-20 · p. 90 · rev 25 APR 13)","opts":["To the entire A319/A320/A321 fleet","Only to the A320 CEO with CFM56 engines","Only to the A321 and A321neo","Only to aircraft without CAT III fail operational capability"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0137","es":{"q":"Tras tres intentos consecutivos de arranque del APU, ¿cuánto tiempo debe esperar la tripulación antes de un nuevo intento?","keys":["60","min","apu"],"answer":"El FCOM establece que, tras tres intentos consecutivos de arranque del APU, la tripulación debe esperar 60 min antes de un nuevo intento. La espera protege al motor de arranque del sobrecalentamiento acumulado. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["60 min","15 min","30 min","90 min"]},"en":{"q":"After three consecutive APU start attempts, how long must the flight crew wait before a new attempt?","keys":["60","min","apu"],"answer":"The FCOM establishes that, after three consecutive APU start attempts, the flight crew must wait 60 min before a new attempt. The wait protects the starter motor from accumulated overheating. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["60 min","15 min","30 min","90 min"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0138","es":{"q":"En parada, con el avión en configuración de tránsito, has realizado tres intentos consecutivos de arranque del APU y ninguno ha prosperado. ¿Qué exige la limitación del FCOM?","keys":["60","min","apu"],"answer":"La limitación es taxativa: tras tres intentos consecutivos hay que esperar 60 min antes de un nuevo intento. El límite se cuenta por intentos, no por la EGT alcanzada. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Esperar 60 min antes de un nuevo intento de arranque","Realizar un cuarto intento inmediatamente y, si falla, esperar 60 min","Esperar 20 min y reintentar con el AIR BLEED en OFF","No hay limitación de espera mientras la EGT se mantenga por debajo del máximo"]},"en":{"q":"On the ground, with the aircraft in transit configuration, you have made three consecutive APU start attempts and none has succeeded. What does the FCOM limitation require?","keys":["60","min","apu"],"answer":"The limitation is strict: after three consecutive attempts you must wait 60 min before a new attempt. The limit is counted by attempts, not by the EGT reached. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Wait 60 min before a new start attempt","Make a fourth attempt immediately and, if it fails, wait 60 min","Wait 20 min and retry with the AIR BLEED OFF","There is no waiting limitation as long as the EGT stays below the maximum"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0139","es":{"q":"Respecto a la limitación de arranque del APU, ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["20","min","apu"],"answer":"FALSA: la espera exigida es de 60 min, no de 20 min. Los 20 min pertenecen a otra limitación distinta (tiempo máximo recomendado sin suministro de aire acondicionado con pasajeros a bordo, LIM-AIR). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["La espera exigida tras tres intentos consecutivos es de 20 min","Tras tres intentos consecutivos de arranque hay que esperar antes de un nuevo intento","La limitación se cuenta por intentos de arranque consecutivos","La limitación aplica a toda la flota, sin distinción de modelo ni de motor"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the APU start limitation, which of the following statements is FALSE?","keys":["20","min","apu"],"answer":"FALSE: the required wait is 60 min, not 20 min. The 20 min belongs to a different limitation (maximum recommended time without air-conditioning supply with passengers on board, LIM-AIR). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The required wait after three consecutive attempts is 20 min","After three consecutive start attempts you must wait before a new attempt","The limitation is counted by consecutive start attempts","The limitation applies to the whole fleet, regardless of model or engine"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0140","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la EGT máxima para el arranque del APU por debajo de 35 000 ft?","keys":["1090","apu","a320"],"answer":"Para este avión, la EGT máxima de arranque del APU por debajo de 35 000 ft es 1 090 °C. Este dato el FCOM lo certifica avión a avión, por eso se ancla al avión de referencia. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 090 °C","900 °C","982 °C","1 120 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum EGT for APU start below 35 000 ft?","keys":["1090","apu","a320"],"answer":"For this aircraft, the maximum APU start EGT below 35 000 ft is 1 090 °C. This figure the FCOM certifies aircraft by aircraft, which is why it is anchored to the reference aircraft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 090 °C","900 °C","982 °C","1 120 °C"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0141","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la EGT máxima con el APU en marcha (APU running)?","keys":["675","apu","a320"],"answer":"La EGT máxima con el APU en marcha para este avión es 675 °C, un valor único y sin escalones. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["675 °C","682 °C","700 °C","742 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum EGT with the APU running?","keys":["675","apu","a320"],"answer":"The maximum EGT with the APU running for this aircraft is 675 °C, a single value with no steps. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["675 °C","682 °C","700 °C","742 °C"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0142","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre los límites de EGT del APU es FALSA?","keys":["25000","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSA: para este avión el umbral que separa los dos máximos de EGT de arranque es 35 000 ft (1 090 °C por debajo, 1 120 °C por encima). Los 25 000 ft son el umbral de otro grupo de aviones de la flota, que además tiene valores de EGT completamente distintos (900 °C / 982 °C). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El umbral de altitud que separa ambos máximos de arranque es 25 000 ft","El máximo de EGT para arranque por debajo del umbral de altitud publicado es 1 090 °C","El máximo de EGT para arranque por encima del umbral de altitud publicado es 1 120 °C","Con el APU en marcha, el máximo de EGT es 675 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements about the APU EGT limits is FALSE?","keys":["25000","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSE: for this aircraft the threshold separating the two maximum start EGTs is 35 000 ft (1 090 °C below, 1 120 °C above). The 25 000 ft is the threshold of another fleet group, which additionally has completely different EGT values (900 °C / 982 °C). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The altitude threshold separating the two start maxima is 25 000 ft","The maximum EGT for start below the published altitude threshold is 1 090 °C","The maximum EGT for start above the published altitude threshold is 1 120 °C","With the APU running, the maximum EGT is 675 °C"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0143","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la velocidad máxima de rotor (N) del APU?","keys":["107","apu","velocidad"],"answer":"El FCOM publica una velocidad máxima de rotor del APU de 107 %. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["107 %","99 %","101 %","105 %"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum APU rotor speed (N)?","keys":["107","apu","rotor"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes a maximum APU rotor speed of 107 %. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["107 %","99 %","101 %","105 %"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0144","es":{"q":"El límite de velocidad máxima de rotor del APU de 107 % de N, ¿a qué aviones de la flota aplica?","keys":["319","320","apu"],"answer":"El bloque ROTOR SPEED está publicado como Applicable to: ALL, por lo que el 107 % de N aplica a toda la flota A319/A320/A321 con independencia del modelo y del motor instalado. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["A toda la flota A319/A320/A321, sin distinción de modelo ni de motor","Sólo a los A320 con motores IAE V2500","Sólo a los A320neo y A321neo con motores PW1100G","Sólo a los aviones equipados con APU de nueva generación"]},"en":{"q":"The maximum APU rotor speed limit of 107 % N applies to which fleet aircraft?","keys":["319","320","apu"],"answer":"The ROTOR SPEED block is published as Applicable to: ALL, so the 107 % N applies to the entire A319/A320/A321 fleet regardless of model and installed engine. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 95 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["To the entire A319/A320/A321 fleet, regardless of model or engine","Only to the A320 with IAE V2500 engines","Only to the A320neo and A321neo with PW1100G engines","Only to aircraft fitted with a new-generation APU"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0145","es":{"q":"Durante procedimientos de repostaje/defueling, los arranques y paradas del APU están permitidos con restricciones. Todas las siguientes son restricciones publicadas en el FCOM EXCEPTO:","keys":["apu","marcha","antes"],"answer":"El FCOM NO exige parar el APU antes de conectar la manguera: precisamente permite arranques y paradas durante el repostaje, con sólo tres restricciones (no arrancar si el APU falló al arrancar, no arrancar tras una parada automática, y parada normal ante derrame de combustible). Exigir la parada previa a conectar la manguera es una restricción inventada. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Si el APU está en marcha antes de iniciar el repostaje, debe pararse antes de conectar la manguera","Si el APU no llegó a arrancar, no se debe arrancar el APU","Tras una parada automática del APU, no se debe arrancar el APU","Si se produce un derrame de combustible, se debe efectuar una parada normal del APU"]},"en":{"q":"During refuel/defueling procedures, APU starts and stops are permitted with restrictions. All of the following are restrictions published in the FCOM EXCEPT:","keys":["apu","hose","before"],"answer":"The FCOM does NOT require stopping the APU before connecting the hose: it precisely permits starts and stops during refueling, with only three restrictions (do not start if the APU failed to start, do not start after an automatic shutdown, and normal shutdown in the event of a fuel spillage). Requiring the shutdown before connecting the hose is an invented restriction. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["If the APU is running before starting refueling, it must be stopped before connecting the hose","If the APU failed to start, the APU must not be started","After an automatic APU shutdown, the APU must not be started","If a fuel spillage occurs, a normal APU shutdown must be carried out"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0146","es":{"q":"Estás repostando en plataforma y el APU se para automáticamente. ¿Qué permite el FCOM?","keys":["apu","arrancar","estas"],"answer":"La restricción es incondicional: tras una parada automática del APU durante el repostaje, no se debe arrancar el APU. El FCOM no ofrece ninguna condición que lo habilite. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No arrancar el APU","Rearrancar el APU de inmediato si no se ha producido derrame de combustible","Rearrancar el APU tras esperar 60 min","Rearrancar el APU sólo con el repostaje interrumpido y autorización del supervisor de rampa"]},"en":{"q":"You are refueling on the apron and the APU shuts down automatically. What does the FCOM permit?","keys":["apu","start","not"],"answer":"The restriction is unconditional: after an automatic APU shutdown during refueling, the APU must not be started. The FCOM offers no condition that enables it. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Do not start the APU","Restart the APU immediately if no fuel spillage has occurred","Restart the APU after waiting 60 min","Restart the APU only with refueling interrupted and authorization from the ramp supervisor"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0147","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), cuando un valor de la envolvente ambiental (environmental envelope) del avión es más limitativo que la envolvente operacional (operational envelope) del APU, ¿qué establece el FCOM?","keys":["apu","exceder","valor"],"answer":"La Note del FCOM es explícita: cuando la envolvente ambiental del avión es más limitativa que la operacional del APU, no se debe exceder el valor de la envolvente ambiental del avión. Es decir, manda siempre la más restrictiva de las dos. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["Que no se debe exceder el valor de la envolvente ambiental del avión","Que prevalece siempre la envolvente operacional del APU por ser específica del sistema","Que la tripulación puede elegir la más favorable de las dos","Que se aplica el valor medio entre ambas envolventes"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), when a value of the aircraft's environmental envelope is more limiting than the APU's operational envelope, what does the FCOM establish?","keys":["apu","exceed","environmental"],"answer":"The FCOM Note is explicit: when the aircraft's environmental envelope is more limiting than the APU's operational envelope, the value of the aircraft's environmental envelope must not be exceeded. That is, the more restrictive of the two always governs. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["That the value of the aircraft's environmental envelope must not be exceeded","That the APU's operational envelope always prevails, being system-specific","That the flight crew may choose the more favorable of the two","That the average value between the two envelopes applies"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0148","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), la envolvente operacional del APU admite unas condiciones ambientales determinadas y quieres comprobar si la envolvente ambiental del avión es más restrictiva. ¿A qué sección del FCOM te remite la Note de OPERATIONAL ENVELOPE?","keys":["apu","environmental","envelope"],"answer":"La Note remite expresamente a LIM-AG-OPS Environmental Envelope, donde está publicada la envolvente ambiental del avión. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["LIM-AG-OPS Environmental Envelope","LIM-AIR Environmental Envelope","LIM-ENG Environmental Envelope","LIM-AG-SPD Environmental Envelope"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), the APU operational envelope allows certain ambient conditions and you want to check whether the aircraft's environmental envelope is more restrictive. To which FCOM section does the Note of the OPERATIONAL ENVELOPE refer you?","keys":["apu","environmental","envelope"],"answer":"The Note refers explicitly to LIM-AG-OPS Environmental Envelope, where the aircraft's environmental envelope is published. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 96 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["LIM-AG-OPS Environmental Envelope","LIM-AIR Environmental Envelope","LIM-ENG Environmental Envelope","LIM-AG-SPD Environmental Envelope"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0149","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿hasta qué altitud de presión llega la envolvente de operación y rearranque NORMAL del APU (APU Operation and Normal Restart Limit)? Ojo: no es el rearranque con batería en configuración eléctrica de emergencia.","keys":["41000","ft","apu"],"answer":"El contorno de la envolvente —operación y rearranque NORMAL— llega a 41 000 ft. No confundir con el APU Battery Restart Limit (Elec Emer Config): ése es el rearranque CON BATERÍA en emergencia eléctrica y está limitado a 25 000 ft (una línea distinta del mismo gráfico, y una limitación aparte). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["41 000 ft","25 000 ft","35 000 ft","39 800 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), up to what pressure altitude does the APU Operation and Normal Restart Limit envelope reach? Note: this is not the battery restart in emergency electrical configuration.","keys":["41000","ft","apu"],"answer":"The envelope contour —operation and NORMAL restart— reaches 41 000 ft. Do not confuse it with the APU Battery Restart Limit (Elec Emer Config): that is the battery restart in electrical emergency and is limited to 25 000 ft (a separate line on the same chart, and a separate limitation). (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["41 000 ft","25 000 ft","35 000 ft","39 800 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope"},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0150","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿hasta qué altitud de presión está definida la APU Ground Operation en la envolvente operacional?","keys":["14500","ft","apu"],"answer":"En la envolvente de este avión, la APU Ground Operation está definida hasta 14 500 ft de altitud de presión. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["14 500 ft","9 200 ft","15 000 ft","22 500 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), up to what pressure altitude is APU Ground Operation defined in the operational envelope?","keys":["14500","ft","apu"],"answer":"On this aircraft's envelope, APU Ground Operation is defined up to 14 500 ft pressure altitude. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["14 500 ft","9 200 ft","15 000 ft","22 500 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope"},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0151","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la envolvente operacional del APU es FALSA?","keys":["9200","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSA: en la envolvente de este avión la APU Ground Operation llega hasta 14 500 ft. Los 9 200 ft corresponden a la envolvente de otro grupo de aviones de la flota, con límites más restrictivos. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["La APU Ground Operation está limitada a 9 200 ft","La envolvente de operación y rearranque normal alcanza 41 000 ft","El límite de rearranque del APU con batería (Elec Emer Config) está en 25 000 ft","El suelo de la envolvente está en -2 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements about the APU operational envelope is FALSE?","keys":["9200","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSE: on this aircraft's envelope APU Ground Operation reaches up to 14 500 ft. The 9 200 ft figure corresponds to the envelope of another group of fleet aircraft, with more restrictive limits. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["APU Ground Operation is limited to 9 200 ft","The operation and normal restart envelope reaches 41 000 ft","The APU battery restart limit (Elec Emer Config) is 25 000 ft","The floor of the envelope is at -2 000 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope","mcOnly":1},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0152","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿por encima de qué altitud de presión el APU sólo proporciona Elec Power Only?","keys":["22500","ft","apu"],"answer":"En la envolvente de este avión, por encima de 22 500 ft el APU sólo proporciona potencia eléctrica (Elec Power Only). Por debajo de esa altitud, y hasta -2 000 ft, proporciona Bleed Air and Elec Power. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["22 500 ft","14 500 ft","20 000 ft","25 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), above what pressure altitude does the APU provide Elec Power Only?","keys":["22500","ft","apu"],"answer":"On this aircraft's envelope, above 22 500 ft the APU provides electrical power only (Elec Power Only). Below that altitude, and down to -2 000 ft, it provides Bleed Air and Elec Power. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["22 500 ft","14 500 ft","20 000 ft","25 000 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope"},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0153","es":{"q":"Vuelas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) en crucero a FL240 y consideras arrancar el APU para suministrar aire de sangrado al acondicionamiento. Según la envolvente operacional del APU, ¿es posible?","keys":["22500","ft","apu"],"answer":"A FL240 (24 000 ft) estás por encima de los 22 500 ft, altitud a partir de la cual la envolvente sólo contempla Elec Power Only. No hay aire de sangrado del APU disponible. Es coherente con el bloque APU BLEED, que limita el uso para acondicionamiento y presurización con un solo pack a 22 500 ft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["No: por encima de 22 500 ft el APU sólo proporciona potencia eléctrica","Sí: la envolvente admite Bleed Air and Elec Power hasta 25 000 ft","Sí, pero sólo con un pack en servicio y por debajo de 41 000 ft","No: por encima de 14 500 ft el APU no puede arrancarse en vuelo"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) in cruise at FL240 and consider starting the APU to supply bleed air to the air conditioning. According to the APU operational envelope, is it possible?","keys":["22500","ft","apu"],"answer":"At FL240 (24 000 ft) you are above 22 500 ft, the altitude above which the envelope only provides Elec Power Only. No APU bleed air is available. This is consistent with the APU BLEED block, which limits its use for air conditioning and pressurization with a single pack to 22 500 ft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["No: above 22 500 ft the APU only provides electrical power","Yes: the envelope allows Bleed Air and Elec Power up to 25 000 ft","Yes, but only with one pack in service and below 41 000 ft","No: above 14 500 ft the APU cannot be started in flight"]},"fig":"apu-envelope"},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0154","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el APU Battery Restart Limit (Elec Emer Config)?","keys":["25000","ft","apu"],"answer":"El límite de rearranque del APU con batería, en configuración eléctrica de emergencia, es 25 000 ft. Por encima de esa altitud no está garantizado el rearranque con batería, aunque la envolvente de operación y rearranque normal llegue hasta 41 000 ft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["25 000 ft","22 500 ft","35 000 ft","41 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the APU Battery Restart Limit (Elec Emer Config)?","keys":["25000","ft","apu"],"answer":"The APU battery restart limit, in emergency electrical configuration, is 25 000 ft. Above that altitude battery restart is not guaranteed, even though the operation and normal restart envelope reaches 41 000 ft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 97 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["25 000 ft","22 500 ft","35 000 ft","41 000 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope"},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0155","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la altitud máxima de uso del APU bleed para asistir el arranque de un motor?","keys":["20000","ft","apu"],"answer":"La altitud máxima del APU bleed para asistir el arranque de motor es 20 000 ft. Este valor es común a los distintos grupos de aviones de la flota. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 99 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["20 000 ft","15 000 ft","22 500 ft","25 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum altitude for APU bleed use to assist engine start?","keys":["20000","ft","apu"],"answer":"The maximum APU bleed altitude to assist engine start is 20 000 ft. This value is common to the different groups of fleet aircraft. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 99 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["20 000 ft","15 000 ft","22 500 ft","25 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"APU","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0156","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre el APU BLEED es FALSA?","keys":["15000","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSA: el FCOM prohíbe sin condiciones el uso del aire de sangrado del APU para el wing anti-ice ('Use of APU bleed air for wing anti-ice is not permitted'). No existe ninguna altitud por debajo de la cual esté permitido. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 99 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["El APU bleed puede utilizarse para el wing anti-ice por debajo de 15 000 ft","La altitud máxima para acondicionamiento y presurización con un solo pack es 22 500 ft","La altitud máxima para acondicionamiento y presurización con los dos packs es 15 000 ft","La altitud máxima para asistir el arranque de motor es 20 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of these statements about the APU BLEED is FALSE?","keys":["15000","ft","apu"],"answer":"FALSE: the FCOM prohibits, without exception, the use of APU bleed air for wing anti-ice ('Use of APU bleed air for wing anti-ice is not permitted'). There is no altitude below which it is allowed. (FCOM LIM-APU · p. 99 · rev 04 JUL 17)","opts":["APU bleed may be used for wing anti-ice below 15 000 ft","The maximum altitude for air conditioning and pressurization with a single pack is 22 500 ft","The maximum altitude for air conditioning and pressurization with both packs is 15 000 ft","The maximum altitude to assist engine start is 20 000 ft"]},"fig":"apu-envelope","mcOnly":1},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0157","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con la Braking Action Computation Function (BACF), ¿a partir de qué pendiente media de pista no deben utilizarse los resultados de la BACF?","keys":["1","bacf","pendiente"],"answer":"Los resultados de la BACF no deben utilizarse en pistas con una pendiente media mayor del 1 %, sea ascendente (uphill) o descendente (downhill). (FCOM LIM-BACF · p. 105 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["Pendiente media mayor del 1 %, tanto ascendente como descendente","Pendiente media mayor del 0,5 %","Pendiente media mayor del 2 %","Pendiente media mayor del 1 %, pero sólo si es descendente"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with the Braking Action Computation Function (BACF), above what mean runway slope must the BACF results not be used?","keys":["1","bacf","slope"],"answer":"The BACF results must not be used on runways with a mean slope greater than 1 %, whether uphill or downhill. (FCOM LIM-BACF · p. 105 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["Mean slope greater than 1 %, both uphill and downhill","Mean slope greater than 0.5 %","Mean slope greater than 2 %","Mean slope greater than 1 %, but only if downhill"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0158","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con la Braking Action Computation Function (BACF), estás en aproximación con un fallo que degrada el sistema de frenos, hacia una pista prácticamente llana. ¿Puedes utilizar los resultados de la BACF?","keys":["bacf","resultados","usarse"],"answer":"La limitación establece dos supuestos independientes en los que los resultados de la BACF no deben usarse: cualquier fallo que afecte a la performance del avión durante el aterrizaje (frenos, motores, aerodinámica...) o pistas con pendiente media mayor del 1 %. Basta con que se dé uno de ellos; aquí el fallo de frenos invalida los resultados aunque la pista sea llana. (FCOM LIM-BACF · p. 105 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["No: los resultados de la BACF no deben usarse ante cualquier fallo que afecte a la performance del avión durante el aterrizaje","Sí: la BACF tiene en cuenta el fallo en su cálculo","Sí, aplicando un margen adicional del 15 % a la distancia calculada","Sí, ya que la pendiente media de la pista es menor del 1 %"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with the Braking Action Computation Function (BACF), you are on approach with a failure that degrades the braking system, towards a virtually flat runway. Can you use the BACF results?","keys":["bacf","failure","results"],"answer":"The limitation sets two independent cases in which the BACF results must not be used: any failure affecting aircraft performance during landing (brakes, engines, aerodynamics...) or runways with a mean slope greater than 1 %. Either one is enough; here the brake failure invalidates the results even though the runway is flat. (FCOM LIM-BACF · p. 105 · rev 26 NOV 19)","opts":["No: the BACF results must not be used with any failure affecting aircraft performance during landing","Yes: the BACF accounts for the failure in its computation","Yes, applying an additional 15 % margin to the computed distance","Yes, since the mean runway slope is less than 1 %"]}},{"sys":"EQUIP","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0159","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿qué exige la limitación sobre el In-Seat Power Supply System (ISPSS) para los dispositivos electrónicos portátiles (PED) de los pasajeros?","keys":["ispss","estar","apagado"],"answer":"La limitación es literal: el ISPSS para los PED que llevan los pasajeros debe estar apagado durante el despegue y el aterrizaje. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["Debe estar apagado durante el despegue y el aterrizaje.","Debe estar apagado únicamente durante el repostaje con pasajeros a bordo.","Debe estar apagado siempre que se vuele por debajo de 10 000 ft.","Puede permanecer encendido en todas las fases si los PED están en modo avión."]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what does the limitation on the In-Seat Power Supply System (ISPSS) require for passengers' portable electronic devices (PED)?","keys":["ispss","off","takeoff"],"answer":"The limitation is literal: the ISPSS for passengers' PEDs must be switched off during takeoff and landing. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["It must be switched off during takeoff and landing.","It must be switched off only during refueling with passengers on board.","It must be switched off whenever flying below 10 000 ft.","It may stay on in all phases if the PEDs are in airplane mode."]}},{"sys":"EQUIP","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0160","es":{"q":"Vuelas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota). Durante la aproximación final, la sobrecargo llama a cabina: un pasajero pide que se reactiven las tomas de corriente del asiento para cargar su portátil antes de llegar. ¿Qué procede según las limitaciones?","keys":["ispss","permanecer","apagado"],"answer":"La limitación cita expresamente el despegue Y el aterrizaje. En aproximación final el avión está en la fase de aterrizaje, así que el ISPSS debe seguir apagado. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["El ISPSS debe permanecer apagado durante el aterrizaje; no se reactiva hasta después.","Se puede reactivar el ISPSS: la limitación sólo aplica al despegue.","Se puede reactivar si el pasajero mantiene el portátil sujeto sobre la mesita.","Se puede reactivar el ISPSS una vez el avión desciende por debajo de 10 000 ft."]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft). During final approach, the purser calls the flight deck: a passenger asks for the in-seat power outlets to be reactivated to charge his laptop before arrival. What is correct according to the limitations?","keys":["ispss","off","landing"],"answer":"The limitation explicitly cites takeoff AND landing. On final approach the aircraft is in the landing phase, so the ISPSS must remain switched off. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["The ISPSS must remain switched off during landing; it is not reactivated until afterwards.","The ISPSS can be reactivated: the limitation only applies to takeoff.","It can be reactivated if the passenger keeps the laptop secured on the tray table.","The ISPSS can be reactivated once the aircraft descends below 10 000 ft."]}},{"sys":"EQUIP","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0161","es":{"q":"¿Cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones sobre el In-Seat Power Supply System (ISPSS) del EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) es FALSA?","keys":["ispss","permanecer","apagado"],"answer":"La limitación acota el apagado a dos fases: despegue y aterrizaje. Fuera de ellas —crucero incluido— el ISPSS puede utilizarse. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["El ISPSS debe permanecer apagado durante todo el vuelo, incluido el crucero.","La limitación se refiere a los dispositivos electrónicos portátiles (PED) que llevan los pasajeros.","El ISPSS debe estar apagado durante el despegue.","El ISPSS debe estar apagado durante el aterrizaje."]},"en":{"q":"Which of the following statements about the In-Seat Power Supply System (ISPSS) of the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) is FALSE?","keys":["ispss","off","takeoff"],"answer":"The limitation restricts the switch-off to two phases: takeoff and landing. Outside them —cruise included— the ISPSS may be used. (FCOM LIM-CAB · p. 111 · rev 22 MAR 17)","opts":["The ISPSS must remain switched off throughout the flight, including cruise.","The limitation refers to passengers' portable electronic devices (PED).","The ISPSS must be switched off during takeoff.","The ISPSS must be switched off during landing."]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"COM","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0162","es":{"q":"¿Por debajo de qué altura está prohibido el uso del GSM Onboard System?","keys":["3000","10000","ft","agl"],"answer":"El uso del GSM Onboard System está prohibido por debajo de 3 000 m AGL (aproximadamente 10 000 ft) y en determinadas áreas geográficas (identificadas en el documento 'Regional Operation Data for the Onboard Mobile Telephony System'). El propio sistema es capaz de identificar esas condiciones y se apaga automáticamente si las detecta. (FCOM LIM-COM · p. 117 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["3 000 m AGL (aproximadamente 10 000 ft)","1 000 m AGL (aproximadamente 3 300 ft)","3 000 ft AGL (aproximadamente 900 m)","10 000 m AGL (aproximadamente 33 000 ft)"]},"en":{"q":"Below what height is the use of the GSM Onboard System prohibited?","keys":["3000","10000","agl"],"answer":"Use of the GSM Onboard System is prohibited below 3 000 m AGL (approximately 10 000 ft) and in certain geographical areas (identified in the document 'Regional Operation Data for the Onboard Mobile Telephony System'). The system itself can identify those conditions and switches off automatically if it detects them. (FCOM LIM-COM · p. 117 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["3 000 m AGL (approximately 10 000 ft)","1 000 m AGL (approximately 3 300 ft)","3 000 ft AGL (approximately 900 m)","10 000 m AGL (approximately 33 000 ft)"]}},{"sys":"COM","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0163","es":{"q":"Según las limitaciones de COMMUNICATION, ¿dónde está prohibido el uso de teléfonos móviles?","keys":["lavabos","cabina","vuelo"],"answer":"El FCOM prohíbe el uso de teléfonos móviles en los lavabos y en la cabina de vuelo. (FCOM LIM-COM · p. 117 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En los lavabos y en la cabina de vuelo (cockpit)","En toda la cabina de pasaje durante todas las fases del vuelo","Únicamente en la cabina de vuelo (cockpit)","Únicamente en los lavabos"]},"en":{"q":"According to the COMMUNICATION limitations, where is the use of mobile phones prohibited?","keys":["lavatories","cockpit","phones"],"answer":"The FCOM prohibits the use of mobile phones in the lavatories and on the flight deck. (FCOM LIM-COM · p. 117 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["In the lavatories and on the flight deck (cockpit)","Throughout the passenger cabin during all flight phases","Only on the flight deck (cockpit)","Only in the lavatories"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0164","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es el límite de EGT para despegue y go-around?","keys":["1083","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"La tabla THRUST SETTING/EGT LIMITS del PW1100G fija 1 083 °C como límite de EGT para Takeoff y Go-around, tanto con todos los motores operativos (5 min) como con un motor inoperativo (10 min). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 083 °C","950 °C","1 043 °C","1 120 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the EGT limit for takeoff and go-around?","keys":["1083","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"The THRUST SETTING/EGT LIMITS table of the PW1100G sets 1 083 °C as the EGT limit for Takeoff and Go-around, both with all engines operative (5 min) and with one engine inoperative (10 min). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 083 °C","950 °C","1 043 °C","1 120 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0165","es":{"q":"Vuelas un A321neo (motores PW1100G) y sufres una falla de motor en el despegue. Con un motor inoperativo aplicas TOGA en el motor bueno. ¿Qué límite de tiempo y de EGT aplican?","keys":["10","1083","min","egt"],"answer":"En la tabla del PW1100G la fila de Takeoff/Go-around distingue el tiempo pero NO el EGT: con un motor inoperativo el límite de tiempo se amplía a 10 min, y el límite de EGT sigue siendo 1 083 °C (la celda de EGT está combinada para ambas filas). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["10 min y 1 083 °C","5 min y 1 083 °C","10 min y 1 043 °C","Sin límite de tiempo y 1 043 °C"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying an A321neo (PW1100G engines) and suffer an engine failure on takeoff. With one engine inoperative you apply TOGA on the good engine. What time and EGT limits apply?","keys":["10","1083","min","egt"],"answer":"In the PW1100G table the Takeoff/Go-around row distinguishes the time but NOT the EGT: with one engine inoperative the time limit extends to 10 min, and the EGT limit remains 1 083 °C (the EGT cell is merged for both rows). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["10 min and 1 083 °C","5 min and 1 083 °C","10 min and 1 043 °C","No time limit and 1 043 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0166","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es el límite de EGT en Maximum Continuous Thrust (MCT)?","keys":["1043","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"El PW1100G limita el EGT en MCT a 1 043 °C, sin límite de tiempo ('Not limited'). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 043 °C","1 083 °C","915 °C","610 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the EGT limit at Maximum Continuous Thrust (MCT)?","keys":["1043","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"The PW1100G limits EGT at MCT to 1 043 °C, with no time limit ('Not limited'). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 043 °C","1 083 °C","915 °C","610 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0167","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es el límite de EGT durante el arranque (Starting), tanto en tierra como en vuelo?","keys":["1083","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"La tabla del PW1100G da un único límite de EGT de arranque, 1 083 °C, aplicable tanto 'On ground' como 'In flight' (la celda de EGT está combinada para las dos filas). Coincide con el límite de despegue. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 083 °C","1 043 °C","725 °C","635 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the EGT limit during Starting, both on the ground and in flight?","keys":["1083","egt","a320neo"],"answer":"The PW1100G table gives a single starting EGT limit, 1 083 °C, applicable both 'On ground' and 'In flight' (the EGT cell is merged for the two rows). It matches the takeoff limit. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 18 MAY 18)","opts":["1 083 °C","1 043 °C","725 °C","635 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0168","es":{"q":"En un A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT para despegue y go-around?","keys":["950","egt","a319"],"answer":"El CFM56 limita el EGT de Takeoff y Go-around a 950 °C (5 min con todos los motores operativos, 10 min con un motor inoperativo). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["950 °C","915 °C","925 °C","1 083 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines, what is the EGT limit for takeoff and go-around?","keys":["950","egt","a319"],"answer":"The CFM56 limits Takeoff and Go-around EGT to 950 °C (5 min with all engines operative, 10 min with one engine inoperative). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["950 °C","915 °C","925 °C","1 083 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0169","es":{"q":"En un A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT en Maximum Continuous Thrust (MCT)?","keys":["915","egt","a319"],"answer":"El CFM56 limita el EGT en MCT a 915 °C, sin límite de tiempo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["915 °C","725 °C","950 °C","1 043 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines, what is the EGT limit at Maximum Continuous Thrust (MCT)?","keys":["915","egt","a319"],"answer":"The CFM56 limits EGT at MCT to 915 °C, with no time limit. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["915 °C","725 °C","950 °C","1 043 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0170","es":{"q":"En un A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT durante el arranque?","keys":["725","egt","a319"],"answer":"El CFM56 limita el EGT de arranque (Starting, en tierra y en vuelo) a 725 °C, muy por debajo de sus límites de despegue (950 °C) y MCT (915 °C). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["725 °C","635 °C","915 °C","950 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines, what is the EGT limit during starting?","keys":["725","egt","a319"],"answer":"The CFM56 limits starting EGT (Starting, on the ground and in flight) to 725 °C, well below its takeoff (950 °C) and MCT (915 °C) limits. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["725 °C","635 °C","915 °C","950 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0171","es":{"q":"En un A320 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT para despegue y go-around?","keys":["635","egt","a320"],"answer":"El A320 con IAE V2500 limita el EGT de Takeoff y Go-around a 635 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["635 °C","725 °C","650 °C","610 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the EGT limit for takeoff and go-around?","keys":["635","egt","a320"],"answer":"The A320 with IAE V2500 limits Takeoff and Go-around EGT to 635 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["635 °C","725 °C","650 °C","610 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0172","es":{"q":"En un A320 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT durante el arranque?","keys":["635","egt","a320"],"answer":"El límite de EGT de arranque del A320 con IAE V2500 es 635 °C, en tierra y en vuelo. Es el mismo valor que su límite de despegue, algo característico de esta familia de motor. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["635 °C","610 °C","650 °C","725 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the EGT limit during starting?","keys":["635","egt","a320"],"answer":"The starting EGT limit of the A320 with IAE V2500 is 635 °C, on the ground and in flight. It is the same value as its takeoff limit, a characteristic of this engine family. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["635 °C","610 °C","650 °C","725 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0173","es":{"q":"En la tabla THRUST SETTING/EGT LIMITS de un A320 con motores IAE V2500, la nota (1) de la fila 'Takeoff' incluye todos estos modos de empuje EXCEPTO:","keys":["toga","tabla","thrust"],"answer":"La nota al pie dice literalmente 'Includes TOGA, FLEX, and DERATE thrust modes': los tres modos comparten el límite de despegue. MCT no es un modo de despegue, es una fila propia de la tabla con su propio límite de EGT (610 °C) y sin límite de tiempo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["MCT","TOGA","FLEX","DERATE"]},"en":{"q":"In the THRUST SETTING/EGT LIMITS table of an A320 with IAE V2500 engines, note (1) of the 'Takeoff' row includes all these thrust modes EXCEPT:","keys":["mct","toga","thrust"],"answer":"The footnote reads literally 'Includes TOGA, FLEX, and DERATE thrust modes': the three modes share the takeoff limit. MCT is not a takeoff mode, it is a row of its own in the table with its own EGT limit (610 °C) and no time limit. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["MCT","TOGA","FLEX","DERATE"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0174","es":{"q":"En un A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56 y todos los motores operativos, ¿cuál es el límite de tiempo en empuje de despegue?","keys":["5","min","cfm56"],"answer":"Con todos los motores operativos el empuje de despegue está limitado a 5 min. Con un motor inoperativo el límite se amplía a 10 min. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["5 min","3 min","10 min","15 min"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines and all engines operative, what is the time limit at takeoff thrust?","keys":["5","min","cfm56"],"answer":"With all engines operative, takeoff thrust is limited to 5 min. With one engine inoperative the limit extends to 10 min. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 123 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["5 min","3 min","10 min","15 min"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0175","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es el N1 máximo?","keys":["100","n1","a320"],"answer":"El bloque SHAFT SPEEDS aplicable al EC-MOG publica un único valor: Maximum N1 100 %. A diferencia de otros grupos, aquí no se distingue entre 'en operación normal' y 'permitido'. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["100 %","104 %","105 %","110 %"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the maximum N1?","keys":["100","n1","a320"],"answer":"The SHAFT SPEEDS block applicable to the EC-MOG publishes a single value: Maximum N1 100 %. Unlike other groups, here there is no distinction between 'in normal operation' and 'permitted'. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 17 NOV 20)","opts":["100 %","104 %","105 %","110 %"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0176","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es el límite de EGT para despegue y go-around?","keys":["650","egt","a321"],"answer":"El A321 con IAE V2500 limita el EGT de Takeoff y Go-around a 650 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["650 °C","610 °C","635 °C","665 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the EGT limit for takeoff and go-around?","keys":["650","egt","a321"],"answer":"The A321 with IAE V2500 limits Takeoff and Go-around EGT to 650 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["650 °C","610 °C","635 °C","665 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0177","es":{"q":"Vuelas indistintamente A320 y A321, ambos con motores IAE V2500. ¿Qué diferencia hay entre sus límites de EGT de despegue?","keys":["321","15","egt"],"answer":"Aunque comparten familia de motor (IAE V2500), el FCOM publica tablas distintas: el A321 con IAE V2500 limita el EGT de despegue a 650 °C y el A320 con IAE V2500 a 635 °C, 15 °C de diferencia. En cambio sus límites de MCT (610 °C) y de arranque (635 °C) sí coinciden. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["El A321 admite 15 °C más (650 °C frente a 635 °C)","Ninguna: ambos limitan a 635 °C","El A320 admite 15 °C más (650 °C frente a 635 °C)","El A321 admite 25 °C más (660 °C frente a 635 °C)"]},"en":{"q":"You fly both the A320 and A321, both with IAE V2500 engines. What is the difference between their takeoff EGT limits?","keys":["321","15","egt"],"answer":"Although they share the same engine family (IAE V2500), the FCOM publishes different tables: the A321 with IAE V2500 limits takeoff EGT to 650 °C and the A320 with IAE V2500 to 635 °C, a 15 °C difference. Their MCT (610 °C) and starting (635 °C) limits do match. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["The A321 allows 15 °C more (650 °C versus 635 °C)","None: both limit to 635 °C","The A320 allows 15 °C more (650 °C versus 635 °C)","The A321 allows 25 °C more (660 °C versus 635 °C)"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0178","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuáles son los límites de EGT de MCT y de arranque, respectivamente?","keys":["610","635","egt"],"answer":"La tabla del A321 con IAE V2500 publica tres valores distintos: 650 °C en despegue/go-around, 610 °C en MCT (sin límite de tiempo) y 635 °C en arranque. Es el único grupo de la flota cuyos tres límites de EGT son diferentes entre sí. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["610 °C y 635 °C","635 °C y 650 °C","610 °C y 650 °C","650 °C y 635 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what are the MCT and starting EGT limits, respectively?","keys":["610","635","egt"],"answer":"The A321 with IAE V2500 table publishes three different values: 650 °C at takeoff/go-around, 610 °C at MCT (no time limit) and 635 °C at starting. It is the only fleet group whose three EGT limits differ from one another. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 124 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["610 °C and 635 °C","635 °C and 650 °C","610 °C and 650 °C","650 °C and 635 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0179","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la presión mínima de aceite?","keys":["60","psi","iae v2500"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 publica una presión mínima de aceite de 60 PSI. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["60 PSI","13 PSI","65 PSI","270 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the minimum oil pressure?","keys":["60","psi","iae v2500"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 publishes a minimum oil pressure of 60 PSI. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["60 PSI","13 PSI","65 PSI","270 PSI"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0180","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la cantidad mínima de aceite?","keys":["11","iae v2500","consumo"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 exige 11 qt más el consumo estimado del vuelo. El FCOM publica un consumo medio estimado de 0.3 qt/h para calcularlo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["11 qt + consumo estimado","9.5 qt + consumo estimado","14 qt + consumo estimado","16.5 qt + consumo estimado"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the minimum oil quantity?","keys":["11","qt","consumption"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 requires 11 qt plus the estimated flight consumption. The FCOM publishes an average estimated consumption of 0.3 qt/h to compute it. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["11 qt + estimated consumption","9.5 qt + estimated consumption","14 qt + estimated consumption","16.5 qt + estimated consumption"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0181","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la temperatura máxima continua de aceite?","keys":["155","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 admite 155 °C de temperatura continua de aceite. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["155 °C","140 °C","151 °C","165 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the maximum continuous oil temperature?","keys":["155","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 allows 155 °C continuous oil temperature. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["155 °C","140 °C","151 °C","165 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0182","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la temperatura máxima transitoria de aceite y durante cuánto tiempo se admite?","keys":["165","15","min","iae v2500"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 admite 165 °C de aceite de forma transitoria durante un máximo de 15 min; por encima de 155 °C (máxima continua) sólo se puede operar dentro de esa ventana. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["165 °C durante 15 min","165 °C durante 5 min","175 °C durante 15 min","155 °C durante 15 min"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the maximum transient oil temperature and for how long is it allowed?","keys":["165","15","min","iae v2500"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 allows 165 °C oil temperature transiently for a maximum of 15 min; above 155 °C (maximum continuous) it can only be operated within that window. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["165 °C for 15 min","165 °C for 5 min","175 °C for 15 min","155 °C for 15 min"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0183","es":{"q":"En crucero en un A320 con motores IAE V2500 observas la temperatura de aceite estabilizada en 160 °C. ¿Cuál es la situación respecto a las limitaciones publicadas?","keys":["15","min","encima"],"answer":"160 °C está por encima de la máxima continua (155 °C) pero por debajo de la máxima transitoria (165 °C), que el FCOM admite durante un máximo de 15 min. No es una condición estabilizable: hay que actuar dentro de esa ventana. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["Está por encima de la máxima continua, en el rango transitorio admitido hasta 15 min","Está dentro de la máxima continua: no hay límite de tiempo","Está dentro de la máxima continua sólo si el motor está en MCT","Está por encima de la máxima transitoria: límite excedido"]},"en":{"q":"In cruise on an A320 with IAE V2500 engines you observe the oil temperature stabilized at 160 °C. What is the situation with respect to the published limitations?","keys":["15","min","above"],"answer":"160 °C is above the maximum continuous (155 °C) but below the maximum transient (165 °C), which the FCOM allows for a maximum of 15 min. It is not a stabilizable condition: you must act within that window. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["It is above the maximum continuous, in the transient range allowed up to 15 min","It is within the maximum continuous: there is no time limit","It is within the maximum continuous only if the engine is at MCT","It is above the maximum transient: limit exceeded"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0184","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la temperatura mínima de aceite para el arranque?","keys":["40","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"La temperatura mínima de aceite para arrancar el IAE V2500 es -40 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["-40 °C","0 °C","-10 °C","-30 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the minimum oil temperature for starting?","keys":["40","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"The minimum oil temperature to start the IAE V2500 is -40 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["-40 °C","0 °C","-10 °C","-30 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0185","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la temperatura mínima de aceite antes del despegue?","keys":["50","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 exige un mínimo de 50 °C de temperatura de aceite antes del despegue. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["50 °C","-10 °C","40 °C","52 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the minimum oil temperature before takeoff?","keys":["50","iae v2500","a320"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 requires a minimum of 50 °C oil temperature before takeoff. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 126 · rev 10 MAY 21)","opts":["50 °C","-10 °C","40 °C","52 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0186","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es la presión mínima de aceite?","keys":["65","psi","pw1100g"],"answer":"El PW1100G publica una presión mínima de aceite de 65 PSI. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["65 PSI","270 PSI","60 PSI","13 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the minimum oil pressure?","keys":["65","psi","pw1100g"],"answer":"The PW1100G publishes a minimum oil pressure of 65 PSI. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["65 PSI","270 PSI","60 PSI","13 PSI"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0187","es":{"q":"¿Cómo se comparan las presiones mínimas de aceite de un A320neo (motores PW1100G) y de un A320 con motores IAE V2500?","keys":["1100","5","psi","pw1100g"],"answer":"El PW1100G exige 65 PSI de presión mínima de aceite y el IAE V2500 exige 60 PSI: el neo es 5 PSI más exigente. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["El PW1100G exige 5 PSI más (65 PSI frente a 60 PSI)","El PW1100G exige 13 PSI y el IAE V2500 60 PSI","El PW1100G exige 5 PSI menos (60 PSI frente a 65 PSI)","Ambos exigen 60 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"How do the minimum oil pressures of an A320neo (PW1100G engines) and an A320 with IAE V2500 engines compare?","keys":["1100","5","psi","pw1100g"],"answer":"The PW1100G requires 65 PSI minimum oil pressure and the IAE V2500 requires 60 PSI: the neo is 5 PSI more demanding. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["The PW1100G requires 5 PSI more (65 PSI versus 60 PSI)","The PW1100G requires 13 PSI and the IAE V2500 60 PSI","The PW1100G requires 5 PSI less (60 PSI versus 65 PSI)","Both require 60 PSI"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0188","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G) con OAT igual o superior a -30 °C, ¿qué cantidad mínima de aceite se exige si el block time máximo previsto es de 14 h?","keys":["14","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"La tabla de OIL QUANTITY del PW1100G exige 14 qt cuando la OAT es igual o superior a -30 °C y el block time máximo es de 14 h. A diferencia del IAE V2500 y el CFM56, aquí la cantidad se lee directamente de la tabla y no se suma consumo estimado. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["14 qt","9.5 qt + consumo estimado","11 qt","16.5 qt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines) with OAT equal to or above -30 °C, what minimum oil quantity is required if the maximum expected block time is 14 h?","keys":["14","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"The PW1100G OIL QUANTITY table requires 14 qt when OAT is equal to or above -30 °C and the maximum block time is 14 h. Unlike the IAE V2500 and the CFM56, here the quantity is read directly from the table and no estimated consumption is added. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["14 qt","9.5 qt + estimated consumption","11 qt","16.5 qt"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0189","es":{"q":"Preparas un A321neo (motores PW1100G) en un aeropuerto con OAT de -35 °C. Según la tabla de OIL QUANTITY, ¿qué cantidad mínima de aceite aplica?","keys":["16.5","pw1100g","preparas"],"answer":"Con OAT por debajo de -30 °C la tabla exige 16.5 qt, sin límite de block time asociado ('Not applicable'). Los 14 qt sólo valen con OAT igual o superior a -30 °C y block time máximo de 14 h. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["16.5 qt","11 qt","14 qt","14 qt + consumo estimado"]},"en":{"q":"You are preparing an A321neo (PW1100G engines) at an airport with an OAT of -35 °C. According to the OIL QUANTITY table, what minimum oil quantity applies?","keys":["16.5","qt","pw1100g"],"answer":"With OAT below -30 °C the table requires 16.5 qt, with no associated block time limit ('Not applicable'). The 14 qt only apply with OAT equal to or above -30 °C and a maximum block time of 14 h. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["16.5 qt","11 qt","14 qt","14 qt + estimated consumption"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0190","es":{"q":"En un A320neo (motores PW1100G) la página ENG del SD indica una cantidad de aceite inferior al mínimo. Según la nota del FCOM, ¿qué puede hacerse antes de considerar el avión no apto?","keys":["pw1100g","comprobar","technical"],"answer":"La nota advierte que un drenaje de aceite del tanque al motor tras el servicio, o un crank/engine run previo al vuelo, pueden producir indicaciones de cantidad reducida en la página ENG del SD. En ese caso el FCOM permite comprobar en el technical logbook que el nivel reportado del tanque está por encima del mínimo, o que el tanque se llenó completamente. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["Comprobar en el technical logbook que el nivel reportado del tanque está por encima del mínimo, o que el tanque se llenó completamente","Aplicar el consumo medio estimado de 0.3 qt/h para corregir la lectura","Arrancar el motor y volver a leer la indicación en marcha","Nada: la indicación del SD es determinante y hay que servir aceite"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo (PW1100G engines) the SD ENG page indicates an oil quantity below the minimum. According to the FCOM note, what can be done before considering the aircraft unserviceable?","keys":["pw1100g","technical","logbook"],"answer":"The note warns that an oil drain from the tank to the engine after servicing, or a crank/engine run before flight, can produce reduced quantity indications on the SD ENG page. In that case the FCOM allows checking in the technical logbook that the reported tank level is above the minimum, or that the tank was completely filled. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["Check in the technical logbook that the reported tank level is above the minimum, or that the tank was completely filled","Apply the average estimated consumption of 0.3 qt/h to correct the reading","Start the engine and read the indication again while running","Nothing: the SD indication is conclusive and oil must be serviced"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0191","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es la temperatura máxima de aceite?","keys":["151","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"El PW1100G publica una única temperatura máxima de aceite: 151 °C. A diferencia del IAE V2500 y del CFM56, no distingue entre máxima continua y máxima transitoria. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["151 °C","165 °C","155 °C","140 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the maximum oil temperature?","keys":["151","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"The PW1100G publishes a single maximum oil temperature: 151 °C. Unlike the IAE V2500 and the CFM56, it does not distinguish between maximum continuous and maximum transient. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["151 °C","165 °C","155 °C","140 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0192","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuál es la temperatura mínima de aceite antes del despegue?","keys":["52","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"El PW1100G exige un mínimo de 52 °C de temperatura de aceite antes del despegue. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["52 °C","-40 °C","-10 °C","50 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), what is the minimum oil temperature before takeoff?","keys":["52","pw1100g","a320neo"],"answer":"The PW1100G requires a minimum of 52 °C oil temperature before takeoff. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["52 °C","-40 °C","-10 °C","50 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0193","es":{"q":"Un día vuelas un A320 con motores IAE V2500 y al siguiente un A320neo (motores PW1100G). ¿Cómo difieren sus temperaturas mínimas de aceite antes del despegue?","keys":["1100","2","pw1100g"],"answer":"El PW1100G exige 52 °C y el IAE V2500 exige 50 °C: 2 °C de diferencia. Ambos comparten la mínima de arranque (-40 °C), pero el neo pide el aceite algo más caliente antes de despegar. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["El PW1100G exige 2 °C más (52 °C frente a 50 °C)","Son idénticas: 50 °C en ambos","El PW1100G exige 2 °C menos (50 °C frente a 52 °C)","El PW1100G no publica mínima antes del despegue"]},"en":{"q":"One day you fly an A320 with IAE V2500 engines and the next an A320neo (PW1100G engines). How do their minimum oil temperatures before takeoff differ?","keys":["1100","2","pw1100g"],"answer":"The PW1100G requires 52 °C and the IAE V2500 requires 50 °C: a 2 °C difference. Both share the minimum for starting (-40 °C), but the neo requires the oil slightly warmer before takeoff. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 127 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["The PW1100G requires 2 °C more (52 °C versus 50 °C)","They are identical: 50 °C on both","The PW1100G requires 2 °C less (50 °C versus 52 °C)","The PW1100G publishes no minimum before takeoff"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0194","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuántos intentos de arranque incluye un ciclo y qué pausa se exige entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra?","keys":["35","pw1100g","intentos"],"answer":"En el PW1100G un arranque automático estándar incluye hasta DOS intentos y cuenta como un ciclo; entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra (automáticos o manuales) se exigen 35 s de pausa. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Hasta dos intentos; 35 s de pausa","Un intento; 15 s de pausa","Hasta tres intentos; 20 s de pausa","Hasta tres intentos; 35 s de pausa"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), how many start attempts does one cycle include and what pause is required between successive cycles on the ground?","keys":["35","pw1100g","attempts"],"answer":"On the PW1100G a standard automatic start includes up to TWO attempts and counts as one cycle; between successive cycles on the ground (automatic or manual) a 35 s pause is required. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["Up to two attempts; 35 s pause","One attempt; 15 s pause","Up to three attempts; 20 s pause","Up to three attempts; 35 s pause"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0195","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuándo se exige un periodo de enfriamiento del arrancador y de cuánto es?","keys":["15","min","pw1100g"],"answer":"El PW1100G exige 15 min de enfriamiento tras tres ciclos fallidos, o tras 15 min de crank continuo o acumulado. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["15 min, tras tres ciclos fallidos o 15 min de crank continuo o acumulado","15 min, tras cuatro ciclos fallidos","30 min, tras tres ciclos fallidos o 4 min de crank continuo","30 min, tras cuatro ciclos fallidos o 5 min de crank acumulado"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), when is a starter cooling period required and how long is it?","keys":["15","min","pw1100g"],"answer":"The PW1100G requires 15 min of cooling after three failed cycles, or after 15 min of continuous or accumulated crank. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 04 JUN 19)","opts":["15 min, after three failed cycles or 15 min of continuous or accumulated crank","15 min, after four failed cycles","30 min, after three failed cycles or 4 min of continuous crank","30 min, after four failed cycles or 5 min of accumulated crank"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0196","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuántos intentos incluye un ciclo de arranque automático estándar y qué pausa se exige entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra?","keys":["15","iae v2500","intento"],"answer":"En el IAE V2500 un arranque automático estándar incluye UN solo intento y eso es un ciclo; entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra se exigen 15 s de pausa. Es el motor más restrictivo de la flota en intentos por ciclo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Un solo intento; 15 s de pausa","Un solo intento; 35 s de pausa","Hasta dos intentos; 15 s de pausa","Hasta tres intentos; 20 s de pausa"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, how many attempts does a standard automatic start cycle include and what pause is required between successive cycles on the ground?","keys":["15","iae v2500","attempt"],"answer":"On the IAE V2500 a standard automatic start includes ONE single attempt and that is one cycle; between successive cycles on the ground a 15 s pause is required. It is the most restrictive engine in the fleet in attempts per cycle. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["One single attempt; 15 s pause","One single attempt; 35 s pause","Up to two attempts; 15 s pause","Up to three attempts; 20 s pause"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0197","es":{"q":"En un A320 con motores IAE V2500, todas estas circunstancias obligan a un periodo de enfriamiento del arrancador de 30 min EXCEPTO:","keys":["iae v2500","ciclos","arranque"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 exige 30 min de enfriamiento tras TRES ciclos fallidos, o tras 4 min de crank continuo, o tras 5 min de crank acumulado. Dos ciclos fallidos no disparan por sí solos el enfriamiento. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Dos ciclos de arranque fallidos","Tres ciclos de arranque fallidos","4 min de crank continuo","5 min de crank acumulado"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 with IAE V2500 engines, all of these circumstances require a 30 min starter cooling period EXCEPT:","keys":["30","min","cycles"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 requires 30 min of cooling after THREE failed cycles, or after 4 min of continuous crank, or after 5 min of accumulated crank. Two failed cycles do not by themselves trigger the cooling. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["Two failed start cycles","Three failed start cycles","4 min of continuous crank","5 min of accumulated crank"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0198","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿por encima de qué N2 no debe accionarse el arrancador?","keys":["10","18","n2"],"answer":"El IAE V2500 es el único motor de la flota que distingue tierra y vuelo: el arrancador no debe accionarse con N2 por encima del 10 % en tierra ni del 18 % en vuelo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["10 % en tierra y 18 % en vuelo","10 % tanto en tierra como en vuelo","20 % tanto en tierra como en vuelo","18 % en tierra y 10 % en vuelo"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines, above what N2 must the starter not be engaged?","keys":["10","18","n2"],"answer":"The IAE V2500 is the only engine in the fleet that distinguishes ground and flight: the starter must not be engaged with N2 above 10 % on the ground or above 18 % in flight. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["10 % on the ground and 18 % in flight","10 % both on the ground and in flight","20 % both on the ground and in flight","18 % on the ground and 10 % in flight"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0199","es":{"q":"En un A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500 y arranque manual, ¿cuál es el tiempo máximo de ciclo?","keys":["2","min","iae v2500"],"answer":"En arranque manual del IAE V2500 no debe excederse el tiempo máximo de ciclo de dos minutos. Es una limitación exclusiva de este motor: ni el CFM56 ni el PW1100G publican un máximo de ciclo para arranque manual. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["2 min","1 min","4 min","5 min"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines and a manual start, what is the maximum cycle time?","keys":["2","min","v2500"],"answer":"On a manual start of the IAE V2500 the maximum cycle time of two minutes must not be exceeded. It is a limitation exclusive to this engine: neither the CFM56 nor the PW1100G publish a maximum cycle time for a manual start. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 06 NOV 23)","opts":["2 min","1 min","4 min","5 min"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0200","es":{"q":"En un A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56, ¿cuántos intentos incluye un ciclo de arranque automático estándar y qué pausa se exige entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra?","keys":["20","cfm56","tres"],"answer":"En el CFM56 un arranque automático estándar incluye hasta TRES intentos y cuenta como un ciclo; entre ciclos sucesivos en tierra se exigen 20 s de pausa. Es el motor más permisivo de la flota en intentos por ciclo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Hasta tres intentos; 20 s de pausa","Un solo intento; 15 s de pausa","Hasta dos intentos; 35 s de pausa","Hasta cuatro intentos; 20 s de pausa"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines, how many attempts does a standard automatic start cycle include, and what pause is required between successive cycles on the ground?","keys":["20","cfm56","three"],"answer":"On the CFM56 a standard automatic start includes up to THREE attempts and counts as one cycle; between successive cycles on the ground a 20 s pause is required. It is the most permissive engine in the fleet in attempts per cycle. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Up to three attempts; 20 s pause","A single attempt; 15 s pause","Up to two attempts; 35 s pause","Up to four attempts; 20 s pause"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0201","es":{"q":"En un A319 con motores CFM56, ¿tras cuántos ciclos fallidos se exige un periodo de enfriamiento, y de cuánto es?","keys":["15","min","cfm56"],"answer":"El CFM56 exige 15 min de enfriamiento tras CUATRO ciclos fallidos. Es el único grupo cuyo umbral son cuatro ciclos, y su bloque no añade condiciones de crank continuo o acumulado. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Cuatro ciclos fallidos; 15 min","Tres ciclos fallidos; 15 min","Tres ciclos fallidos; 30 min","Cuatro ciclos fallidos; 30 min"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319 with CFM56 engines, after how many failed cycles is a cooling period required, and how long is it?","keys":["15","min","cfm56"],"answer":"The CFM56 requires 15 min of cooling after FOUR failed cycles. It is the only engine group whose threshold is four cycles, and its block adds no continuous or accumulated crank conditions. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Four failed cycles; 15 min","Three failed cycles; 15 min","Three failed cycles; 30 min","Four failed cycles; 30 min"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0202","es":{"q":"Un piloto pasa de volar A320 con motores CFM56 a volar A320 con motores IAE V2500. Respecto al N2 por encima del cual no debe accionarse el arrancador en tierra, ¿qué cambia?","keys":["20","10","n2"],"answer":"El CFM56 prohíbe accionar el arrancador con N2 por encima del 20 % (sin distinguir tierra o vuelo), mientras que el IAE V2500 baja el límite al 10 % en tierra (18 % en vuelo). Al cambiar de motor el límite en tierra se reduce a la mitad. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Pasa de 20 % a 10 %: el IAE V2500 es más restrictivo","Nada: ambos limitan al 20 %","Pasa de 10 % a 20 %: el IAE V2500 es más permisivo","Pasa de 20 % a 18 %: el IAE V2500 es ligeramente más restrictivo"]},"en":{"q":"A pilot moves from flying the A320 with CFM56 engines to the A320 with IAE V2500 engines. Regarding the N2 above which the starter must not be engaged on the ground, what changes?","keys":["20","10","n2"],"answer":"The CFM56 prohibits engaging the starter with N2 above 20 % (without distinguishing ground or flight), whereas the IAE V2500 lowers the limit to 10 % on the ground (18 % in flight). When changing engine, the ground limit is halved. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 128 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["It goes from 20 % to 10 %: the IAE V2500 is more restrictive","Nothing: both limit to 20 %","It goes from 10 % to 20 %: the IAE V2500 is more permissive","It goes from 20 % to 18 %: the IAE V2500 is slightly more restrictive"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0203","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la TMAXFLEX?","keys":["42","flex","a321"],"answer":"En el A321 con IAE V2500 la TFLEX no puede ser superior a la TMAXFLEX, igual a ISA + 42 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 43 °C","ISA + 53 °C","ISA + 55 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the TMAXFLEX?","keys":["42","flex","a321"],"answer":"On the A321 with IAE V2500 the TFLEX cannot be higher than the TMAXFLEX, equal to ISA + 42 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 43 °C","ISA + 53 °C","ISA + 55 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0204","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores CFM56, ¿cuál es la TMAXFLEX?","keys":["43","flex","a321"],"answer":"El bloque de FLEXIBLE TAKEOFF de los A321 con motores CFM56 fija la TMAXFLEX en ISA + 43 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["ISA + 43 °C","ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 50 °C","ISA + 60 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with CFM56 engines, what is the TMAXFLEX?","keys":["43","flex","a321"],"answer":"The FLEXIBLE TAKEOFF block for the A321 with CFM56 engines sets the TMAXFLEX at ISA + 43 °C. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["ISA + 43 °C","ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 50 °C","ISA + 60 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0205","es":{"q":"Vueling opera A321 con motores IAE V2500 y A321 con motores CFM56. ¿Qué diferencia hay entre sus TMAXFLEX?","keys":["321","56","flex"],"answer":"El A321 con IAE V2500 tiene TMAXFLEX de ISA + 42 °C y el A321 con CFM56 de ISA + 43 °C: sólo 1 °C de diferencia, pero son bloques distintos del FCOM. El mismo modelo de avión tiene TMAXFLEX distinta según el motor. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["El A321 con CFM56 admite 1 °C más (ISA + 43 °C frente a ISA + 42 °C)","Ninguna: ambos ISA + 42 °C","El A321 con CFM56 admite 1 °C menos (ISA + 42 °C frente a ISA + 43 °C)","El A321 con CFM56 admite 13 °C más (ISA + 55 °C frente a ISA + 42 °C)"]},"en":{"q":"Vueling operates A321s with IAE V2500 engines and A321s with CFM56 engines. What is the difference between their TMAXFLEX values?","keys":["321","56","flex"],"answer":"The A321 with IAE V2500 has a TMAXFLEX of ISA + 42 °C and the A321 with CFM56 of ISA + 43 °C: only 1 °C of difference, but they are different FCOM blocks. The same aircraft model has a different TMAXFLEX depending on the engine. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["The A321 with CFM56 allows 1 °C more (ISA + 43 °C versus ISA + 42 °C)","None: both ISA + 42 °C","The A321 with CFM56 allows 1 °C less (ISA + 42 °C versus ISA + 43 °C)","The A321 with CFM56 allows 13 °C more (ISA + 55 °C versus ISA + 42 °C)"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0206","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿está permitido el despegue FLEX en pista contaminada?","keys":["flex","despegue","permitido"],"answer":"'FLEX takeoff is not permitted on contaminated runways'. Es una prohibición sin excepciones. En pista contaminada sí se puede usar despegue con derate, que está permitido con cualquier estado de pista. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["No: el despegue FLEX no está permitido en pista contaminada","Sí, sin restricciones","Sí, si se aplica el déficit de performance correspondiente","Sí, siempre que la TFLEX no supere ISA + 42 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, is a FLEX takeoff permitted on a contaminated runway?","keys":["flex","contaminated","permitted"],"answer":"'FLEX takeoff is not permitted on contaminated runways'. It is a prohibition without exceptions. On a contaminated runway a derated takeoff may be used, which is permitted with any runway state. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["No: a FLEX takeoff is not permitted on a contaminated runway","Yes, without restrictions","Yes, if the corresponding performance shortfall is applied","Yes, provided the TFLEX does not exceed ISA + 42 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0207","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, la TFLEX no puede ser ninguna de estas cosas EXCEPTO:","keys":["flex","superior","real"],"answer":"El FCOM prohíbe tres cosas: TFLEX superior a TMAXFLEX, inferior a TREF e inferior a la OAT real. Que la TFLEX sea SUPERIOR a la OAT real no sólo está permitido: es justamente el fundamento del despegue FLEX (se declara una temperatura más alta que la real para reducir el empuje). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Superior a la OAT real","Inferior a la flat temperature (TREF)","Inferior a la OAT real","Superior a TMAXFLEX (ISA + 42 °C)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, the TFLEX cannot be any of these things EXCEPT:","keys":["flex","higher","oat"],"answer":"The FCOM prohibits three things: TFLEX higher than TMAXFLEX, lower than TREF, and lower than the actual OAT. That the TFLEX is HIGHER than the actual OAT is not only permitted: it is precisely the basis of the FLEX takeoff (a temperature higher than the actual one is declared to reduce thrust). (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Higher than the actual OAT","Lower than the flat temperature (TREF)","Lower than the actual OAT","Higher than TMAXFLEX (ISA + 42 °C)"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0208","es":{"q":"Sales con un A321 con motores CFM56 con un elemento inoperativo que afecta a la performance de despegue. ¿Puedes hacer un despegue con empuje reducido (flexible)?","keys":["flex","siempre","haya"],"answer":"El FCOM lo permite expresamente: 'Takeoff at reduced thrust is permitted with any inoperative item affecting the performance only if the associated performance shortfall has been applied to meet the above requirements'. La condición es haber aplicado el déficit de performance para seguir cumpliendo los requisitos al peso de despegue. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["Sí, siempre que se haya aplicado el déficit de performance asociado y se sigan cumpliendo los requisitos de performance al peso de despegue","No: con cualquier elemento inoperativo el despegue flexible queda prohibido","Sí, sin condiciones: el despacho bajo MEL ya garantiza la performance","Sólo si además la pista está seca y la TFLEX es inferior a la OAT real"]},"en":{"q":"You are departing an A321 with CFM56 engines with an inoperative item affecting takeoff performance. Can you make a reduced-thrust (flexible) takeoff?","keys":["flex","shortfall","permitted"],"answer":"The FCOM expressly permits it: 'Takeoff at reduced thrust is permitted with any inoperative item affecting the performance only if the associated performance shortfall has been applied to meet the above requirements'. The condition is having applied the performance shortfall to keep meeting the requirements at the takeoff weight. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 03 MAY 23)","opts":["Yes, provided the associated performance shortfall has been applied and the performance requirements at the takeoff weight are still met","No: with any inoperative item the flexible takeoff is prohibited","Yes, unconditionally: dispatch under MEL already guarantees performance","Only if in addition the runway is dry and the TFLEX is lower than the actual OAT"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0209","es":{"q":"¿Por debajo de qué velocidad no debería usarse la reversa máxima?","keys":["70","kt","debajo"],"answer":"La reversa máxima no debería usarse por debajo de 70 kt. La reversa a IDLE sí está permitida hasta la parada completa del avión. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["70 kt","100 kt","80 kt","60 kt"]},"en":{"q":"Below what speed should maximum reverse not be used?","keys":["70","kt","reverse"],"answer":"Maximum reverse should not be used below 70 kt. IDLE reverse is permitted down to the complete stop of the aircraft. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["70 kt","100 kt","80 kt","60 kt"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0210","es":{"q":"Sobre las limitaciones de reversa, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["retroceder","avion","reversa"],"answer":"El FCOM prohíbe sin condiciones retroceder el avión con reversa ('Backing the aircraft with reverse thrust is not permitted'). No hay excepción por peso ni por ninguna otra circunstancia. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Retroceder el avión con reversa está permitido si el peso está por debajo del MLW","La selección de reversa está prohibida en vuelo","Retroceder el avión con reversa no está permitido","La reversa IDLE está permitida hasta la parada del avión"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the reverse limitations, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["backing","aircraft","reverse"],"answer":"The FCOM prohibits without conditions backing the aircraft with reverse ('Backing the aircraft with reverse thrust is not permitted'). There is no exception for weight or any other circumstance. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 129 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Backing the aircraft with reverse thrust is permitted if the weight is below MLW","Reverse selection is prohibited in flight","Backing the aircraft with reverse thrust is not permitted","IDLE reverse is permitted down to the aircraft stop"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0211","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál es la TMAXFLEX?","keys":["55","flex","a320"],"answer":"El bloque de FLEX TAKEOFF aplicable al EC-MOG fija la TMAXFLEX en ISA + 55 °C. La TMAXFLEX se certifica por avión concreto: no existe 'la TMAXFLEX del A320', ni siquiera dentro de la misma familia de motor. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 131 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["ISA + 55 °C","ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 50 °C","ISA + 60 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what is the TMAXFLEX?","keys":["55","flex","a320"],"answer":"The FLEX TAKEOFF block applicable to the EC-MOG sets the TMAXFLEX at ISA + 55 °C. The TMAXFLEX is certified aircraft by aircraft: there is no 'TMAXFLEX of the A320', not even within the same engine family. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 131 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["ISA + 55 °C","ISA + 42 °C","ISA + 50 °C","ISA + 60 °C"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0212","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿hasta qué viento cruzado es capaz de arrancar el motor?","keys":["35","kt","pw1100g"],"answer":"El bloque CROSSWIND OPERATION ON GROUND del PW1100G indica que el motor es capaz de arrancar con viento cruzado de hasta 35 kt. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["35 kt","25 kt","30 kt","40 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), up to what crosswind is the engine able to start?","keys":["35","kt","pw1100g"],"answer":"The CROSSWIND OPERATION ON GROUND block for the PW1100G states that the engine is able to start with a crosswind of up to 35 kt. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["35 kt","25 kt","30 kt","40 kt"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0213","es":{"q":"Durante un despegue con derate, ¿cuándo está permitido seleccionar empuje TOGA?","keys":["toga","requiera","procedimiento"],"answer":"La selección de TOGA no está permitida en un despegue con derate, EXCEPTO cuando lo requiera un procedimiento anormal o de emergencia. El motivo es que el derate se calcula sobre una VMCG asociada al empuje reducido: aplicar TOGA podría dejar el avión sin control direccional garantizado en tierra. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Sólo cuando lo requiera un procedimiento anormal o de emergencia","Nunca, bajo ninguna circunstancia","Siempre que el comandante lo considere necesario","Sólo por encima de la altitud de aceleración"]},"en":{"q":"During a derated takeoff, when is the selection of TOGA thrust permitted?","keys":["toga","required","procedure"],"answer":"The selection of TOGA is not permitted on a derated takeoff, EXCEPT when required by an abnormal or emergency procedure. The reason is that the derate is computed on a VMCG associated with the reduced thrust: applying TOGA could leave the aircraft without guaranteed directional control on the ground. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Only when required by an abnormal or emergency procedure","Never, under any circumstances","Whenever the captain considers it necessary","Only above the acceleration altitude"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0214","es":{"q":"¿Está permitido combinar despegue con empuje reducido (FLEX) y despegue con derate?","keys":["flex","permitido","asociacion"],"answer":"'The use of reduced thrust takeoff (FLEX takeoff) is not permitted in association with derated takeoff'. Son dos métodos de reducción de empuje mutuamente excluyentes: o FLEX o derate. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["No: el uso de FLEX no está permitido en asociación con el derate","Sí, es la técnica habitual para maximizar el ahorro de motor","Sí, pero sólo en pista seca","Sí, siempre que la TFLEX no supere la TMAXFLEX"]},"en":{"q":"Is it permitted to combine a reduced-thrust takeoff (FLEX) and a derated takeoff?","keys":["flex","derate","permitted"],"answer":"'The use of reduced thrust takeoff (FLEX takeoff) is not permitted in association with derated takeoff'. They are two mutually exclusive thrust-reduction methods: either FLEX or derate. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["No: the use of FLEX is not permitted in association with derate","Yes, it is the usual technique to maximise engine savings","Yes, but only on a dry runway","Yes, provided the TFLEX does not exceed the TMAXFLEX"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0215","es":{"q":"Sales de una pista contaminada por nieve. ¿Qué método de reducción de empuje puedes emplear en el despegue?","keys":["derate","permitido","cualquier"],"answer":"El derate está permitido con independencia del estado de la pista (seca, mojada o contaminada), mientras que el FLEX está prohibido en pista contaminada. Por eso el derate es el método utilizable en esa situación. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Derate, que está permitido con cualquier estado de pista","FLEX, porque cumples los requisitos de performance al peso de despegue","Ninguno: en pista contaminada hay que despegar siempre con TOGA","FLEX combinado con derate, para compensar el estado de la pista"]},"en":{"q":"You are departing a runway contaminated by snow. What thrust-reduction method may you use for takeoff?","keys":["derate","permitted","runway"],"answer":"The derate is permitted regardless of the runway state (dry, wet or contaminated), whereas FLEX is prohibited on a contaminated runway. That is why the derate is the usable method in that situation. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 132 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Derate, which is permitted with any runway state","FLEX, because you meet the performance requirements at the takeoff weight","None: on a contaminated runway you must always take off with TOGA","FLEX combined with derate, to compensate for the runway state"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0216","es":{"q":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre el viento cruzado hasta el que es capaz de arrancar el motor de un A320neo (PW1100G) y el de un A320 con motores IAE V2500?","keys":["35","kt","ninguna"],"answer":"Los dos bloques de CROSSWIND OPERATION ON GROUND publican el mismo valor: el motor es capaz de arrancar con viento cruzado de hasta 35 kt, tanto en el PW1100G como en el IAE V2500. Es un caso en que la familia de motor no cambia la limitación. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["Ninguna: ambos hasta 35 kt","El PW1100G llega a 35 kt y el IAE V2500 sólo a 30 kt","El IAE V2500 llega a 35 kt y el PW1100G sólo a 25 kt","El PW1100G llega a 40 kt y el IAE V2500 a 35 kt"]},"en":{"q":"What is the difference between the crosswind up to which an A320neo (PW1100G) engine is able to start and that of an A320 with IAE V2500 engines?","keys":["35","kt","crosswind"],"answer":"Both CROSSWIND OPERATION ON GROUND blocks publish the same value: the engine is able to start with a crosswind of up to 35 kt, both on the PW1100G and on the IAE V2500. It is a case where the engine family does not change the limitation. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 20 MAR 17)","opts":["None: both up to 35 kt","The PW1100G reaches 35 kt and the IAE V2500 only 30 kt","The IAE V2500 reaches 35 kt and the PW1100G only 25 kt","The PW1100G reaches 40 kt and the IAE V2500 35 kt"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0217","es":{"q":"En un A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G), ¿cuándo está prohibido el uso del modo GA SOFT?","keys":["ga soft","motor","inoperativo"],"answer":"'The use of GA SOFT mode is prohibited with one engine inoperative'. Con un motor inoperativo se necesita todo el empuje disponible, así que el modo suave de go-around queda prohibido. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 04 DEC 17)","opts":["Con un motor inoperativo","Por encima de ISA + 42 °C","En pista contaminada","Con viento cruzado superior a 35 kt"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines), when is the use of GA SOFT mode prohibited?","keys":["ga soft","engine","inoperative"],"answer":"'The use of GA SOFT mode is prohibited with one engine inoperative'. With one engine inoperative all available thrust is needed, so the soft go-around mode is prohibited. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 04 DEC 17)","opts":["With one engine inoperative","Above ISA + 42 °C","On a contaminated runway","With a crosswind above 35 kt"]}},{"sys":"ENG","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0218","es":{"q":"¿En qué aviones de la flota publica el FCOM la limitación del modo GA SOFT?","keys":["320","321","ga soft"],"answer":"El bloque SOFT GO-AROUND del capítulo LIM-ENG sólo existe para los A320neo / A321neo con motores PW1100G, donde prohíbe el GA SOFT con un motor inoperativo. Ni los CFM56 ni los IAE V2500 tienen bloque de SOFT GO-AROUND en este capítulo. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 04 DEC 17)","opts":["Sólo en los A320neo / A321neo (motores PW1100G)","En toda la flota A319/A320/A321","Sólo en los A319 / A320 / A321 con motores CFM56","Sólo en los A320 / A321 con motores IAE V2500"]},"en":{"q":"On which fleet aircraft does the FCOM publish the GA SOFT mode limitation?","keys":["320","321","ga soft"],"answer":"The SOFT GO-AROUND block of the LIM-ENG chapter exists only for the A320neo / A321neo with PW1100G engines, where it prohibits GA SOFT with one engine inoperative. Neither the CFM56 nor the IAE V2500 have a SOFT GO-AROUND block in this chapter. (FCOM LIM-ENG · p. 133 · rev 04 DEC 17)","opts":["Only on the A320neo / A321neo (PW1100G engines)","On the entire A319/A320/A321 fleet","Only on the A319 / A320 / A321 with CFM56 engines","Only on the A320 / A321 with IAE V2500 engines"]}},{"sys":"FCTL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0219","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la altitud máxima de operación con slats y/o flaps extendidos?","keys":["20000","ft","altitud"],"answer":"La altitud máxima de operación con slats y/o flaps extendidos es 20 000 ft. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 000 ft","15 000 ft","18 000 ft","25 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum operating altitude with slats and/or flaps extended?","keys":["20000","ft","altitude"],"answer":"The maximum operating altitude with slats and/or flaps extended is 20 000 ft. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["20 000 ft","15 000 ft","18 000 ft","25 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"FCTL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0220","es":{"q":"En una espera prolongada el ATC te mantiene en FL220 y valoras extender CONF 1 para reducir velocidad. ¿Es admisible según las limitaciones?","keys":["20000","ft","vfe"],"answer":"Existe una limitación de altitud independiente de la velocidad: la altitud máxima de operación con slats y/o flaps extendidos es 20 000 ft. En FL220 se estaría por encima de ese límite, así que no procede extender CONF 1 aunque la velocidad sea inferior a VFE. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: la altitud máxima de operación con slats y/o flaps extendidos es 20 000 ft","Sí, siempre que se respete la VFE de CONF 1","Sí, hasta FL250 con CONF 1","Sí, siempre que el A/P esté desconectado"]},"en":{"q":"On a prolonged hold ATC keeps you at FL220 and you consider extending CONF 1 to reduce speed. Is it acceptable according to the limitations?","keys":["20000","ft","vfe"],"answer":"There is an altitude limitation independent of speed: the maximum operating altitude with slats and/or flaps extended is 20 000 ft. At FL220 you would be above that limit, so extending CONF 1 is not appropriate even if the speed is below VFE. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No: the maximum operating altitude with slats and/or flaps extended is 20 000 ft","Yes, provided the CONF 1 VFE is respected","Yes, up to FL250 with CONF 1","Yes, provided the A/P is disconnected"]}},{"sys":"FCTL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0221","es":{"q":"Sobre el uso de los mandos de vuelo (CAUTION del capítulo), ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["caution","debajo","entradas"],"answer":"La CAUTION advierte de que entradas de mando rápidas y amplias alternadas, especialmente combinadas con grandes cambios de cabeceo, balance o guiñada (p. ej. grandes ángulos de resbalamiento), pueden provocar fallos estructurales A CUALQUIER VELOCIDAD. Estar por debajo de VMO no protege frente a ese riesgo. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Por debajo de la VMO las entradas de mando alternadas no pueden provocar fallo estructural","Entradas de mando rápidas, amplias y alternadas pueden provocar fallos estructurales","El riesgo aumenta si se combinan con grandes cambios de cabeceo, balance o guiñada","Los grandes ángulos de resbalamiento (sideslip) son un ejemplo de esos grandes cambios"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the use of the flight controls (chapter CAUTION), which of the following statements is FALSE?","keys":["caution","below","inputs"],"answer":"The CAUTION warns that rapid and large alternating control inputs, especially combined with large changes in pitch, roll or yaw (e.g. large sideslip angles), can cause structural failures AT ANY SPEED. Being below VMO does not protect against that risk. (FCOM LIM-F_CTL · p. 139 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Below VMO, alternating control inputs cannot cause structural failure","Rapid, large and alternating control inputs can cause structural failures","The risk increases if combined with large changes in pitch, roll or yaw","Large sideslip angles are an example of those large changes"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0222","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320/A321 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), ¿con qué combustibles está certificado el sistema de combustible?","keys":["1","4","jet a1"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que en los CEO el sistema de combustible está certificado con nueve especificaciones: JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1, de acuerdo con los fabricantes de motores y las especificaciones de combustible. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5 y JP8 únicamente","JET A1, JP8 y N° 3 JET únicamente"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320/A321 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), which fuels is the fuel system certified with?","keys":["jet a1","jp4","ts-1"],"answer":"The FCOM indicates that on the CEO the fuel system is certified with nine specifications: JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1, in accordance with the engine manufacturers and the fuel specifications. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5 and JP8 only","JET A1, JP8 and N° 3 JET only"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0223","es":{"q":"¿En qué aviones de la flota está certificado el sistema de combustible con JET B y JP4?","keys":["319","320","jet b"],"answer":"La lista de combustibles certificados de los CEO incluye JET B y JP4, mientras que la de los A320neo/A321neo con PW1100G sólo recoge JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1: en los neo no aparecen ni JET B ni JP4. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En los A319/A320/A321 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), pero no en los neo con PW1100G","En toda la flota, sin distinción","Sólo en los A320neo/A321neo con motores PW1100G","Sólo en los A321 con motores IAE V2500"]},"en":{"q":"On which fleet aircraft is the fuel system certified with JET B and JP4?","keys":["319","320","jet b"],"answer":"The list of certified fuels of the CEO includes JET B and JP4, whereas that of the A320neo/A321neo with PW1100G only lists JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1: on the neo neither JET B nor JP4 appear. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["On the A319/A320/A321 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), but not on the neo with PW1100G","On the entire fleet, without distinction","Only on the A320neo/A321neo with PW1100G engines","Only on the A321 with IAE V2500 engines"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0224","es":{"q":"En un A320neo/A321neo con motores PW1100G, ¿con qué combustibles está certificado el sistema de combustible?","keys":["1","5","pw1100g"],"answer":"En los neo con PW1100G el sistema está certificado con siete especificaciones: JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1. JET B y JP4 no figuran en su lista. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1","Únicamente JET A1 y JET A","JET A, JET A1, JP4, JP5, JP8 y RT"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo/A321neo with PW1100G engines, which fuels is the fuel system certified with?","keys":["pw1100g","jp5","seven"],"answer":"On the neo with PW1100G the system is certified with seven specifications: JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1. JET B and JP4 are not on its list. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1","JET A, JET A1, JET B, JP4, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1","JET A1 and JET A only","JET A, JET A1, JP4, JP5, JP8 and RT"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0225","es":{"q":"Estás en una escala con un A320neo (motores PW1100G) y el suministrador local sólo dispone de JP4. ¿Qué establece el FCOM?","keys":["4","jp4","figura"],"answer":"En los A320neo/A321neo con PW1100G el sistema está certificado únicamente con JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT y TS-1. El JP4 no aparece en esa lista, por lo que no es un combustible certificado para ese avión. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El JP4 no figura entre los combustibles certificados de ese avión","Se puede repostar JP4 sin restricciones, igual que en los CEO","Se puede repostar JP4 siempre que la temperatura del combustible se mantenga por debajo de 49 °C","Se puede repostar JP4 sólo si se mezcla con JET A1 en proporción máxima del 50 %"]},"en":{"q":"You are at a stopover with an A320neo (PW1100G engines) and the local supplier only has JP4. What does the FCOM establish?","keys":["jp4","pw1100g","certified"],"answer":"On the A320neo/A321neo with PW1100G the system is certified only with JET A, JET A1, JP5, JP8, N° 3 JET, RT and TS-1. JP4 does not appear on that list, so it is not a certified fuel for that aircraft. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["JP4 is not among the certified fuels of that aircraft","JP4 can be refuelled without restrictions, just as on the CEO","JP4 can be refuelled provided the fuel temperature stays below 49 °C","JP4 can be refuelled only if mixed with JET A1 in a maximum proportion of 50 %"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0226","es":{"q":"Respecto a la mezcla de tipos de combustible, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA según el FCOM?","keys":["50","mini","mezcla"],"answer":"La nota del FCOM dice que los distintos tipos de combustible pueden mezclarse en todas las proporciones y que, en caso de mezcla, los valores MINI de la tabla dejan de ser aplicables. No existe ningún límite del 50 %: esa afirmación es la falsa. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["La mezcla sólo se permite hasta un máximo del 50 % del combustible de menor especificación","Los distintos tipos de combustible se pueden mezclar en todas las proporciones","En caso de mezcla, los valores mínimos de especificación de la tabla dejan de ser aplicables","La nota sobre la mezcla acompaña a la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the mixing of fuel types, which of these statements is FALSE according to the FCOM?","keys":["50","mini","mixed"],"answer":"The FCOM note says that the different fuel types may be mixed in all proportions and that, in case of mixing, the MINI values of the table are no longer applicable. There is no 50 % limit: that statement is the false one. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["Mixing is only permitted up to a maximum of 50 % of the lower-specification fuel","The different fuel types may be mixed in all proportions","In case of mixing, the minimum specification values of the table are no longer applicable","The note on mixing accompanies the FUEL TEMPERATURE table"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0227","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), ¿cuál es la temperatura MÍNIMA de combustible con JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET?","keys":["43","mini","a319"],"answer":"La tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE fija la MINI en -43 °C para la columna JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["-43 °C","-36 °C","-45 °C","-54 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), what is the MINIMUM fuel temperature with JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET?","keys":["43","mini","a319"],"answer":"The FUEL TEMPERATURE table sets the MINI at -43 °C for the JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET column. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["-43 °C","-36 °C","-45 °C","-54 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0228","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), ¿cuál de estas temperaturas MÍNIMAS de combustible es FALSA según la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE?","keys":["42","mini","a319"],"answer":"La MINI de JET B es -46 °C, no -42 °C. Los -42 °C corresponden a la columna JP5. El resto de valores de la tabla (RT y TS-1 a -45 °C, JP4 a -54 °C) son correctos. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["JET B: -42 °C","JP5: -42 °C","RT y TS-1: -45 °C","JP4: -54 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), which of these MINIMUM fuel temperatures is FALSE according to the FUEL TEMPERATURE table?","keys":["42","mini","a319"],"answer":"The MINI of JET B is -46 °C, not -42 °C. The -42 °C corresponds to the JP5 column. The rest of the table values (RT and TS-1 at -45 °C, JP4 at -54 °C) are correct. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["JET B: -42 °C","JP5: -42 °C","RT and TS-1: -45 °C","JP4: -54 °C"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0229","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) operando con JET A1, ¿cuál es la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible?","keys":["54","maxi","a319"],"answer":"La fila MAXI de la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE marca 54 °C para las columnas JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT y TS-1. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["54 °C","49 °C","55 °C","30 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) operating with JET A1, what is the MAXIMUM fuel temperature?","keys":["54","maxi","a319"],"answer":"The MAXI row of the FUEL TEMPERATURE table marks 54 °C for the JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT and TS-1 columns. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["54 °C","49 °C","55 °C","30 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0230","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500), la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible es de 54 °C con todas las especificaciones siguientes EXCEPTO...","keys":["4","maxi","a319"],"answer":"La fila MAXI de esta tabla está partida: 54 °C abarca JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT y TS-1, mientras que para JET B y JP4 la máxima baja a 49 °C. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["JET B y JP4","JET A y JP5","RT y TS-1","JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines), the MAXIMUM fuel temperature is 54 °C with all of the following specifications EXCEPT...","keys":["49","maxi","a319"],"answer":"The MAXI row of this table is split: 54 °C covers JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT and TS-1, whereas for JET B and JP4 the maximum drops to 49 °C. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["JET B and JP4","JET A and JP5","RT and TS-1","JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0231","es":{"q":"Vas a operar un A319/A320 CEO (motores CFM56 o IAE V2500) repostado con JET B en un aeropuerto muy caluroso. ¿Qué temperatura máxima de combustible no debes superar?","keys":["49","maxi","operar"],"answer":"Con JET B (y con JP4) la fila MAXI de la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE de este grupo baja a 49 °C, frente a los 54 °C del resto de especificaciones. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["49 °C","54 °C, igual que con JET A1","55 °C","40 °C"]},"en":{"q":"You are going to operate an A319/A320 CEO (CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines) refuelled with JET B at a very hot airport. What maximum fuel temperature must you not exceed?","keys":["49","maxi","jet b"],"answer":"With JET B (and with JP4) the MAXI row of the FUEL TEMPERATURE table of this group drops to 49 °C, versus the 54 °C of the other specifications. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["49 °C","54 °C, same as with JET A1","55 °C","40 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0232","es":{"q":"La nota (1) de la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE, asociada a la columna JET A, ¿qué exige?","keys":["34","36","jet a"],"answer":"La nota dice literalmente que sólo para JET A, si la TAT alcanza -34 °C, hay que vigilar la temperatura del combustible en la página FUEL del SD para asegurar que permanece por encima de -36 °C (la MINI de esa columna). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["Si la TAT alcanza -34 °C, vigilar la temperatura del combustible en la página FUEL del SD para asegurar que se mantiene por encima de -36 °C","Si la TAT alcanza -36 °C, vigilar la temperatura del combustible en la página FUEL del SD para asegurar que se mantiene por encima de -43 °C","Si la temperatura del combustible alcanza -34 °C, iniciar descenso inmediato","Si la TAT alcanza -34 °C, limitar la altitud a 35 000 ft"]},"en":{"q":"Note (1) of the FUEL TEMPERATURE table, associated with the JET A column, what does it require?","keys":["34","36","jet a"],"answer":"The note states literally that only for JET A, if the TAT reaches -34 °C, the fuel temperature must be monitored on the SD FUEL page to ensure it remains above -36 °C (the MINI of that column). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["If the TAT reaches -34 °C, monitor the fuel temperature on the SD FUEL page to ensure it stays above -36 °C","If the TAT reaches -36 °C, monitor the fuel temperature on the SD FUEL page to ensure it stays above -43 °C","If the fuel temperature reaches -34 °C, initiate an immediate descent","If the TAT reaches -34 °C, limit the altitude to 35 000 ft"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0233","es":{"q":"Vuelas en crucero con JET A a bordo y la TAT alcanza -34 °C. ¿Qué establece el FCOM?","keys":["36","jet a","vigilar"],"answer":"La nota (1) de la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE, aplicable sólo al JET A, exige que al alcanzar la TAT los -34 °C se vigile la temperatura del combustible en la página FUEL del SD, asegurando que no baja de -36 °C, que es su MINI. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["Vigilar la temperatura del combustible en la página FUEL del SD y asegurar que se mantiene por encima de -36 °C","Nada especial: -34 °C de TAT no es un valor relevante para el JET A","Aumentar el Mach para elevar la TAT por encima de -34 °C","Vigilar la temperatura del combustible y asegurar que se mantiene por encima de -45 °C"]},"en":{"q":"You are cruising with JET A on board and the TAT reaches -34 °C. What does the FCOM establish?","keys":["36","jet a","monitor"],"answer":"Note (1) of the FUEL TEMPERATURE table, applicable only to JET A, requires that when the TAT reaches -34 °C the fuel temperature be monitored on the SD FUEL page, ensuring it does not drop below -36 °C, which is its MINI. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 145 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["Monitor the fuel temperature on the SD FUEL page and ensure it stays above -36 °C","Nothing special: -34 °C TAT is not a relevant value for JET A","Increase the Mach to raise the TAT above -34 °C","Monitor the fuel temperature and ensure it stays above -45 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0234","es":{"q":"En un A320neo/A321neo con motores PW1100G, ¿cuál es la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible?","keys":["55","maxi","a320neo"],"answer":"La tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE de los neo con PW1100G tiene una única celda MAXI de 55 °C que abarca las cinco columnas certificadas (JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT y TS-1). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["55 °C","49 °C","54 °C","60 °C"]},"en":{"q":"On an A320neo/A321neo with PW1100G engines, what is the MAXIMUM fuel temperature?","keys":["55","maxi","a320neo"],"answer":"The FUEL TEMPERATURE table of the neo with PW1100G has a single MAXI cell of 55 °C covering the five certified columns (JET A1/JP8/N° 3 JET, JET A, JP5, RT and TS-1). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["55 °C","49 °C","54 °C","60 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0235","es":{"q":"¿Cómo es la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible de un A320neo/A321neo (PW1100G) frente a la de un A321 con motores IAE V2500?","keys":["1","55","maxi"],"answer":"La tabla de los neo con PW1100G fija la MAXI en 55 °C, mientras que la del A321 con IAE V2500 la fija en 54 °C para las siete columnas de su tabla. La diferencia es de 1 °C a favor del neo. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["Es 1 °C mayor en el neo (55 °C frente a 54 °C)","Es idéntica en ambos (54 °C)","Es 5 °C menor en el neo (49 °C frente a 54 °C)","Es 2 °C mayor en el neo (55 °C frente a 53 °C)"]},"en":{"q":"How does the MAXIMUM fuel temperature of an A320neo/A321neo (PW1100G) compare with that of an A321 with IAE V2500 engines?","keys":["1","55","maxi"],"answer":"The table of the neo with PW1100G sets the MAXI at 55 °C, whereas that of the A321 with IAE V2500 sets it at 54 °C for the seven columns of its table. The difference is 1 °C in favour of the neo. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["It is 1 °C higher on the neo (55 °C versus 54 °C)","It is identical on both (54 °C)","It is 5 °C lower on the neo (49 °C versus 54 °C)","It is 2 °C higher on the neo (55 °C versus 53 °C)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0236","es":{"q":"En un A321 con motores IAE V2500, ¿cuál es la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible?","keys":["54","maxi","todas"],"answer":"En la tabla de FUEL TEMPERATURE del A321 con IAE V2500 la celda MAXI de 54 °C abarca las siete columnas, incluidas JET B y JP4. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["54 °C para todas las especificaciones de su tabla","54 °C salvo con JET B y JP4, que es 49 °C","55 °C para todas las especificaciones de su tabla","49 °C para todas las especificaciones de su tabla"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 with IAE V2500 engines, what is the MAXIMUM fuel temperature?","keys":["54","maxi","v2500"],"answer":"In the FUEL TEMPERATURE table of the A321 with IAE V2500 the MAXI cell of 54 °C covers the seven columns, including JET B and JP4. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["54 °C for all the specifications of its table","54 °C except with JET B and JP4, which is 49 °C","55 °C for all the specifications of its table","49 °C for all the specifications of its table"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0237","es":{"q":"Operando con JET B, ¿qué diferencia hay entre la temperatura MÁXIMA de combustible de un A321 con motores IAE V2500 y la de un A319/A320 CEO?","keys":["321","2500","maxi"],"answer":"En la tabla del A321 con IAE V2500 los 54 °C cubren las siete columnas, JET B incluida. En la de los A319/A320 CEO la fila MAXI está partida y JET B (junto con JP4) queda limitado a 49 °C. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["El A321 con IAE V2500 admite 54 °C, mientras que el A319/A320 CEO queda limitado a 49 °C","Ninguna: en ambos es 49 °C","Ninguna: en ambos es 54 °C","El A321 con IAE V2500 queda limitado a 49 °C, mientras que el A319/A320 CEO admite 55 °C"]},"en":{"q":"Operating with JET B, what is the difference between the MAXIMUM fuel temperature of an A321 with IAE V2500 engines and that of an A319/A320 CEO?","keys":["321","2500","maxi"],"answer":"In the table of the A321 with IAE V2500 the 54 °C cover the seven columns, JET B included. In that of the A319/A320 CEO the MAXI row is split and JET B (together with JP4) is limited to 49 °C. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 146 · rev 28 NOV 17)","opts":["The A321 with IAE V2500 allows 54 °C, whereas the A319/A320 CEO is limited to 49 °C","None: on both it is 49 °C","None: on both it is 54 °C","The A321 with IAE V2500 is limited to 49 °C, whereas the A319/A320 CEO allows 55 °C"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0238","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500 (o un A320neo con PW1100G), con los depósitos exteriores equilibrados y el depósito interior más pesado LLENO, ¿cuál es la asimetría máxima permitida al despegue?","keys":["500","1102","kg"],"answer":"En la tabla FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF (INNER TANKS, OUTER TANKS BALANCED) de este grupo, con el depósito más pesado lleno (Full) la asimetría máxima es de 500 kg (1 102 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["500 kg (1 102 lb)","400 kg (882 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines (or an A320neo with PW1100G), with the outer tanks balanced and the heavier inner tank FULL, what is the maximum imbalance permitted at takeoff?","keys":["500","1102","kg"],"answer":"In the FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF (INNER TANKS, OUTER TANKS BALANCED) table of this group, with the heavier tank full (Full) the maximum imbalance is 500 kg (1 102 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["500 kg (1 102 lb)","400 kg (882 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0239","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500 (o un A320neo con PW1100G), y con los depósitos exteriores equilibrados, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la asimetría máxima al despegue en los depósitos interiores es FALSA?","keys":["valores","tabla","variacion"],"answer":"El FCOM indica expresamente que \"the variation is linear between these values\": la variación entre los puntos de la tabla es LINEAL, no escalonada. Las otras tres afirmaciones reproducen literalmente las filas de la tabla FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF (Full → 500 kg, 3 000 kg → 1 050 kg, 1 450 kg → 1 450 kg). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Entre los valores de la tabla la variación es escalonada, por lo que debe tomarse siempre el valor de la fila inmediatamente superior","Con el depósito más pesado lleno, la asimetría máxima es de 500 kg (1 102 lb)","Con 3 000 kg (6 613 lb) en el depósito más pesado, la asimetría máxima es de 1 050 kg (2 314 lb)","Con 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) en el depósito más pesado, la asimetría máxima es de 1 450 kg (3 196 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines (or an A320neo with PW1100G), and with the outer tanks balanced, which of these statements about the maximum imbalance at takeoff in the inner tanks is FALSE?","keys":["linear","variation","imbalance"],"answer":"The FCOM expressly states that \"the variation is linear between these values\": the variation between the table points is LINEAR, not stepped. The other three statements literally reproduce the rows of the FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF table (Full → 500 kg, 3 000 kg → 1 050 kg, 1 450 kg → 1 450 kg). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Between the table values the variation is stepped, so the value of the row immediately above must always be taken","With the heavier tank full, the maximum imbalance is 500 kg (1 102 lb)","With 3 000 kg (6 613 lb) in the heavier tank, the maximum imbalance is 1 050 kg (2 314 lb)","With 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) in the heavier tank, the maximum imbalance is 1 450 kg (3 196 lb)"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0240","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500, con los depósitos exteriores equilibrados, el depósito interior más pesado tiene 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) y el opuesto está vacío. ¿Es aceptable para el despegue?","keys":["1450","kg","deposito"],"answer":"La tabla FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF de este grupo indica que con 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) en el depósito más pesado la asimetría máxima admitida es de 1 450 kg (3 196 lb), es decir, se admite el depósito opuesto vacío. La variación es lineal entre los valores de la tabla. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Sí: para 1 450 kg en el depósito más pesado la asimetría máxima al despegue es precisamente de 1 450 kg","No: la asimetría máxima al despegue es de 500 kg en cualquier caso","No: la asimetría máxima para esa cantidad es de 1 050 kg","Sí, pero sólo porque en vuelo no hay limitación por debajo de 2 250 kg"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines, with the outer tanks balanced, the heavier inner tank has 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) and the opposite one is empty. Is it acceptable for takeoff?","keys":["1450","kg","tank"],"answer":"The FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF table of this group indicates that with 1 450 kg (3 196 lb) in the heavier tank the maximum permitted imbalance is 1 450 kg (3 196 lb), that is, the opposite tank empty is allowed. The variation is linear between the table values. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Yes: for 1 450 kg in the heavier tank the maximum imbalance at takeoff is precisely 1 450 kg","No: the maximum imbalance at takeoff is 500 kg in any case","No: the maximum imbalance for that quantity is 1 050 kg","Yes, but only because in flight there is no limitation below 2 250 kg"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0241","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500 (o un A320neo con PW1100G), con los depósitos interiores equilibrados, ¿cuál es la asimetría máxima permitida en los depósitos exteriores al despegue?","keys":["370","815","kg"],"answer":"La tabla OUTER TANKS (INNER TANKS BALANCED) de FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF fija una asimetría máxima de 370 kg (815 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["370 kg (815 lb)","500 kg (1 102 lb)","690 kg (1 521 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines (or an A320neo with PW1100G), with the inner tanks balanced, what is the maximum imbalance permitted in the outer tanks at takeoff?","keys":["370","815","kg"],"answer":"The OUTER TANKS (INNER TANKS BALANCED) table of FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF sets a maximum imbalance of 370 kg (815 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 147 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["370 kg (815 lb)","500 kg (1 102 lb)","690 kg (1 521 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0242","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500, en aproximación, el depósito interior más pesado indica 2 000 kg y los exteriores están equilibrados. ¿Qué asimetría máxima aplica?","keys":["2250","4960","kg"],"answer":"Tras la tabla de vuelo y aterrizaje el FCOM precisa que la variación es lineal entre los valores dados y que no hay limitación por debajo de 2 250 kg (4 960 lb). Con 2 000 kg en el depósito más pesado se está por debajo de ese umbral. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Ninguna: por debajo de 2 250 kg (4 960 lb) no hay limitación","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)","1 600 kg (3 527 lb)","2 350 kg (5 180 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines, on approach, the heavier inner tank indicates 2 000 kg and the outer tanks are balanced. What maximum imbalance applies?","keys":["2250","4960","kg"],"answer":"After the flight and landing table the FCOM specifies that the variation is linear between the given values and that there is no limitation below 2 250 kg (4 960 lb). With 2 000 kg in the heavier tank you are below that threshold. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["None: below 2 250 kg (4 960 lb) there is no limitation","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)","1 600 kg (3 527 lb)","2 350 kg (5 180 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0243","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500 (o un A320neo con PW1100G), ¿cuál es la asimetría máxima permitida en los depósitos exteriores en vuelo y al aterrizaje?","keys":["690","1521","kg"],"answer":"En la tabla OUTER TANKS de FUEL IMBALANCE IN FLIGHT AND AT LANDING la asimetría máxima es de 690 kg (1 521 lb), sujeta a las condiciones de la nota (1). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["690 kg (1 521 lb)","370 kg (815 lb)","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines (or an A320neo with PW1100G), what is the maximum imbalance permitted in the outer tanks in flight and at landing?","keys":["690","1521","kg"],"answer":"In the OUTER TANKS table of FUEL IMBALANCE IN FLIGHT AND AT LANDING the maximum imbalance is 690 kg (1 521 lb), subject to the conditions of note (1). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["690 kg (1 521 lb)","370 kg (815 lb)","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0244","es":{"q":"En un A319/A320 con motores CFM56 o IAE V2500, la asimetría máxima de los depósitos exteriores (uno lleno / uno vacío) se admite si se cumple alguna de las condiciones de la nota (1). ¿Cuál de las siguientes NO forma parte de esa nota?","keys":["1500","3307","kg","except"],"answer":"La nota (1) recoge la igualdad por lados, el criterio del interior más lleno en el lado del exterior más ligero y el tope de 3 000 kg (6 613 lb) de diferencia entre interiores. Los 1 500 kg son la cantidad mínima de combustible para el despegue, una limitación distinta que no forma parte de esta nota. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Que la cantidad total de combustible a bordo no sea inferior a 1 500 kg (3 307 lb)","Que la cantidad de combustible de los depósitos exterior e interior de un lado sea igual a la de los depósitos exterior e interior del otro lado","Que, en el lado del depósito exterior más ligero, el depósito interior tenga más combustible que el interior opuesto","Que la diferencia entre la cantidad de combustible de los depósitos interiores no sea superior a 3 000 kg (6 613 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A319/A320 with CFM56 or IAE V2500 engines, the maximum imbalance of the outer tanks (one full / one empty) is allowed if any of the conditions of note (1) is met. Which of the following is NOT part of that note?","keys":["1500","3307","kg","takeoff"],"answer":"Note (1) covers the side-to-side equality, the criterion of the fuller inner tank on the side of the lighter outer tank, and the cap of 3 000 kg (6 613 lb) difference between inner tanks. The 1 500 kg is the minimum fuel quantity for takeoff, a separate limitation that is not part of this note. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["That the total fuel quantity on board is not below 1 500 kg (3 307 lb)","That the fuel quantity of the outer and inner tanks of one side equals that of the outer and inner tanks of the other side","That, on the side of the lighter outer tank, the inner tank has more fuel than the opposite inner tank","That the difference between the fuel quantity of the inner tanks is not above 3 000 kg (6 613 lb)"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0245","es":{"q":"En un A321 (motores IAE V2500 o CFM56) o un A321neo (PW1100G), con el depósito más pesado LLENO, ¿cuál es la asimetría máxima permitida al despegue?","keys":["400","882","kg","a321"],"answer":"La tabla FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF de los A321 asigna 400 kg (882 lb) tanto a la fila Full como a la de 3 000 kg (6 614 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["400 kg (882 lb)","500 kg (1 102 lb)","700 kg (1 543 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 (IAE V2500 or CFM56 engines) or an A321neo (PW1100G), with the heavier tank FULL, what is the maximum imbalance permitted at takeoff?","keys":["400","882","kg","a321"],"answer":"The FUEL IMBALANCE AT TAKEOFF table of the A321 assigns 400 kg (882 lb) to both the Full row and the 3 000 kg (6 614 lb) row. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["400 kg (882 lb)","500 kg (1 102 lb)","700 kg (1 543 lb)","1 050 kg (2 314 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0246","es":{"q":"Con el depósito más pesado lleno, ¿cómo es la asimetría máxima al despegue de un A321 frente a la de un A319/A320?","keys":["100","321","kg","a321"],"answer":"La tabla de despegue de los A321 fija 400 kg (882 lb) con el depósito más pesado lleno, mientras que la de los A319/A320 y A320neo fija 500 kg (1 102 lb): el A321 es 100 kg más restrictivo. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Es 100 kg menor en el A321 (400 kg frente a 500 kg)","Es idéntica en ambos (500 kg)","Es 300 kg mayor en el A321 (700 kg frente a 400 kg)","Es 100 kg mayor en el A321 (500 kg frente a 400 kg)"]},"en":{"q":"With the heavier tank full, how does the maximum takeoff asymmetry of an A321 compare with that of an A319/A320?","keys":["100","321","kg","a321"],"answer":"The A321 takeoff table sets 400 kg (882 lb) with the heavier tank full, whereas the A319/A320 and A320neo table sets 500 kg (1 102 lb): the A321 is 100 kg more restrictive. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["It is 100 kg lower on the A321 (400 kg versus 500 kg)","It is identical on both (500 kg)","It is 300 kg higher on the A321 (700 kg versus 400 kg)","It is 100 kg higher on the A321 (500 kg versus 400 kg)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0247","es":{"q":"En un A321 (motores IAE V2500 o CFM56) o un A321neo (PW1100G), con el depósito más pesado LLENO, ¿cuál es la asimetría máxima permitida en vuelo y al aterrizaje?","keys":["1320","2910","kg","a321"],"answer":"La tabla FUEL IMBALANCE IN FLIGHT AND AT LANDING de los A321 asigna 1 320 kg (2 910 lb) a la fila Full. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)","2 350 kg (5 180 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"On an A321 (IAE V2500 or CFM56 engines) or an A321neo (PW1100G), with the heavier tank FULL, what is the maximum imbalance allowed in flight and at landing?","keys":["1320","2910","kg","a321"],"answer":"The A321 FUEL IMBALANCE IN FLIGHT AND AT LANDING table assigns 1 320 kg (2 910 lb) to the Full row. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)","1 500 kg (3 306 lb)","2 350 kg (5 180 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0248","es":{"q":"Vuelas un A321 (motores IAE V2500 o CFM56) y en descenso el depósito más pesado indica 2 300 kg. ¿Qué limitación de asimetría aplica?","keys":["2350","5180","kg","a321"],"answer":"Tras la tabla de vuelo y aterrizaje de los A321 el FCOM indica que la variación es lineal entre los valores dados y que no hay limitación por debajo de 2 350 kg (5 180 lb). Con 2 300 kg se está por debajo de ese umbral. Ojo: en un A319/A320 el umbral es 2 250 kg, de modo que esa misma cantidad sí quedaría limitada. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Ninguna: por debajo de 2 350 kg (5 180 lb) no hay limitación en este avión","Ninguna: por debajo de 2 250 kg (4 960 lb) no hay limitación","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying an A321 (IAE V2500 or CFM56 engines) and on descent the heavier tank indicates 2 300 kg. Which imbalance limitation applies?","keys":["2350","5180","kg","a321"],"answer":"After the A321 in-flight and landing table, the FCOM states that the variation is linear between the given values and that there is no limitation below 2 350 kg (5 180 lb). At 2 300 kg you are below that threshold. Note: on an A319/A320 the threshold is 2 250 kg, so that same quantity would indeed be limited. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["None: below 2 350 kg (5 180 lb) there is no limitation on this aircraft","None: below 2 250 kg (4 960 lb) there is no limitation","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0249","es":{"q":"Comparando las tablas de asimetría en vuelo y al aterrizaje, ¿qué diferencia hay entre la fila intermedia de un A321 y la de un A319/A320?","keys":["321","1450","kg"],"answer":"La fila intermedia de la tabla de vuelo y aterrizaje de los A321 es 4 000 kg (8 818 lb) → 1 450 kg (3 196 lb), mientras que la de los A319/A320 y A320neo es 4 300 kg (9 479 lb) → 1 600 kg (3 527 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El A321 admite 1 450 kg con 4 000 kg en el depósito más pesado; el A319/A320, 1 600 kg con 4 300 kg","El A321 admite 1 600 kg con 4 300 kg en el depósito más pesado; el A319/A320, 1 450 kg con 4 000 kg","Ambos admiten 1 500 kg con 4 000 kg en el depósito más pesado","El A321 admite 2 350 kg con 4 000 kg; el A319/A320, 2 250 kg con 4 300 kg"]},"en":{"q":"Comparing the in-flight and landing imbalance tables, what is the difference between the intermediate row of an A321 and that of an A319/A320?","keys":["321","1450","kg"],"answer":"The intermediate row of the A321 in-flight and landing table is 4 000 kg (8 818 lb) → 1 450 kg (3 196 lb), whereas that of the A319/A320 and A320neo is 4 300 kg (9 479 lb) → 1 600 kg (3 527 lb). (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The A321 allows 1 450 kg with 4 000 kg in the heavier tank; the A319/A320, 1 600 kg with 4 300 kg","The A321 allows 1 600 kg with 4 300 kg in the heavier tank; the A319/A320, 1 450 kg with 4 000 kg","Both allow 1 500 kg with 4 000 kg in the heavier tank","The A321 allows 2 350 kg with 4 000 kg; the A319/A320, 2 250 kg with 4 300 kg"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0250","es":{"q":"Sobre la nota que acompaña a las tablas de asimetría máxima de combustible, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["exceden","valores","realizarse"],"answer":"La nota dice que en condiciones excepcionales (por ejemplo, un fallo del sistema de combustible) los valores de asimetría máxima pueden excederse sin efecto significativo en las cualidades de manejo, y que el avión permanece totalmente controlable en todas las fases de vuelo. No prescribe ningún aterrizaje inmediato. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Si se exceden esos valores debe realizarse un aterrizaje inmediato en el aeropuerto adecuado más próximo","En condiciones excepcionales, como un fallo del sistema de combustible, los valores de asimetría máxima pueden excederse","Al excederse esos valores en condiciones excepcionales no se produce un efecto significativo en las cualidades de manejo del avión","El avión sigue siendo totalmente controlable en todas las fases de vuelo"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the note accompanying the maximum fuel asymmetry tables, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["immediate","landing","exceeded"],"answer":"The note states that under exceptional conditions (for example, a fuel system failure) the maximum imbalance values may be exceeded with no significant effect on the handling qualities, and that the aircraft remains fully controllable in all flight phases. It does not prescribe any immediate landing. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 148 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["If those values are exceeded, an immediate landing must be made at the nearest suitable airport","Under exceptional conditions, such as a fuel system failure, the maximum imbalance values may be exceeded","When those values are exceeded under exceptional conditions, there is no significant effect on the aircraft handling qualities","The aircraft remains fully controllable in all flight phases"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0251","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la cantidad mínima de combustible para el despegue?","keys":["1500","3307","kg"],"answer":"El FCOM fija la cantidad mínima de combustible para el despegue en 1 500 kg (3 307 lb), aplicable a toda la flota. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 149 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 500 kg (3 307 lb)","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)","2 250 kg (4 960 lb)"]},"en":{"q":"What is the minimum fuel quantity for takeoff?","keys":["1500","3307","kg"],"answer":"The FCOM sets the minimum fuel quantity for takeoff at 1 500 kg (3 307 lb), applicable to the whole fleet. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 149 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["1 500 kg (3 307 lb)","1 320 kg (2 910 lb)","1 450 kg (3 196 lb)","2 250 kg (4 960 lb)"]}},{"sys":"FUEL","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0252","es":{"q":"Alineado en pista para despegar, tienes 1 600 kg de combustible a bordo pero se muestra la alerta ECAM FUEL WING TK LO LVL. ¿Qué establece el FCOM?","keys":["ecam","alertas","bajo"],"answer":"Además de los 1 500 kg (3 307 lb) mínimos, el FCOM exige que las alertas ECAM relacionadas con el bajo nivel de combustible en los depósitos de ala (FUEL WING TK LO LVL, etc.) no aparezcan para el despegue. Son dos condiciones independientes: cumplir la cantidad mínima no basta. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 149 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Las alertas ECAM de bajo nivel de combustible en los depósitos de ala no deben mostrarse para el despegue","Se puede despegar: se superan los 1 500 kg mínimos y la alerta es sólo informativa","Se puede despegar siempre que los depósitos exteriores estén equilibrados","Se puede despegar si la asimetría es inferior a 500 kg"]},"en":{"q":"Lined up on the runway for takeoff, you have 1 600 kg of fuel on board but the ECAM FUEL WING TK LO LVL alert is displayed. What does the FCOM state?","keys":["ecam","wing","displayed"],"answer":"In addition to the 1 500 kg (3 307 lb) minimum, the FCOM requires that the ECAM alerts related to low fuel level in the wing tanks (FUEL WING TK LO LVL, etc.) must not be displayed for takeoff. These are two independent conditions: meeting the minimum quantity is not enough. (FCOM LIM-FUEL · p. 149 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The ECAM low fuel level alerts in the wing tanks must not be displayed for takeoff","Takeoff is allowed: the 1 500 kg minimum is exceeded and the alert is only informative","Takeoff is allowed provided the outer tanks are balanced","Takeoff is allowed if the imbalance is less than 500 kg"]}},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0253","es":{"q":"¿A partir de qué temperatura, con humedad visible presente, se considera que existen condiciones de engelamiento (OAT en tierra o tras el despegue, TAT en vuelo)?","keys":["10","oat","igual"],"answer":"Existen condiciones de engelamiento cuando la OAT (en tierra o tras el despegue) o la TAT (en vuelo) es igual o inferior a 10 °C y hay humedad visible en cualquier forma. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["Igual o inferior a 10 °C","Igual o inferior a 0 °C","Igual o inferior a 5 °C","Inferior a 15 °C"]},"en":{"q":"At or below what temperature, with visible moisture present, are icing conditions considered to exist (OAT on the ground or after takeoff, TAT in flight)?","keys":["10","oat","icing"],"answer":"Icing conditions exist when the OAT (on the ground or after takeoff) or the TAT (in flight) is at or below 10 °C and there is visible moisture in any form. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["At or below 10 °C","At or below 0 °C","At or below 5 °C","Below 15 °C"]}},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0254","es":{"q":"Con la OAT igual o inferior a 10 °C, todas las siguientes situaciones constituyen humedad visible que define condiciones de engelamiento, EXCEPTO:","keys":["5","bruma","seca"],"answer":"El FCOM enumera como humedad visible las nubes, la niebla con visibilidad de 1 sm (1 600 m) o menos, la lluvia, la nieve, el aguanieve y los cristales de hielo. La bruma seca con 5 km de visibilidad no figura en esa lista. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["Bruma seca (haze) con visibilidad de 5 km","Niebla con visibilidad de 1 sm (1 600 m) o menos","Lluvia, nieve, aguanieve o cristales de hielo","Nubes"]},"en":{"q":"With the OAT at or below 10 °C, all of the following situations constitute visible moisture defining icing conditions, EXCEPT:","keys":["5","haze","dry"],"answer":"The FCOM lists as visible moisture: clouds, fog with visibility of 1 sm (1 600 m) or less, rain, snow, sleet and ice crystals. Dry haze with 5 km visibility does not appear on that list. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["Dry haze with 5 km visibility","Fog with visibility of 1 sm (1 600 m) or less","Rain, snow, sleet or ice crystals","Clouds"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0255","es":{"q":"Está en plataforma con OAT de 6 °C, cielo despejado y sin precipitación, pero las calles de rodaje y la pista tienen nieve y agua estancada que pueden ser ingeridas por los motores. ¿Existen condiciones de engelamiento para el despegue?","keys":["10","oat","porque"],"answer":"El FCOM define un segundo caso: también existen condiciones de engelamiento cuando la OAT en tierra y para el despegue es igual o inferior a 10 °C y se opera en plataformas, calles de rodaje o pistas donde la nieve en superficie, el agua estancada o el slush pueden ser ingeridos por los motores, o congelarse en motores, góndolas o sondas. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["Sí, porque con OAT igual o inferior a 10 °C y nieve, agua estancada o slush en superficie susceptibles de ser ingeridos, existen condiciones de engelamiento","No, porque no hay humedad visible en el aire","No, porque la OAT está por encima de 0 °C","Sí, pero sólo si la visibilidad es de 1 600 m o menos"]},"en":{"q":"You are on the apron with OAT of 6 °C, clear sky and no precipitation, but the taxiways and runway have snow and standing water that may be ingested by the engines. Do icing conditions exist for takeoff?","keys":["10","oat","ingested"],"answer":"The FCOM defines a second case: icing conditions also exist when the OAT on the ground and for takeoff is at or below 10 °C and operating on aprons, taxiways or runways where surface snow, standing water or slush may be ingested by the engines, or freeze on engines, nacelles or probes. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 05 JUN 18)","opts":["Yes, because with OAT at or below 10 °C and surface snow, standing water or slush liable to be ingested, icing conditions exist","No, because there is no visible moisture in the air","No, because the OAT is above 0 °C","Yes, but only if visibility is 1 600 m or less"]}},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0256","es":{"q":"¿A partir de qué espesor aproximado de acumulación de hielo sobre la célula se considera que la acreción de hielo es severa?","keys":["5","0.2","partir"],"answer":"La acreción de hielo se considera severa cuando la acumulación de hielo sobre la célula alcanza aproximadamente 5 mm (0.2 in) de espesor o más. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["5 mm (0.2 in)","2 mm (0.08 in)","10 mm (0.4 in)","13 mm (0.5 in)"]},"en":{"q":"At approximately what thickness of ice accumulation on the airframe is ice accretion considered severe?","keys":["5","0.2","accretion"],"answer":"Ice accretion is considered severe when the ice accumulation on the airframe reaches approximately 5 mm (0.2 in) thickness or more. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["5 mm (0.2 in)","2 mm (0.08 in)","10 mm (0.4 in)","13 mm (0.5 in)"]}},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0257","es":{"q":"Sobre la definición de thin hoarfrost (escarcha fina), ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["opaca","impide","distinguir"],"answer":"El FCOM define el thin hoarfrost precisamente por lo contrario: es tan fino que las características de la superficie (líneas o marcas) pueden distinguirse por debajo. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Es tan opaca que impide distinguir bajo ella las líneas o marcas de la superficie","Es típicamente un depósito cristalino blanco","Se desarrolla normalmente de forma uniforme sobre las superficies expuestas en noches frías y despejadas","Es tan fina que se pueden distinguir bajo ella los detalles de la superficie (líneas o marcas)"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding the definition of thin hoarfrost, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["thin","surface","distinguished"],"answer":"The FCOM defines thin hoarfrost as precisely the opposite: it is so thin that the surface features (lines or markings) can be distinguished underneath. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["It is so opaque that it prevents distinguishing the surface lines or markings underneath","It is typically a white crystalline deposit","It normally develops uniformly on exposed surfaces on cold, clear nights","It is so thin that surface details (lines or markings) can be distinguished underneath"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"ICE","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0258","es":{"q":"¿En qué caso debe utilizar la tripulación el rain repellent?","keys":["unicamente","caso","lluvia"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que la tripulación sólo debe usar el rain repellent en caso de lluvia moderada a fuerte. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Únicamente en caso de lluvia moderada a fuerte","En cualquier intensidad de lluvia, para mejorar la visibilidad","Únicamente con el limpiaparabrisas inoperativo","Únicamente en lluvia ligera, antes de que la lluvia arrecie"]},"en":{"q":"In which case must the crew use the rain repellent?","keys":["moderate","heavy","rain"],"answer":"The FCOM states that the crew must only use the rain repellent in case of moderate to heavy rain. (FCOM LIM-ICE_RAIN · p. 155 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Only in case of moderate to heavy rain","In any rain intensity, to improve visibility","Only with the windshield wiper inoperative","Only in light rain, before the rain intensifies"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0259","es":{"q":"¿Cuál es la temperatura máxima de frenos para el despegue, con los brake fans en off?","keys":["300","temperatura","maxima"],"answer":"El FCOM publica una temperatura máxima de frenos para el despegue (brake fans off) de 300 °C. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["300 °C","150 °C","200 °C","500 °C"]},"en":{"q":"What is the maximum brake temperature for takeoff, with the brake fans off?","keys":["300","brake","temperature"],"answer":"The FCOM publishes a maximum brake temperature for takeoff (brake fans off) of 300 °C. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["300 °C","150 °C","200 °C","500 °C"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0260","es":{"q":"Tras un turnaround corto, en el punto de espera los frenos indican 320 °C con los brake fans en off. ¿Qué aplica?","keys":["300","cumple","limitacion"],"answer":"La temperatura máxima de frenos para el despegue con brake fans off es 300 °C. Con 320 °C se está por encima del límite y no se cumple la limitación para despegar. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["No cumple la limitación: el máximo para el despegue con brake fans off es 300 °C","Puede despegar: el límite publicado con brake fans off es 500 °C","Puede despegar: el límite sólo aplica al aterrizaje","Puede despegar si la temperatura es decreciente en al menos dos frenos"]},"en":{"q":"After a short turnaround, at the holding point the brakes indicate 320 °C with the brake fans off. What applies?","keys":["300","brake","limit"],"answer":"The maximum brake temperature for takeoff with brake fans off is 300 °C. At 320 °C you are above the limit and the limitation for takeoff is not met. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The limitation is not met: the maximum for takeoff with brake fans off is 300 °C","Takeoff is allowed: the published limit with brake fans off is 500 °C","Takeoff is allowed: the limit only applies to landing","Takeoff is allowed if the temperature is decreasing on at least two brakes"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0261","es":{"q":"Según LIM-LG, ¿qué establece el FCOM sobre la capacidad del sistema de frenado para mantener el avión parado?","keys":["sistema","frenado","disenado"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que el sistema de frenado no está diseñado para mantener el avión en posición estacionaria cuando se aplica un nivel de empuje elevado en al menos un motor. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El sistema de frenado no está diseñado para mantener el avión en posición estacionaria cuando se aplica un nivel de empuje elevado en al menos un motor","El sistema de frenado mantiene el avión parado con empuje máximo en ambos motores","El sistema de frenado sólo mantiene el avión parado si el freno de parking está aplicado","El sistema de frenado mantiene el avión parado hasta empuje de despegue si la pista está seca"]},"en":{"q":"According to LIM-LG, what does the FCOM state about the braking system's capability to hold the aircraft stationary?","keys":["braking","system","stationary"],"answer":"The FCOM states that the braking system is not designed to hold the aircraft stationary when a high thrust level is applied on at least one engine. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The braking system is not designed to hold the aircraft stationary when a high thrust level is applied on at least one engine","The braking system holds the aircraft stationary with maximum thrust on both engines","The braking system only holds the aircraft stationary if the parking brake is applied","The braking system holds the aircraft stationary up to takeoff thrust if the runway is dry"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0262","es":{"q":"Va a realizar en tierra un procedimiento que requiere aumentar el empuje con los frenos aplicados. ¿Qué exige el FCOM a la tripulación?","keys":["asegurarse","avion","permanece"],"answer":"Durante procedimientos en tierra que requieren un aumento de empuje con frenado, la tripulación debe asegurarse de que el avión permanece estacionario y estar preparada para retrasar inmediatamente las palancas de empuje a IDLE, porque el sistema de frenado no está diseñado para retener el avión con empuje elevado. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Asegurarse de que el avión permanece estacionario y estar preparada para retrasar inmediatamente las palancas de empuje a IDLE","Aplicar el freno de parking y aumentar el empuje hasta el valor requerido sin más precauciones","Limitar el empuje a un máximo del 50 % de N1 en todos los casos","Realizar el procedimiento únicamente con un motor en marcha"]},"en":{"q":"You are about to perform a ground procedure that requires increasing thrust with the brakes applied. What does the FCOM require of the crew?","keys":["stationary","idle","thrust"],"answer":"During ground procedures that require a thrust increase with braking, the crew must ensure that the aircraft remains stationary and be ready to immediately retard the thrust levers to IDLE, because the braking system is not designed to hold the aircraft with high thrust. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Ensure that the aircraft remains stationary and be ready to immediately retard the thrust levers to IDLE","Apply the parking brake and increase thrust to the required value with no further precautions","Limit thrust to a maximum of 50 % N1 in all cases","Perform the procedure with only one engine running"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0263","es":{"q":"En operación towbarless (remolque y pushback) sobre el tren de morro, ¿cuál es el ángulo máximo de NWS publicado?","keys":["85","nws","operacion"],"answer":"La operación towbarless sobre el tren de morro está aprobada usando los vehículos aceptados listados en el Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001, con un ángulo máximo de NWS de ±85 °. (Verificado sobre la página 161 del PDF: el FCOM imprime «Maximum NWS angle ±85 °».) (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 12 SEP 17)","opts":["±85 °","±30 °","±75 °","±95 °"]},"en":{"q":"In towbarless operation (towing and pushback) on the nose gear, what is the published maximum NWS angle?","keys":["85","nws","towbarless"],"answer":"Towbarless operation on the nose gear is approved using the accepted vehicles listed in Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001, with a maximum NWS angle of ±85 °. (Verified on page 161 of the PDF: the FCOM prints «Maximum NWS angle ±85 °».) (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 12 SEP 17)","opts":["±85 °","±30 °","±75 °","±95 °"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0264","es":{"q":"¿En qué condiciones está aprobada la operación towbarless (remolque y pushback) sobre el tren de morro?","keys":["09.11","00001","nws"],"answer":"El FCOM aprueba la operación towbarless sobre el tren de morro cuando se utilizan los vehículos de remolque towbarless aceptados listados en el Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001, con un ángulo máximo de NWS de ±85 °. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 12 SEP 17)","opts":["Utilizando los vehículos de remolque towbarless aceptados que figuran en el Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001","En cualquier avión y con cualquier vehículo, siempre que se respete el ángulo de NWS","Únicamente en los aviones equipados con la opción de remolque towbarless","Únicamente en los A321, por su mayor peso sobre el tren de morro"]},"en":{"q":"Under what conditions is towbarless operation (towing and pushback) on the nose gear approved?","keys":["09.11","00001","nws"],"answer":"The FCOM approves towbarless operation on the nose gear when the accepted towbarless towing vehicles listed in Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001 are used, with a maximum NWS angle of ±85 °. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 161 · rev 12 SEP 17)","opts":["Using the accepted towbarless towing vehicles listed in Airbus WISE ISI 09.11.00001","On any aircraft and with any vehicle, provided the NWS angle is respected","Only on aircraft fitted with the towbarless towing option","Only on A321s, due to their greater nose-gear load"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0265","es":{"q":"Para abandonar la pista o rodar a baja velocidad con un máximo de un neumático desinflado (no dañado) por tren, considerando los tres trenes, ¿cuál es la velocidad máxima de rodaje durante un viraje?","keys":["7","kt","abandonar"],"answer":"Con un máximo de un neumático desinflado por tren (considerando los tres trenes), la velocidad máxima de rodaje durante el viraje es 7 kt. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["7 kt","3 kt","5 kt","10 kt"]},"en":{"q":"To vacate the runway or taxi at low speed with a maximum of one deflated (not damaged) tyre per gear, considering the three gears, what is the maximum taxi speed during a turn?","keys":["7","kt","taxi"],"answer":"With a maximum of one deflated tyre per gear (considering the three gears), the maximum taxi speed during the turn is 7 kt. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["7 kt","3 kt","5 kt","10 kt"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0266","es":{"q":"Tras el aterrizaje detecta dos neumáticos desinflados (no dañados) en el mismo tren principal y debe abandonar la pista. ¿Qué limitaciones aplican?","keys":["3","30","kt","nws"],"answer":"Con dos neumáticos desinflados en el mismo tren principal (máximo un tren principal) la velocidad máxima de rodaje es 3 kt, y el ángulo máximo de NWS aplicable en rodaje con neumáticos desinflados es 30 °. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["Velocidad máxima de rodaje 3 kt y ángulo máximo de NWS 30 °","Velocidad máxima de rodaje 7 kt y ángulo máximo de NWS 85 °","Velocidad máxima de rodaje 3 kt sin límite específico de NWS","Velocidad máxima de rodaje 7 kt sólo en viraje y ángulo máximo de NWS 30 °"]},"en":{"q":"After landing you detect two deflated (not damaged) tyres on the same main gear and you must vacate the runway. Which limitations apply?","keys":["3","30","kt","nws"],"answer":"With two deflated tyres on the same main gear (maximum one main gear) the maximum taxi speed is 3 kt, and the maximum NWS angle applicable when taxiing with deflated tyres is 30 °. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["Maximum taxi speed 3 kt and maximum NWS angle 30 °","Maximum taxi speed 7 kt and maximum NWS angle 85 °","Maximum taxi speed 3 kt with no specific NWS limit","Maximum taxi speed 7 kt only in a turn and maximum NWS angle 30 °"]}},{"sys":"GEAR","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0267","es":{"q":"Sobre el rodaje con neumáticos desinflados o dañados, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["85","nws","angulo"],"answer":"El ángulo máximo de NWS publicado para el rodaje con neumáticos desinflados es 30 °. El valor de ±85 ° corresponde a la operación towbarless sobre el tren de morro, que es otra limitación distinta. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["El ángulo máximo de NWS en rodaje con neumáticos desinflados es de 85 °","Si se sospecha daño en un neumático, la tripulación debe solicitar una inspección del avión antes de abandonar la pista o rodar","El caso de dos neumáticos desinflados contempla como máximo un tren principal","Si el personal de tierra sospecha que el reventón de un neumático puede haber dañado el tren, procede acción de mantenimiento"]},"en":{"q":"Regarding taxiing with deflated or damaged tyres, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["30","nws","angle"],"answer":"The published maximum NWS angle for taxiing with deflated tyres is 30 °. The ±85 ° value corresponds to towbarless operation on the nose gear, which is a different limitation. (FCOM LIM-LG · p. 162 · rev 01 JUN 17)","opts":["The maximum NWS angle when taxiing with deflated tyres is 85 °","If tyre damage is suspected, the crew must request an aircraft inspection before vacating the runway or taxiing","The two-deflated-tyres case considers a maximum of one main gear","If ground staff suspect that a tyre burst may have damaged the gear, maintenance action is required"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0268","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿entre qué latitudes es posible el alineamiento en tierra del IRS?","keys":["73","irs","norte"],"answer":"El FCOM establece para este avión que el alineamiento en tierra del IRS es posible en latitudes comprendidas entre 73 ° Norte y 73 ° Sur. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Entre 73 ° Norte y 73 ° Sur","Entre 82 ° Norte y 82 ° Sur","Entre 75 ° Norte y 75 ° Sur","Entre 60 ° Norte y 60 ° Sur"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), between which latitudes is IRS ground alignment possible?","keys":["73","irs","north"],"answer":"The FCOM states for this aircraft that IRS ground alignment is possible at latitudes between 73 ° North and 73 ° South. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Between 73 ° North and 73 ° South","Between 82 ° North and 82 ° South","Between 75 ° North and 75 ° South","Between 60 ° North and 60 ° South"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0269","es":{"q":"Vuela el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) y debe alinear los IRS en tierra en un aeropuerto situado a 78 ° de latitud Norte. ¿Qué aplica?","keys":["73","irs","alineamiento"],"answer":"El alineamiento en tierra del IRS en este avión sólo es posible entre 73 ° Norte y 73 ° Sur. A 78 ° Norte se está fuera de la envolvente publicada, por lo que el alineamiento en tierra no es posible. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El alineamiento no es posible: en este avión el alineamiento en tierra sólo es posible hasta 73 ° Norte","El alineamiento es posible: el límite de este avión llega hasta 82 ° Norte","El alineamiento es posible siempre que se introduzca la posición manualmente en el MCDU","El alineamiento es posible utilizando una sola ADIRU"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) and must align the IRS on the ground at an airport located at 78 ° North latitude. What applies?","keys":["73","irs","alignment"],"answer":"IRS ground alignment on this aircraft is only possible between 73 ° North and 73 ° South. At 78 ° North you are outside the published envelope, so ground alignment is not possible. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Alignment is not possible: on this aircraft ground alignment is only possible up to 73 ° North","Alignment is possible: this aircraft's limit reaches up to 82 ° North","Alignment is possible provided the position is entered manually in the MCDU","Alignment is possible using a single ADIRU"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0270","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones sobre el alineamiento en tierra del IRS es FALSA?","keys":["82","irs","alineamiento"],"answer":"En este avión el alineamiento en tierra del IRS es posible entre 73 ° Norte y 73 ° Sur; 82 ° Norte queda fuera de ese rango. Las otras tres afirmaciones son coherentes con el límite publicado (73 ° N / 73 ° S, simétrico e inclusivo). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El alineamiento en tierra es posible a 82 ° de latitud Norte","El alineamiento en tierra es posible a 60 ° de latitud Sur","El límite de alineamiento en tierra es simétrico entre hemisferio Norte y Sur","El alineamiento en tierra es posible a 73 ° de latitud Norte"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), which of the following statements about IRS ground alignment is FALSE?","keys":["82","irs","alignment"],"answer":"On this aircraft IRS ground alignment is possible between 73 ° North and 73 ° South; 82 ° North is outside that range. The other three statements are consistent with the published limit (73 ° N / 73 ° S, symmetric and inclusive). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 167 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Ground alignment is possible at 82 ° North latitude","Ground alignment is possible at 60 ° South latitude","The ground alignment limit is symmetric between the Northern and Southern hemispheres","Ground alignment is possible at 73 ° North latitude"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0271","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), con todas las ADIRUs con la misma tabla de variación magnética: en modo NAV, ¿al norte de qué latitud el IR deja de proporcionar rumbo magnético y derrota magnética válidos?","keys":["73","irs","norte"],"answer":"Si todas las ADIRUs tienen la misma tabla de variación magnética, en modo NAV el IR no proporciona rumbo ni derrota magnéticos válidos al norte de 73 ° Norte (y al sur de 60 ° Sur). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Al norte de 73 ° Norte","Al norte de 60 ° Norte","Al norte de 70 ° Norte","Al norte de 82 ° Norte"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), with all ADIRUs using the same magnetic variation table: in NAV mode, north of which latitude does the IR stop providing valid magnetic heading and magnetic track?","keys":["73","irs","north"],"answer":"If all ADIRUs use the same magnetic variation table, in NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading or track north of 73 ° North (and south of 60 ° South). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["North of 73 ° North","North of 60 ° North","North of 70 ° North","North of 82 ° North"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0272","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), con todas las ADIRUs con la misma tabla de variación magnética, ¿cuál de estas afirmaciones es FALSA?","keys":["55","irs","modo"],"answer":"Con todas las ADIRUs con la misma tabla de variación magnética el límite sur es 60 ° Sur, no 55 ° Sur. 55 ° Sur sólo aplica en el caso de que una ADIRU tenga una tabla de variación magnética distinta. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En modo NAV el IR no proporciona rumbo magnético válido al sur de 55 ° Sur","En modo NAV el IR no proporciona rumbo magnético válido al sur de 60 ° Sur","En modo NAV el IR no proporciona derrota magnética válida al norte de 73 ° Norte","Está prohibido volar a latitudes más allá de estos límites"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), with all ADIRUs using the same magnetic variation table, which of these statements is FALSE?","keys":["55","irs","south"],"answer":"With all ADIRUs using the same magnetic variation table the southern limit is 60 ° South, not 55 ° South. 55 ° South only applies when one ADIRU has a different magnetic variation table. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["In NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading south of 55 ° South","In NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading south of 60 ° South","In NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic track north of 73 ° North","Flying at latitudes beyond these limits is prohibited"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0273","es":{"q":"Vuela el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota). Todas las ADIRUs tienen la misma tabla de variación magnética y Operaciones le propone una ruta que pasa por 76 ° Norte. ¿Qué debe hacer?","keys":["73","irs","rechazar"],"answer":"Con todas las ADIRUs con la misma tabla de variación magnética, en modo NAV el IR no proporciona rumbo ni derrota magnéticos válidos al norte de 73 ° Norte, y el FCOM establece expresamente que volar a latitudes más allá de esos límites está prohibido. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Rechazar la ruta: volar a latitudes más allá de 73 ° Norte está prohibido","Aceptar la ruta: basta con seleccionar referencia TRUE en la ADIRS","Aceptar la ruta: el rumbo magnético sigue siendo válido hasta 82 ° Norte","Aceptar la ruta si al menos dos ADIRUs permanecen operativas en modo NAV"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft). All ADIRUs have the same magnetic variation table and Operations proposes a route passing through 76 ° North. What must you do?","keys":["73","irs","prohibited"],"answer":"With all ADIRUs using the same magnetic variation table, in NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading or track north of 73 ° North, and the FCOM expressly states that flying at latitudes beyond those limits is prohibited. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Reject the route: flying at latitudes beyond 73 ° North is prohibited","Accept the route: it is enough to select TRUE reference on the ADIRS","Accept the route: magnetic heading remains valid up to 82 ° North","Accept the route if at least two ADIRUs remain operative in NAV mode"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0274","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), si una ADIRU tiene una tabla de variación magnética distinta: en modo NAV, al norte de 60 ° Norte el IR no proporciona rumbo ni derrota magnéticos válidos, ¿entre qué longitudes?","keys":["30","160","irs"],"answer":"Con una ADIRU con tabla de variación magnética distinta, en modo NAV el IR no proporciona rumbo ni derrota magnéticos válidos al norte de 60 ° Norte entre 30 ° Oeste y 160 ° Oeste (además de al norte de 73 ° Norte y al sur de 55 ° Sur). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Entre 30 ° Oeste y 160 ° Oeste","Entre 90 ° Oeste y 120 ° Oeste","Entre 180 ° Oeste y 160 ° Oeste","Entre 30 ° Este y 160 ° Este"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), if one ADIRU has a different magnetic variation table: in NAV mode, north of 60 ° North the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading or track, between which longitudes?","keys":["30","160","irs"],"answer":"With one ADIRU having a different magnetic variation table, in NAV mode the IR does not provide valid magnetic heading or track north of 60 ° North between 30 ° West and 160 ° West (in addition to north of 73 ° North and south of 55 ° South). (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Between 30 ° West and 160 ° West","Between 90 ° West and 120 ° West","Between 180 ° West and 160 ° West","Between 30 ° East and 160 ° East"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0275","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿cómo cambia el límite SUR de validez del rumbo y la derrota magnéticos en modo NAV cuando una ADIRU tiene una tabla de variación magnética distinta, frente al caso en que todas tienen la misma tabla?","keys":["60","55","irs"],"answer":"Con todas las ADIRUs con la misma tabla el límite sur es 60 ° Sur; si una ADIRU tiene una tabla distinta, el límite sur se adelanta a 55 ° Sur, es decir, la envolvente utilizable se reduce. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Se hace más restrictivo: pasa de 60 ° Sur a 55 ° Sur","Se hace menos restrictivo: pasa de 55 ° Sur a 60 ° Sur","No cambia: se mantiene en 60 ° Sur en ambos casos","Se hace más restrictivo: pasa de 73 ° Sur a 60 ° Sur"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), how does the SOUTHERN limit of validity for magnetic heading and track in NAV mode change when one ADIRU has a different magnetic variation table, compared with the case where all have the same table?","keys":["60","55","irs"],"answer":"With all ADIRUs using the same table the southern limit is 60 ° South; if one ADIRU has a different table, the southern limit is brought forward to 55 ° South, that is, the usable envelope is reduced. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["It becomes more restrictive: it changes from 60 ° South to 55 ° South","It becomes less restrictive: it changes from 55 ° South to 60 ° South","It does not change: it remains at 60 ° South in both cases","It becomes more restrictive: it changes from 73 ° South to 60 ° South"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0276","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), con una ADIRU con tabla de variación magnética distinta, todas las siguientes zonas están afectadas por la pérdida de rumbo y derrota magnéticos válidos en modo NAV, EXCEPTO:","keys":["60","30","irs"],"answer":"La limitación afecta al norte de 60 ° Norte sólo entre 30 ° Oeste y 160 ° Oeste, al norte de 73 ° Norte y al sur de 55 ° Sur. La franja de 30 ° Este a 90 ° Este no figura en la limitación. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["Al norte de 60 ° Norte entre 30 ° Este y 90 ° Este","Al norte de 60 ° Norte entre 30 ° Oeste y 160 ° Oeste","Al norte de 73 ° Norte","Al sur de 55 ° Sur"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), with one ADIRU having a different magnetic variation table, all of the following areas are affected by the loss of valid magnetic heading and track in NAV mode, EXCEPT:","keys":["60","30","irs"],"answer":"The limitation affects north of 60 ° North only between 30 ° West and 160 ° West, north of 73 ° North and south of 55 ° South. The band from 30 ° East to 90 ° East is not part of the limitation. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 168 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["North of 60 ° North between 30 ° East and 90 ° East","North of 60 ° North between 30 ° West and 160 ° West","North of 73 ° North","South of 55 ° South"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0277","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), ¿qué establece el FCOM sobre el uso de la referencia barométrica QFE?","keys":["qfe","utilizarse","aviones"],"answer":"El FCOM indica que la referencia barométrica QFE no debe utilizarse para operaciones en aviones que no estén equipados con la opción QFE. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 169 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["No debe utilizarse en aviones que no estén equipados con la opción QFE","No debe utilizarse por debajo de la altitud de transición","Sólo debe utilizarse en aproximaciones de no precisión","No debe utilizarse cuando el QNH es inferior a 1013 hPa"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), what does the FCOM state about the use of the QFE barometric reference?","keys":["qfe","option","aircraft"],"answer":"The FCOM states that the QFE barometric reference must not be used for operations on aircraft that are not fitted with the QFE option. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 169 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["It must not be used on aircraft that are not fitted with the QFE option","It must not be used below the transition altitude","It must only be used on non-precision approaches","It must not be used when the QNH is below 1013 hPa"]}},{"sys":"NAV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0278","es":{"q":"Vuela el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) hacia un aeropuerto que publica sus mínimos en QFE. El avión no está equipado con la opción QFE. ¿Qué aplica según el FCOM?","keys":["qfe","usar","referencia"],"answer":"La limitación es explícita: la referencia barométrica QFE no debe utilizarse para operaciones en aviones que no estén equipados con la opción QFE. No existe procedimiento alternativo en el FCOM que permita usarla. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 169 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["No debe usar la referencia barométrica QFE, porque el avión no está equipado con la opción QFE","Puede usar la referencia QFE ajustando manualmente el baro-reference en el FCU","Puede usar la referencia QFE sólo el Pilot Flying, manteniendo el otro altímetro en QNH","Puede usar la referencia QFE si la aproximación se vuela en modo selected"]},"en":{"q":"You are flying the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) to an airport that publishes its minima in QFE. The aircraft is not fitted with the QFE option. What applies according to the FCOM?","keys":["qfe","reference","option"],"answer":"The limitation is explicit: the QFE barometric reference must not be used for operations on aircraft that are not fitted with the QFE option. There is no alternative procedure in the FCOM that allows its use. (FCOM LIM-NAV · p. 169 · rev 06 NOV 25)","opts":["You must not use the QFE barometric reference, because the aircraft is not fitted with the QFE option","You may use the QFE reference by manually setting the baro-reference on the FCU","Only the Pilot Flying may use the QFE reference, keeping the other altimeter on QNH","You may use the QFE reference if the approach is flown in selected mode"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0279","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), con 2 tripulantes de vuelo y una REF Temperature de 20 °C, ¿cuál es la presión mínima de botella de oxígeno?","keys":["731","psi","a320"],"answer":"En la tabla MINIMUM FLIGHT CREW OXYGEN PRESSURE del avión de referencia, la fila '2 Crewmembers' da 731 PSI para una REF Temperature de 20 °C (68 °F). (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["731 PSI","706 PSI","959 PSI","1 215 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), with 2 flight crew members and a REF Temperature of 20 °C, what is the minimum oxygen cylinder pressure?","keys":["731","psi","a320"],"answer":"In the MINIMUM FLIGHT CREW OXYGEN PRESSURE table of the reference aircraft, the '2 Crewmembers' row gives 731 PSI for a REF Temperature of 20 °C (68 °F). (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["731 PSI","706 PSI","959 PSI","1 215 PSI"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0280","es":{"q":"Preparas el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota) en plataforma. La OAT es +30 °C y la Cockpit TEMP indica +10 °C. Además de los dos pilotos volará un observador en el jump seat. ¿Cuál es la presión mínima de botella de oxígeno requerida?","keys":["959","psi","preparas"],"answer":"En tierra, REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2 = (30 + 10) / 2 = 20 °C. Con 2 tripulantes + 1 observador a 20 °C, la tabla exige 959 PSI. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["959 PSI","731 PSI","992 PSI","1 215 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"You are preparing the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft) on the apron. The OAT is +30 °C and the Cockpit TEMP indicates +10 °C. In addition to the two pilots, an observer will fly in the jump seat. What is the minimum oxygen cylinder pressure required?","keys":["959","psi","observer"],"answer":"On the ground, REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2 = (30 + 10) / 2 = 20 °C. With 2 crew members + 1 observer at 20 °C, the table requires 959 PSI. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["959 PSI","731 PSI","992 PSI","1 215 PSI"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0281","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), a una REF Temperature de 0 °C, ¿cuánta presión mínima de oxígeno adicional exige llevar 2 observadores en cabina frente a volar sólo con los 2 tripulantes de vuelo?","keys":["451","psi","a320"],"answer":"A 0 °C la tabla exige 681 PSI con 2 tripulantes y 1 132 PSI con 2 tripulantes + 2 observadores: 1 132 − 681 = 451 PSI de diferencia. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["451 PSI","212 PSI","239 PSI","434 PSI"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), at a REF Temperature of 0 °C, how much additional minimum oxygen pressure is required to carry 2 observers in the cockpit compared with flying with only the 2 flight crew members?","keys":["451","psi","a320"],"answer":"At 0 °C the table requires 681 PSI with 2 crew members and 1 132 PSI with 2 crew members + 2 observers: 1 132 − 681 = 451 PSI difference. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["451 PSI","212 PSI","239 PSI","434 PSI"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0282","es":{"q":"En el EC-MOG (A320-232 con motores IAE V2500, avión de referencia de la flota), la presión mínima de botella cubre la protección tras una pérdida de presurización con el regulador de la máscara en NORMAL (oxígeno diluido). ¿Durante cuántos minutos garantiza el oxígeno a todos los tripulantes de vuelo y observadores durante el descenso de emergencia?","keys":["13","min","a320"],"answer":"Para el avión de referencia, el FCOM indica protección durante el descenso de emergencia para todos los tripulantes de vuelo y observadores durante 13 min. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["13 min","15 min","22 min","107 min"]},"en":{"q":"On the EC-MOG (A320-232 with IAE V2500 engines, fleet reference aircraft), the minimum cylinder pressure covers protection after a loss of pressurization with the mask regulator in NORMAL (diluted oxygen). For how many minutes does it guarantee oxygen to all flight crew members and observers during the emergency descent?","keys":["13","min","a320"],"answer":"For the reference aircraft, the FCOM indicates protection during the emergency descent for all flight crew members and observers for 13 min. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["13 min","15 min","22 min","107 min"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0283","es":{"q":"La presión mínima de botella de oxígeno de la tripulación de vuelo está calculada para cubrir todos los conceptos siguientes EXCEPTO:","keys":["suministro","oxigeno","pasajeros"],"answer":"El FCOM enumera lo que cubre la presión mínima de botella: preflight checks, el uso de oxígeno cuando sólo hay un tripulante en cockpit, la cantidad inutilizable, la fuga normal del sistema y el caso más exigente entre la protección tras despresurización y la protección contra humo. Es una limitación del sistema de la TRIPULACIÓN DE VUELO: el oxígeno de los pasajeros es un sistema independiente y no entra en este cálculo. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["El suministro de oxígeno a los pasajeros tras una pérdida de presurización","Los chequeos previos al vuelo (preflight checks)","La cantidad inutilizable, para asegurar la operación del regulador con presión mínima","La fuga normal del sistema"]},"en":{"q":"The minimum flight crew oxygen cylinder pressure is calculated to cover all of the following items EXCEPT:","keys":["passenger","oxygen","independent"],"answer":"The FCOM lists what the minimum cylinder pressure covers: the preflight checks, the use of oxygen when only one crew member is in the cockpit, the unusable quantity, the normal system leakage and the most demanding case between post-depressurization protection and smoke protection. It is a FLIGHT CREW system limitation: passenger oxygen is an independent system and is not part of this calculation. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["The supply of oxygen to the passengers after a loss of pressurization","The preflight checks","The unusable quantity, to ensure regulator operation at minimum pressure","The normal system leakage"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0284","es":{"q":"En tierra, ¿cómo se calcula la REF Temperature con la que se entra en la tabla de presión mínima de oxígeno de la tripulación de vuelo?","keys":["2","temperature","cockpit"],"answer":"En tierra la REF Temperature es la media aritmética entre la temperatura exterior (OAT) y la temperatura de cockpit: REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2","REF Temperature = OAT − 10 °C","REF Temperature = Cockpit TEMP − 10 °C","REF Temperature = (OAT + CAB TEMP) / 2"]},"en":{"q":"On the ground, how is the REF Temperature used to enter the flight crew minimum oxygen pressure table calculated?","keys":["2","temperature","cockpit"],"answer":"On the ground the REF Temperature is the arithmetic mean of the outside temperature (OAT) and the cockpit temperature: REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2","REF Temperature = OAT − 10 °C","REF Temperature = Cockpit TEMP − 10 °C","REF Temperature = (OAT + CAB TEMP) / 2"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0285","es":{"q":"En crucero, la CAB TEMP indica 24 °C. ¿Qué REF Temperature debes usar para entrar en la tabla de presión mínima de oxígeno?","keys":["14","cab temp","crucero"],"answer":"En vuelo, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°C) − 10 °C. Con CAB TEMP 24 °C, la REF Temperature es 14 °C. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["14 °C","34 °C","24 °C","12 °C"]},"en":{"q":"In cruise, the CAB TEMP indicates 24 °C. What REF Temperature must you use to enter the minimum oxygen pressure table?","keys":["14","cab temp","cruise"],"answer":"In flight, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°C) − 10 °C. With CAB TEMP 24 °C, the REF Temperature is 14 °C. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["14 °C","34 °C","24 °C","12 °C"]}},{"sys":"O2","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0286","es":{"q":"¿Cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones sobre el cálculo de la REF Temperature para la presión mínima de oxígeno es FALSA?","keys":["2","vuelo","temperature"],"answer":"El FCOM sólo publica dos fórmulas: en tierra la media de OAT y Cockpit TEMP, y en vuelo la CAB TEMP menos 10 °C (o menos 18 °F si se trabaja en Fahrenheit). Promediar OAT y CAB TEMP en vuelo no existe. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["En vuelo, REF Temperature = (OAT + CAB TEMP) / 2","En tierra, REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2","En vuelo, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°C) − 10 °C","En vuelo, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°F) − 18 °F"]},"en":{"q":"Which of the following statements about the calculation of the REF Temperature for the minimum oxygen pressure is FALSE?","keys":["2","flight","temperature"],"answer":"The FCOM only publishes two formulas: on the ground the mean of OAT and Cockpit TEMP, and in flight the CAB TEMP minus 10 °C (or minus 18 °F if working in Fahrenheit). Averaging OAT and CAB TEMP in flight does not exist. (FCOM LIM-OXY · p. 176 · rev 17 MAR 17)","opts":["In flight, REF Temperature = (OAT + CAB TEMP) / 2","On the ground, REF Temperature = (OAT + Cockpit TEMP) / 2","In flight, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°C) − 10 °C","In flight, REF Temperature = CAB TEMP (°F) − 18 °F"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0287","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con ROW/ROP, durante la preparación del descenso el FLD evaluado resulta mayor que la longitud de pista ROPS del aeropuerto de destino. ¿Qué establece la limitación?","keys":["row","operacion","realizarse"],"answer":"El FCOM prohíbe realizar operaciones en las que el FLD evaluado durante la preparación del descenso sea mayor que la longitud de pista ROPS, salvo autorización específica de la autoridad correspondiente. En esas pistas, si el ROPS no está inhibido (pb-sw ROW/ROP en ON), pueden dispararse alertas ROW. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["La operación no debe realizarse, salvo que se obtenga una autorización específica de la autoridad correspondiente","Se puede continuar: el ROPS avisará con alertas ROW si existe riesgo real de salida de pista","Se puede continuar siempre que se inhiba el ROW/ROP para evitar alertas indebidas","Se puede continuar siempre que la condición de pista sea DRY y las reversas estén disponibles"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with ROW/ROP, during descent preparation the assessed FLD turns out to be greater than the ROPS runway length of the destination airport. What does the limitation state?","keys":["fld","rops","approval"],"answer":"The FCOM prohibits performing operations in which the FLD assessed during descent preparation is greater than the ROPS runway length, unless specific approval is obtained from the appropriate authority. On such runways, if ROPS is not inhibited (ROW/ROP pb-sw ON), ROW alerts may be triggered. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["The operation must not be performed, unless specific approval is obtained from the appropriate authority","It may be continued: ROPS will warn with ROW alerts if there is a real risk of runway excursion","It may be continued provided ROW/ROP is inhibited to avoid undue alerts","It may be continued provided the runway condition is DRY and the reversers are available"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0288","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con ROW/ROP, vas a volar una aproximación que el operador ha identificado previamente como potencialmente generadora de alertas ROW indebidas. ¿Qué prevé la limitación?","keys":["row","funciones","rops"],"answer":"El FCOM permite inhibir las funciones ROW/ROPS (pb-sw ROW/ROP en OFF, en el panel SURV) para procedimientos de aproximación específicos previamente identificados como potencialmente productores de alertas ROW indebidas. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["Que las funciones ROW/ROPS pueden inhibirse poniendo el pb-sw ROW/ROP en OFF en el panel SURV","Que las funciones ROW/ROPS pueden inhibirse poniendo el pb-sw TERR en OFF en el panel GPWS","Que el ROW/ROP no puede inhibirse en vuelo, por lo que hay que aceptar las alertas","Que se seleccione manualmente condición de pista DRY para suprimir las alertas"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with ROW/ROP, you are going to fly an approach that the operator has previously identified as potentially generating undue ROW alerts. What does the limitation provide?","keys":["row","rops","inhibited"],"answer":"The FCOM allows the ROW/ROPS functions to be inhibited (ROW/ROP pb-sw OFF, on the SURV panel) for specific approach procedures previously identified as potentially producing undue ROW alerts. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["That the ROW/ROPS functions can be inhibited by setting the ROW/ROP pb-sw to OFF on the SURV panel","That the ROW/ROPS functions can be inhibited by setting the TERR pb-sw to OFF on the GPWS panel","That ROW/ROP cannot be inhibited in flight, so the alerts must be accepted","That runway condition DRY be manually selected to suppress the alerts"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0289","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con ROW/ROP, ¿cuál de las siguientes afirmaciones sobre el ROPS es FALSA?","keys":["row","mientras","reversas"],"answer":"El ROPS nunca garantiza la parada dentro de la pista: el FCOM enumera expresamente casos en los que no evita la excursión (fallos que afecten a la performance de aterrizaje o a las reversas, o condición DRY seleccionada en pista WET PFC/GROOVED). Las otras tres afirmaciones son literales del capítulo. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["Mientras las reversas estén disponibles, el ROPS garantiza la parada del avión dentro de la pista","Ante un fallo que afecte a la performance de aterrizaje y/o a la disponibilidad de las reversas, el ROPS no evita la salida de pista","Si se selecciona condición de pista DRY en una pista WET PFC/GROOVED, el ROPS no evita la salida de pista","En cualquier caso, si se disparan alertas ROPS, la tripulación debe aplicar inmediatamente los procedimientos ROPS"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with ROW/ROP, which of the following statements about ROPS is FALSE?","keys":["rops","reversers","excursion"],"answer":"ROPS never guarantees stopping within the runway: the FCOM expressly lists cases where it does not prevent the excursion (failures affecting landing performance or the reversers, or DRY condition selected on a WET PFC/GROOVED runway). The other three statements are literal from the chapter. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["As long as the reversers are available, ROPS guarantees stopping the aircraft within the runway","In the event of a failure affecting landing performance and/or reverser availability, ROPS does not prevent the runway excursion","If runway condition DRY is selected on a WET PFC/GROOVED runway, ROPS does not prevent the runway excursion","In any case, if ROPS alerts are triggered, the crew must immediately apply the ROPS procedures"]},"mcOnly":1},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0290","es":{"q":"En un avión equipado con ROW/ROP, ¿en qué situación queda el ROPS cuando la pista no está validada para ROPS en la base de datos del TAWS?","keys":["row","rops","inoperativo"],"answer":"El FCOM es explícito: en pistas que no están validadas para ROPS en la base de datos del TAWS, el ROPS está inoperativo. Además, es responsabilidad del operador informar a la tripulación de qué pistas no están validadas para ROPS a lo largo de la ruta programada. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["El ROPS está inoperativo","El ROPS sigue operativo, pero sólo genera alertas ROW (no ROP)","El ROPS sigue operativo aplicando márgenes de parada reducidos","El ROPS sigue operativo, pero sólo con condición de pista DRY seleccionada"]},"en":{"q":"On an aircraft fitted with ROW/ROP, what is the status of ROPS when the runway is not validated for ROPS in the TAWS database?","keys":["rops","taws","inoperative"],"answer":"The FCOM is explicit: on runways that are not validated for ROPS in the TAWS database, ROPS is inoperative. In addition, it is the operator's responsibility to inform the crew of which runways are not validated for ROPS along the planned route. (FCOM LIM-ROW_ROP · p. 183 · rev 02 MAY 24)","opts":["ROPS is inoperative","ROPS remains operative, but only generates ROW alerts (not ROP)","ROPS remains operative applying reduced stopping margins","ROPS remains operative, but only with runway condition DRY selected"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0291","es":{"q":"A 12 NM del aeródromo, tu copiloto propone poner el pb TERR en OFF porque, a su juicio, esta aproximación podría generar alertas de terreno espurias. La pista sí está en la base de datos del predictive GPWS y el operador no ha identificado este procedimiento como problemático. ¿Qué dice la limitación?","keys":["terr","decision","inhibir"],"answer":"La Note del FCOM es taxativa: la decisión de inhibir las funciones de predictive GPWS no debe basarse únicamente en el criterio de la tripulación. La inhibición está prevista para pistas no incorporadas en la base de datos del predictive GPWS o para procedimientos previamente identificados por el operador; ninguno de los dos supuestos se da en este escenario. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["La decisión de inhibir las funciones de predictive GPWS no debe basarse únicamente en el criterio de la tripulación","Es correcto: a menos de 15 NM del aeródromo, la decisión de inhibir corresponde a la tripulación","Es correcto, pero sólo si el TAWS ya ha generado previamente una alerta de terreno en esa aproximación","Es correcto siempre que se anote en el technical logbook"]},"en":{"q":"At 12 NM from the aerodrome, your copilot suggests setting the TERR pb to OFF because, in his judgment, this approach could generate spurious terrain alerts. The runway is in the predictive GPWS database and the operator has not identified this procedure as problematic. What does the limitation say?","keys":["terr","decision","inhibit"],"answer":"The FCOM Note is categorical: the decision to inhibit the predictive GPWS functions must not be based solely on crew judgment. Inhibition is provided for runways not incorporated in the predictive GPWS database or for procedures previously identified by the operator; neither of the two cases applies in this scenario. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["The decision to inhibit the predictive GPWS functions must not be based solely on crew judgment","It is correct: within 15 NM of the aerodrome, the decision to inhibit is up to the crew","It is correct, but only if the TAWS has previously generated a terrain alert on that approach","It is correct provided it is recorded in the technical logbook"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0292","es":{"q":"¿A qué distancia del aeródromo deben inhibirse las funciones de predictive GPWS (pb TERR en OFF, en el panel GPWS) en los casos previstos por la limitación?","keys":["15","nm","terr"],"answer":"Las funciones de predictive GPWS deben inhibirse (pb TERR en OFF, en el panel GPWS) cuando la posición del avión es de menos de 15 NM del aeródromo, en dos supuestos: operaciones desde/hacia pistas no incorporadas en la base de datos del predictive GPWS, y procedimientos específicos de aproximación o salida previamente identificados por el operador como potencialmente causantes de alertas de terreno esperadas o espurias. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["Cuando la posición del avión es de menos de 15 NM del aeródromo","Cuando la posición del avión es de menos de 10 NM del aeródromo","Cuando la posición del avión es de menos de 20 NM del aeródromo","Cuando la posición del avión es de menos de 25 NM del aeródromo"]},"en":{"q":"At what distance from the aerodrome must the predictive GPWS functions be inhibited (TERR pb to OFF, on the GPWS panel) in the cases provided by the limitation?","keys":["15","nm","terr"],"answer":"The predictive GPWS functions must be inhibited (TERR pb to OFF, on the GPWS panel) when the aircraft position is less than 15 NM from the aerodrome, in two cases: operations from/to runways not incorporated in the predictive GPWS database, and specific approach or departure procedures previously identified by the operator as potentially causing expected or spurious terrain alerts. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["When the aircraft position is less than 15 NM from the aerodrome","When the aircraft position is less than 10 NM from the aerodrome","When the aircraft position is less than 20 NM from the aerodrome","When the aircraft position is less than 25 NM from the aerodrome"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0293","es":{"q":"¿Qué aviones pueden mostrar obstáculos en la ND y generar alertas de obstáculo?","keys":["nd","aviones","equipados"],"answer":"Únicamente los aviones que llevan instalada la Man-made Obstacle Function pueden mostrar obstáculos en la ND y disparar alertas, basándose en una base de datos dedicada que incluye obstáculos artificiales de todo el mundo. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["Sólo los aviones equipados con la Man-made Obstacle Function","Todos los de la flota, ya que todos llevan TAWS instalado","Sólo los aviones equipados con ROW/ROP","Sólo los aviones equipados con predictive GPWS"]},"en":{"q":"Which aircraft can display obstacles on the ND and generate obstacle alerts?","keys":["nd","obstacle","function"],"answer":"Only aircraft with the Man-made Obstacle Function installed can display obstacles on the ND and trigger alerts, based on a dedicated database that includes man-made obstacles worldwide. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["Only aircraft fitted with the Man-made Obstacle Function","All aircraft in the fleet, since they all have TAWS installed","Only aircraft fitted with ROW/ROP","Only aircraft fitted with predictive GPWS"]}},{"sys":"SURV","type":"LIM","kid":"K-LIM-0294","es":{"q":"¿Qué establece la limitación sobre el uso del terrain display?","keys":["taws","navegacion","avion"],"answer":"La navegación del avión no debe basarse en el terrain display: es únicamente una herramienta de conciencia situacional y puede no ofrecer la precisión necesaria para basar en él, por sí solo, una maniobra de evitación de terreno. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["La navegación del avión no debe basarse en el uso del terrain display","El terrain display puede usarse para navegar siempre que el TAWS esté operativo","El terrain display puede usarse como medio primario de navegación por debajo de FL100","El terrain display sólo puede usarse en aproximaciones que no sean de precisión"]},"en":{"q":"What does the limitation state about the use of the terrain display?","keys":["terrain","navigation","display"],"answer":"Aircraft navigation must not be based on the terrain display: it is solely a situational awareness tool and may not provide the accuracy needed to base, on its own, a terrain avoidance maneuver. (FCOM LIM-SURV · p. 189 · rev 28 MAY 20)","opts":["Aircraft navigation must not be based on the use of the terrain display","The terrain display can be used to navigate provided the TAWS is operative","The terrain display can be used as a primary means of navigation below FL100","The terrain display can only be used on non-precision approaches"]}}];
